{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "That’s the reason I’m late (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["That's the reason I'm late (Yeah)"], "meaning": "An Audemars Piguet, is a luxury watch commonly worn by rappers and other celebrities. Busting the face refers to embellishing the watch face with diamonds. Uzi is late because all the diamonds on the watch face makes it difficult to see the time. He’s flexing that he’s rich.", "annotation_id": "36780043", "url": "https://genius.com/36780043", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Audemars, bust the face, huh That’s the reason I’m late", "vault_lines": ["That's the reason I'm late (Yeah)"], "meaning": "An Audemars Piguet, is a luxury watch commonly worn by rappers and other celebrities. Busting the face refers to embellishing the watch face with diamonds. Uzi is late because all the diamonds on the watch face makes it difficult to see the time. He’s flexing that he’s rich.", "annotation_id": "36780021", "url": "https://genius.com/36780021", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Step in this bitch with my boots untied, I feel safe ’cause I got all of the steppers Most of these niggas out here be façades, never ever they could step in my sector", "vault_lines": ["Step in this bitch with my boots untied, I feel safe 'cause I got all of the steppers"], "meaning": "In these lines, Lil Uzi Vert is emphasizing his confidence and toughness. He feels secure because he’s surrounded by loyal people (“steppers”) who have his back. He also critiques others for being fake, suggesting they aren’t on his level or capable of surviving in his world. Uzi highlights his authenticity and strength, setting himself apart from those who are merely pretending.", "annotation_id": "33530010", "url": "https://genius.com/33530010", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "All black like it’s Kray", "vault_lines": ["All black like it's Kray"], "meaning": "A reference to Black Kray, an extremely influential underground rapper who is credited with inspiring much of the cloud rap and emo rap genres for over a decade. Black Kray is a leading member of Goth Money, a label that often collaborated with Yung Lean and his Sadboys group very early on.", "annotation_id": "28904740", "url": "https://genius.com/28904740", "state": "pending", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "[Intro] Yeah This shit, this shit cray (This shit cray) This shit cray (It’s really bray) This shit cray This shit—", "vault_lines": ["This shit, this shit cray (This shit cray)"], "meaning": "The repeated phrase “this shit cray” used throughout the song may be an interpolation of JAY-Z & Kanye West’s 2011 hit song “Ni**as In Paris” featured on their collabrotive album Watch The Throne.\n\nThe line interpolated is featured in the chorus of “Ni**as In Paris” with Kanye repeating that line:\n\nThat shit cray, that shit cray, that shit cray", "annotation_id": "29004468", "url": "https://genius.com/29004468", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Chopper on my body hang all way down to my shoes", "vault_lines": ["Chopper on my body hang all way down to my shoes"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is most likely referring to some sort of Assault Rifle  that is long enough to touch his shoes when he’s holding it downwards.\n\nAlso a reference to his short height of 5’4", "annotation_id": "28961709", "url": "https://genius.com/28961709", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Audemars, bust the face, huh", "vault_lines": ["Audemars, bust the face, huh (Face)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert boasts his lavish lifestyle by referencing Swiss luxury watch manufacturer Audemars Piget—which is known for their expensive watches.\n\nLil Uzi Vert on the other hand, has also been seen accompanied by a $300,000, 18 karat, rose gold, diamond Audemars Piguet Skeleton back in February 2019.", "annotation_id": "28952052", "url": "https://genius.com/28952052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Audemars, bust the face, huh (Face)", "vault_lines": ["Audemars, bust the face, huh (Face)"], "meaning": "With this line, Lil Uzi Vert emphasizes his taste for high-end watches by referencing Audemars Piguet, a prestigious Swiss watch brand synonymous with luxury and exclusivity.\n\n“Bust the face,” references the process of putting Diamonds, or other gems, around or into the face of a luxury watch.", "annotation_id": "28952047", "url": "https://genius.com/28952047", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Believe in God to get out my deal like I’m Ma$e", "vault_lines": ["They try to say I’m the— ah, believe in God to get out my deal like I'm Ma$e"], "meaning": "Here Uzi is claiming he would believe in Christianity’s God and leave his rap career to get out of his record deal like Ma$e.\n\nMa$e famously retired from hip-hop to pursue a calling from God. Mase then became an ordained minister as well as continued his college studies.\n\n\n\nBefore Uzi signed with Roc Nation, he was in a deal with DJ Drama, Don Cannon, and Generation Now under Atlantic Records who he had accused of blocking the release of his Eternal Atake album prior.", "annotation_id": "28934773", "url": "https://genius.com/28934773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "I fuck with the vamps, but I’m werewolf times two (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I fuck with the vamps, but I'm werewolf times two (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi may be shouting out the Opium label collective, led by longtime friend and collaborator Playboi Carti, who is known for his “King Vamp” aesthetic, highlighted in songs such as “King Vamp”. Those affiliated with Carti, as well as fans of the artist, are often referred to as “vamps.” Furthermore, “x2” is coproduced by Ken Carson, a signee to Opium. Uzi has shown a lot of love towards Ken and Destroy Lonely, another Opium signee, prior to the release of Pink Tape, even bringing them out for their Governors Ball 2023 performance. Uzi positions themselves at odds with Carti and the Opium crew, despite the love they share for one other.\n\nFurthermore, the rivalry between vampires and werewolves is often seen throughout popular culture such as The Twilight Saga where battles break out between vampires, led by Edward Cullen, played by Robert Pattinson, and werewolves led by Jacob Black, played by Taylor Lautner.\n\nUzi reinterprets “vamps” for their fans and affiliates in another Pink Tape track titled “Werewolf”.", "annotation_id": "28934454", "url": "https://genius.com/28934454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "I got fangs in my mouth, but stare at the moon", "vault_lines": ["I got fangs in my mouth, but stare at the moon"], "meaning": "The fangs in their mouth makes him a vampire, but they act like a werewolf, which are known to howl at full moons.", "annotation_id": "28931903", "url": "https://genius.com/28931903", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Twilight, twilight moon", "vault_lines": ["This shit, this shit cray (This shit cray)"], "meaning": "Twilights occur twice a day, once before the sun rises as the sky begins to get light and once after sunset when the sky is just beginning to get dark. The hues of twilight are produced by the sun’s rays being scattered by the atmosphere. When the sun sets on worlds without atmospheres, like the moon, it becomes pitch black right away.", "annotation_id": "28931814", "url": "https://genius.com/28931814", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "I might matte the Wraith", "vault_lines": ["I might matte the Wraith"], "meaning": "Deglossing is the process of removing the gloss from a car’s paint and making it non-reflective.\n\nUzi shares their intent to matte out, or remove the gloss, of their luxury Rolls-Royce Wraith.", "annotation_id": "28931764", "url": "https://genius.com/28931764", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "All black like it’s Kray", "vault_lines": ["All black like it's Kray"], "meaning": "In these lines, Lil Uzi Vert references fellow artist Black Kray\n\nBlack Kray is an American rapper, producer, film director, and the founding member of the collective Goth Money Records. Black Kray in also affiliated with Bladee.", "annotation_id": "28929965", "url": "https://genius.com/28929965", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
