{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "All black like it’s Kray", "vault_lines": ["All black like it's Kray"], "meaning": "Uzi make reference to an underground rapper Black Kray (also Sickboyrari) who well known in the goth trap and cloud subgenres. He is also known for his collaborations with artists like Bones and SpaceGhostPurrp. He is the founder of the Goth Money Records crew.", "annotation_id": "28791157", "url": "https://genius.com/28791157", "state": "pending", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "You still waitin’ on the Pink Tape, huh", "vault_lines": ["You still waitin’ on the Pink Tape, huh"], "meaning": "In this line, Uzi is referring to the long-awaited release of his album, Pink Tape. More than three years have passed since the release of his most recent album, Eternal Atake and its deluxe edition.\n\nHe implies that fans have been eagerly anticipating this album’s release. Despite the passage of time, Uzi is aware that his fans are still waiting for new music from him.", "annotation_id": "28789679", "url": "https://genius.com/28789679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Got a Montana bae Her dad Billy Ray", "vault_lines": ["Got a Montana bae"], "meaning": "American singer and songwriter, Billy Ray Cyrus, is father to American actor and singer, Miley Cyrus, who played the character Hannah Montana in the self-titled sitcom Hannah Montana.", "annotation_id": "28779814", "url": "https://genius.com/28779814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "I knew I was a star as many times I drove the Wraith", "vault_lines": ["I knew I was a star as many times I drove the Wraith"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Wraith is a luxury SUV manufactured by British automaker Rolls-Royce—being first introduced in 2013 at a starting price of $210,000. Lil Uzi Vert likens their stardom to the Wraith’s built-in “Starlight Headliner” feature, which projects light onto the ceiling in the form of stars.\n\n 2022 Rolls-Royce Wraith Starlight Headliner. \n\nLil Uzi Vert previously mentioned the vehicle in their June 2023 track, “Flooded The Face,” rapping:\n\nFlooded the face, matted the Wraith (Woo, woo)", "annotation_id": "28768129", "url": "https://genius.com/28768129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Shoutout to Tay-K, man, it’s time I did the race", "vault_lines": ["Shoutout to Tay-K, man, it’s time I did the race"], "meaning": "Tay-K is a rapper who first began making noise on the Hip-Hop scene in 2017. More specifically, with his breakout hit “The Race”. The song, as its name implies, was made while on the run from law enforcement.\n\nLil Uzi Vert was one of many who supported Tay-K and his music, and was seen listening to “The Race” in their car:\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=Snk3sJpe7QQ\n\nHowever, Tay-K‘s career has since been halted, after being apprehended in 2017, and 2 years later receiving a 55-year sentence in prison for 3 counts of aggravated robbery, there hasn’t been much hope for Tay-K’s musical career to expand further.", "annotation_id": "28768032", "url": "https://genius.com/28768032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Two different names like Jace!", "vault_lines": ["Two different names like Jace!"], "meaning": "Uzi gives a shout-out to Texas rapper iayze—alternatively known as Jace!, in which both names are pronounced the same.\n\nUzi also alludes to that they, too, have different names or aliases—such as Leslie Chow. It highlights the concept of artists adopting different personas or identities within their art. This similarity between the two rappers' use of alternate names creates a connection through wordplay and their own artistic expression.", "annotation_id": "28761925", "url": "https://genius.com/28761925", "state": "accepted", "votes": 140, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "‎x2", "line": "Make my avi pink like my biggest opp, UziRareUpdates (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Make my avi pink like my biggest opp, UziRareUpdates (Woah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert addresses one of their more famous fanpages, uzirareupdates on Instagram, in which Uzi compares the color of their (Uzi’s) avatar, being the cover to Pink Tape, to uzirareupdates' profile picture.\n\nThis comes from the negative critique and hate spewed by the page, as screenshots posted on URU’s Instagram Story the days leading up to Pink Tape were constantly showing negativity towards Uzi, his producers, and his visual artists, claiming the album was horrible and that half the songs should’ve been scrapped, as well as spreading hate in group chats, shown in leaked Instagram screenshots.\n\nFollowing the track’s release, Complex interviewed URU about Uzi’s line on “x2”. The fanpage admitted to sharing their hateful yet honest thoughts on Uzi and their work, but at the same time, they were supported by Uzi and thanked for their criticism, even going so far as to admit that the hate they spewed was all playful banter:\n\nUzi’s called me twin and says [they love] me, but calls me [their] biggest opp because of some of the stuff I be posting. […] Uzi could’ve said some outrageous shit about me. But left me off easy. Just by calling me [their] biggest opp. I never was beefing with Uzi seriously. It was always jokes.\n\n\n\nuzirareupdates profile picture on Instagram", "annotation_id": "28757709", "url": "https://genius.com/28757709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 200, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
