{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I been gettin’ money, so don’t nothin’ really excite me (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I been gettin' money, so don't nothin' really excite me (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi is referring to the money he makes. Indicating he has a lot, since anything that he gets doesn’t excite him, because he’s used to the luxurious lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "37204167", "url": "https://genius.com/37204167", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "These young niggas don’t like me, but act just like me (Why?)", "vault_lines": ["These young niggas don't like me, but act just like me (Why?)"], "meaning": "Playboi Carti & Lil Uzi claim that other smaller artists are imitating their distinct styles, whether it be their musical style or clothing/physical appearance despite the hate they receive from the same people.", "annotation_id": "36415661", "url": "https://genius.com/36415661", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Fuck me, Bentley coupe, I’m riding with a thottie, fuck", "vault_lines": ["Fuck me, Bentley coupe, I'm riding with a thottie, fuck"], "meaning": "A Bentley coupe is a luxurious car considered to be one of the most stylish and sought after vehicles especially in the hip-hop/rap community. Carti refers to the person he’s riding with as a “Thottie”, which is a promiscuous woman.", "annotation_id": "35064868", "url": "https://genius.com/35064868", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Xans, Percs, molly, we got hella things", "vault_lines": ["Xans, Percs, molly, we got hella things"], "meaning": "I’m from Atlanta, home of music and trapping. We still got everything. So whatever you want, we got. I drink lean. Sprite is the drink that I mix with it. It’s cool.", "annotation_id": "11699621", "url": "https://genius.com/11699621", "state": "verified", "votes": 147, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "My Draco, bitch, a Spike Lee, diamonds on me biting", "vault_lines": ["My Draco, bitch, a Spike Lee, diamonds on me biting"], "meaning": "Shooting like a movie. Therefore I’m Spike Lee. My draco is a movie. My draco is Spike Lee.", "annotation_id": "11699605", "url": "https://genius.com/11699605", "state": "verified", "votes": 209, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "These boys all up in my lane, I swear they keep on merging (Keep on what?)", "vault_lines": ["These boys all up in my lane, I swear they keep on merging (Keep on what?)"], "meaning": "Uzi expands on the theme in this song of other rappers sounding like him and biting his style. He’s saying they are in his lane however “they keep on merging” a play on how cars merge into lanes on highways.", "annotation_id": "13006968", "url": "https://genius.com/13006968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "No, I cannot see a lame ’cause my Rolls-Royce got curtains (Lil Uzi)", "vault_lines": ["No, I cannot see a lame 'cause my Rolls-Royce got curtains (Lil Uzi)"], "meaning": "Uzi has previously mentioned his love for the Rolls Royce Phantom on his 2017 smash hit “XO TOUR Llif3:”\n\nPhantom that’s all red, inside all white\n\nHe also delivered a similar bar on the lesser-known track “I Don’t Give A Fuck:”\n\nYour bitch in the whip, yeah, the one with the curtains\nI’m sucking that titty, that bitch’ll be nursing", "annotation_id": "12643478", "url": "https://genius.com/12643478", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Shoutout G Weed and Yung L, yeah, ho, that the gang", "vault_lines": ["Shoutout G Weed and Yung L, yeah, ho, that the gang"], "meaning": "G Weed and Yung L are two Campanella Park Pirus from Compton, California; G Weed is considered an OG as well. Both are known childhood friends of Kendrick Lamar, and made appearances on the documentary Noisey Bompton. They frequently appear in music videos for him, such as “Alright”, “King Kunta”, and “ELEMENT.”", "annotation_id": "12600769", "url": "https://genius.com/12600769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I heard these niggas wanna fight me", "vault_lines": ["I heard these niggas wanna fight me"], "meaning": "Although nothing major, Carti has gotten into a fight before. He fought Asspizza & Kerwin after an Ian Conner dispute:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/jsrnW2URD7I", "annotation_id": "11883866", "url": "https://genius.com/11883866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Diamonds on me, ice cream (Huh?), ho, that slightly", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds on me, ice cream (Huh?), ho, that slightly"], "meaning": "Carti likens his diamonds to ice cream, playing on the notion that his diamonds mimic the shiny nature of ice crystals. Carti’s diamonds are a source of pride; he’s referenced his diamond collection multiple times before, specifically on “The Omen”:\n\nValentino yellow diamond ropes\nGot yo' ho on go!", "annotation_id": "11831315", "url": "https://genius.com/11831315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Fucked all of y’all bitches, so they parties don’t invite me", "vault_lines": ["Fucked all of y'all bitches, so they parties don't invite me"], "meaning": "That’s real shit that he was saying. He bagged so many girls that they don’t even want to invite him to the parties no more. I feel like that was one of the hardest lines he said. His whole verse was fire, though.", "annotation_id": "11699645", "url": "https://genius.com/11699645", "state": "verified", "votes": 489, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Shootin’ at these niggas like I’m in the paint", "vault_lines": ["Shootin' at these niggas like I'm in the paint"], "meaning": "I used to play ball. Hell yeah. I need start back up. But I haven’t played in a minute. I played in school. I was playing point guard, and then when I got taller, I played the three.", "annotation_id": "11699639", "url": "https://genius.com/11699639", "state": "verified", "votes": 137, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Shoutout GiGi, that’s my boo, she know that I claim", "vault_lines": ["Shoutout GiGi, that's my boo, she know that I claim"], "meaning": "It’s just one of  my homegirls. Shout out to GiGi.", "annotation_id": "11699629", "url": "https://genius.com/11699629", "state": "verified", "votes": 223, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I’m in Bompton with Pirus and I don’t even bang, yeah (Slatt)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in Bompton with Pirus and I don't even bang, yeah (Slatt)"], "meaning": "I’m not from Cali, bro. I’m from Atlanta. Some people got different lifestyles. People come from different places and stuff, but we still find certain shit that we just we be like, “We’re on the same shit.” Everybody is trying to get out.", "annotation_id": "11699625", "url": "https://genius.com/11699625", "state": "verified", "votes": 146, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "And I swear I had these thots before I got the fame And I swear I had the Glock before I got the chain", "vault_lines": ["And I swear I had these thots before I got the fame"], "meaning": "I’ve always been a ladies man before the rap. I love females. That’s my thing. Being from Atlanta. Everybody has guns. You feel me? And I most definitely had a gun before I got a chain.", "annotation_id": "11699624", "url": "https://genius.com/11699624", "state": "verified", "votes": 147, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "The bitch want to indict me, she can’t find me", "vault_lines": ["The bitch want to indict me, she can't find me"], "meaning": "I just feel like it gets real dangerous. Females, I feel like they go out their way sometimes and a lot of females chase me so I just be hiding, ducking.", "annotation_id": "11699618", "url": "https://genius.com/11699618", "state": "verified", "votes": 160, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Bitch, I’m off the lean, I crash the Audi, fuck", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm off the lean, I crash the Audi, fuck"], "meaning": "I crashed a lot of cars. I don’t think kids should drive and do lean. Don’t do that. Just keep that in the wraps. It’s not cool.", "annotation_id": "11699615", "url": "https://genius.com/11699615", "state": "verified", "votes": 363, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I done fell in love with a thottie, fuck", "vault_lines": ["I done fell in love with a thottie, fuck"], "meaning": "That’s the life we live. Lifestyle. Who doesn’t? Everybody’s got to fall in love with somebody, right?", "annotation_id": "11699614", "url": "https://genius.com/11699614", "state": "verified", "votes": 258, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I just spent a hundred on my watch piece, fuck", "vault_lines": ["I just spent a hundred on my watch piece, fuck"], "meaning": "I didn’t spend 100 on a watch. I spent 100 on bracelets. Uzi spent 100 on a watch.", "annotation_id": "11699609", "url": "https://genius.com/11699609", "state": "verified", "votes": 792, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Meet me at my next show but you better bring a pipe, B, yeah We ain’t fighting", "vault_lines": ["Meet me at my next show but you better bring a pipe, B, yeah"], "meaning": "Yeah, we be in fights. I don’t like to fight. I’m a pretty boy. At this point I shouldn’t be fighting. So you better bring a pipe. That’s how I feel.", "annotation_id": "11699607", "url": "https://genius.com/11699607", "state": "verified", "votes": 238, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Oh, I think they like me, yeah, they like me (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I think they like me, yeah, they like me (Hey)"], "meaning": "Franchize Boys’ “White Tee.” Atlanta classic. We were really influenced by that while we were making that song, and we just went with it.", "annotation_id": "11699599", "url": "https://genius.com/11699599", "state": "verified", "votes": 245, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Yeah, that’s that dirty, that’s that dirty (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, that's that dirty, that's that dirty (Woo)"], "meaning": "“Dirty,” also know as “Lean” and “Purple Drank” is a mixture of Sprite, promethazine (with codeine) and Jolly Rancher candies. Uzi is saying that they aren’t drinking regular sprite, but instead are sipping “Dirty Sprite”.\n\n\n\nThe drink has become very relevant in recent years due to the increased consumption of narcotics rather than alcohol. It has been referenced in many popular songs such as: “Panda”, “Black Beatles,” “X”, and was also the name of Future’s 2015 studio album Dirty Sprite 2.", "annotation_id": "11669777", "url": "https://genius.com/11669777", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Carti poured a six in the four of the right lean Damn, that boy askin’ for some more like the Sprite clean (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Carti poured a six in the four of the right lean"], "meaning": "Carti poured a 6 in a 4, meaning he poured 6 ounces of lean into a drink that was intended for 4 ounces of lean, which explains Uzi’s surprise at his request for more lean; he’s already been consuming extra strong mixtures up until that point.\n\nWhile this may not seem important in the moment, making a strong drink can pose problems for Carti later on—especially as it pertains to the threat of a lean overdose.", "annotation_id": "11665942", "url": "https://genius.com/11665942", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "She just wanna fuck me for my clout, fuck", "vault_lines": ["She just wanna fuck me for my clout, fuck"], "meaning": "Clout refers to someone’s influence or power; Carti has a large amount of this due to his success. Therefore, this girl just wants to have sex with Carti because of his fame and influence in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "11650648", "url": "https://genius.com/11650648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Woke up to niggas talkin’ like me, talk (What?) Woke up to niggas soundin’ like me, talk (Huh?) Woke up to niggas talkin’ like me, talk Woke up to niggas soundin’ like me, talk (Woke up, yeah) I woke up to niggas soundin’ like me (Woke up, damn) Woke up to niggas talkin’ like me (Woke up) Woke up to niggas soundin’ like me (Woke up) Woke up to niggas talkin’ like me (Woke up)", "vault_lines": ["Woke up to niggas talkin' like me, talk (What?)"], "meaning": "Playboi Carti & Lil Uzi claim that other smaller artists are imitating their distinct styles, whether it be their musical style or clothing/physical appearance.", "annotation_id": "11646827", "url": "https://genius.com/11646827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 324, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Oh, no, no, no, baby, smoke so much dope, need some Visine", "vault_lines": ["Oh, no, no, no, baby, smoke so much dope, need some Visine"], "meaning": "Visine eye drops relieve redness due to minor eye irritation. It works by constricting swollen blood vessels in the eye, which reduces redness.\n\n\n\nSmoking marijuana often causes red-eye due to irritation, and since Uzi smokes his fair share of marijuana, it’s safe to say he might need Visine to relieve the irritation.", "annotation_id": "11646817", "url": "https://genius.com/11646817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I’m in love with the guap, gave it a wedding ring", "vault_lines": ["I'm in love with the guap, gave it a wedding ring"], "meaning": "Guap is slang for money. Carti  expresses his love for money by giving it a wedding ring. Rather than being committed in a traditional relationship, he vows to spend his life keeping cash his number one priority.", "annotation_id": "11624396", "url": "https://genius.com/11624396", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "I’m a rockstar (Yeah) I’m a rockstar (Know I got a lot, lot) I’m a rockstar I’m a rockstar", "vault_lines": ["Know I got a lot, lot"], "meaning": "Uzi is a self-proclaimed rockstar, frequently using the term to describe his musical career.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/liluzivert/status/725331530189541376?lang=en\n\nHe uses the term to distinguish the difference between the old and new generations of hip-hop. In an interview on HOT 97, Uzi refuses to freestyle on old hip-hop beat:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/Bq6IsU390E0?t=675\n\nUzi has stated multiple artists as an influence on his career. Some of these artists are rockstars such as GG Allin and Marilyn Manson.", "annotation_id": "11570875", "url": "https://genius.com/11570875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 111, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "wokeuplikethis*", "line": "Oh, I think they like me (Yup), in my white tee (Yup)", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I think they like me (Yup), in my white tee (Yup)"], "meaning": "A reference to both Dem Franchize Boyz songs “Oh I Think They Like Me”, and “White Tee”:\n\nWell I hit the mall in my white tee, ohh I think they like me\n\nThis exact dual reference was first used by Nas on “Hip Hop is dead,” a song that critiqued the rising popularity of non-lyrical rappers in the mid 2000s. Thus, this line may be an aside to the same type of criticism that Lil Uzi and Carti get for not having enough substance in their raps.\n\nLil Uzi has spoken about white tees being one of his favourite items of clothing in a 2019 interview:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/UOqkhnckKTM?t=220", "annotation_id": "11485511", "url": "https://genius.com/11485511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
