{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Got a plug, bring that shit right from Providence", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "uzi got a plug coming from Providence, Rhode island", "annotation_id": "34132025", "url": "https://genius.com/34132025", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Niggas rattin’, they get hit with the MAC today (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas rattin', they get hit with the MAC today (Woo)"], "meaning": "The Military Armament Corporation is an American firearms manufacturer known for their MAC lineup of submachine guns. The MAC lineup–designed by Gordon Ingram–became popular partly due to their compact design in which the magazine is held inside the grip.\n\n\n\nPictured: Ingram’s MAC-10\n\nUzi isn’t new to bringing up submachine guns in his music. In “Canadian Goose” off April 2016’s Lil Uzi Vert vs. The World, Uzi raps:\n\nIn a Cadillac, do a drive-by with a MAC (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "22356591", "url": "https://genius.com/22356591", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Wonton, flood the block with some Wock’ in it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Wontons are a variation of the Chinese dumplings and are extremely popular in Chinese cuisine. Woks are round bottom cooking pans that originated from China and are most commonly used to prepare stir fry.\n\n\n\nUzi creates a double entendre with the word Wok as it is also used to refer to “Wock”, a codeine phosphate syrup manufactured by the pharmaceutical company Wockhardt.\n\nhttps://images.genius.com/cbcbc9577f3b83ac85c9653fed30f74d.1000x263x1.jpg*\n\nFlooding the block could therefore refer to the large amount of lean that he consumes.", "annotation_id": "16823158", "url": "https://genius.com/16823158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Bulletproof on my tank, that’s my insurgency", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "In 2018, Uzi made headlines after purchasing a bullet proof SUV called the Rhino GX that more closely resembles an APC than an SUV. Uzi references his street legal tank by comparing it to the Insurgent from GTA V that was modeled after it’s real life counterpart. https://youtu.be/AU6pgw9LyIE?t=41", "annotation_id": "16820678", "url": "https://genius.com/16820678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Got a tattooed face so you can’t see my blasphemy", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Tattooing oneself is considered an act in defiance of many religions. For example, Leviticus 19:28 reads:\n\nAnd a cutting for the dead you will not make in your flesh; and writing marks you will not make on you; I am the Lord.\n\nWhile Uzi is known for imbuing blasphemous phrases and symbols in his music, one of his face tattoos (the word “Faith” on the right side of his forehead) actually seems to have an anti-blasphemous message.", "annotation_id": "16820642", "url": "https://genius.com/16820642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Backwood on me, bitch, you stay ’rello (What else?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Backwoods are a brand of cigars that are popular amongst many rappers. They come in an assortment of flavors such as Honey and Russian Cream.\n\n\n\n“Rello” refers to cigarellos,  a short, narrow cigar. They are a much lower quality than a hand-rolled Backwood.\n\nUzi has shows his preference to Backwoods before; on “Canadian Goose” off Lil Uzi Vert vs. The World he raps:\n\nSmoking Backwoods I don’t fuck with doobies", "annotation_id": "16820137", "url": "https://genius.com/16820137", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Got them boulders, my neck won’t see a pebble (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Uzi is referring to diamond rocks. While boulders would be really large diamonds, pebbles are small and puny.\nUzi has absurd amounts of diamond-encrusted chains and pendants and all of them are covered with big diamonds.", "annotation_id": "16818525", "url": "https://genius.com/16818525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Pastry, pocket, boy, you not havin’ cake", "vault_lines": ["Pastry, pocket, boy, you not havin' cake"], "meaning": "Pastry is slang for a person who is really cheap.\nCake is slang for money. Pastry is also used as a double entendre in this line, as cake is a type of pastry, Uzi is using that as another way to refer to money.\n\nUzi spells out the fact that he has a lot of money in his pockets in comparison to others.", "annotation_id": "16818449", "url": "https://genius.com/16818449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "These old niggas wan’ rob me like a burglary (Let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is referencing the drama that he is dealing with, as a result of conflict with his record label. The leaders of his record label, Don Cannon and DJ Drama, are supposedly keeping him hostage and reportedly being dishonest in compensating him for his music.\n\nWhile DJ Drama (40 years old) and Don Cannon (39) can hardly be considered “old”, Lil Uzi considers them such since he is only 24 years old.\n\nhttps://images.complex.com/complex/images/c_limit,w_680/fl_lossy,pg_1,q_auto/vmqrbl4psfpzrqel9tds/lil-uzi-vert-don-cannon-dj-drama\n\nUzi would later make similar comments after DJ Drama danced to Uzi’s late 2019 single “Futsal Shuffle 2020”:\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/1202995742308274181", "annotation_id": "16818397", "url": "https://genius.com/16818397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "I’m liftin’ these big ol’ stacks like my name Hercules", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Hercules is a Roman God and hero, known for his adventures and inhumane strength. Hercules was put through a long list of challenges, dubbed the “labours”. Along the way during his challenges, Hercules had to lift the son of Poseidon, Antaeus, in order to defeat him in a wrestling match, which he also did.\n\n\n\nUzi compares Hercules' heroic lift to the way he has to lift his stacks of cash.", "annotation_id": "16818363", "url": "https://genius.com/16818363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Alexander Wang, bitch, I came from poverty", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Alexander Wang is a famous American designer clothing brand. Uzi mentioned wearing Alexander Wang clothing before, on the 2015 track, “Paradise”, where he sung:\n\nAlexander the Wang, Alexander McQueen\n\nUzi utilizes juxtaposition to demonstrate how far he’s come. He went from being poor in the projects of Philadelphia to being able to afford expensive brands like Alexander Wang.", "annotation_id": "16818349", "url": "https://genius.com/16818349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Rollie cost me forty thousand, that’s half the face (Let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Rollie cost me forty thousand, that's half the face (Let's go)"], "meaning": "Rolex is a luxury watch manufacturer from Switzerland. Their watches are very popular in rap-culture and many artists use them to display their lavish lifestyles.\n\nLil Uzi Vert is no exception to the rapper Rolex craze and has owned a variety of timepieces. A story was posted to his Instagram in January 2018 showing off his new rainbow diamond bezel Rolex.\n\nUzi isn’t new to rapping about his expensive watches. In his November 2017 track, “Loaded,” he raps about another watch:\n\nWatch cost 81 thousand like Terrell Owens", "annotation_id": "16818336", "url": "https://genius.com/16818336", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Frito-Lay, yeah, you know that I’m stackin’ chips", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Frito-Lay is an American company that specializes in the production of chips. Uzi compares his stacks of money to the supply of chips that are made by the company.", "annotation_id": "16818308", "url": "https://genius.com/16818308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "I can’t trust none of these niggas, might turn on me I’m still a millionaire, this shit not hurtin’ me (Woah) But it’s hurtin’ you (Yeah) And I know the truth", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert has addressed trust issues before and has been open about it on songs too, like on YoungBoy NBA’s June 2018 track, “Rich Nigga”:\n\nThey changed on me so many times, I cannot trust no one\n\nThese lines could be directed toward DJ Don Cannon and DJ Drama, co-founders of the label Generation Now, who Uzi inked a deal with in 2015. Due to label disputes, the Philadelphia rapper hasn’t been able to release his second studio album Eternal Atake. Despite this, Uzi’s still well-off, with an estimated net worth of $17 million.\n\nOn Instagram Live, Lil Uzi mentioned his frustration with Generation Now as well:\n\nYou think I don’t wanna drop music? You just gotta understand, when people don’t love you, they’ll hold your life if you sign a motherfucking—Hold that shit against you…", "annotation_id": "16818268", "url": "https://genius.com/16818268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Grandma in the kitchen still singin’ “Happy Days” (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Grandma in the kitchen still singin' \"Happy Days\" (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Happy Days is an American sitcom that aired from January 1974 to September 1984. The theme song was considered very catchy and peaked at number 5 on the Billboard Hot 100.", "annotation_id": "16818220", "url": "https://genius.com/16818220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Nigga’s lyin’, yeah, he stuck with a cappin’ face", "vault_lines": ["Nigga's lyin', yeah, he stuck with a cappin' face"], "meaning": "This line is referring to Uzi’s feud with his label, Generation Now, and the label’s owners, DJ Drama and Don Cannon.\n\nUzi has had troubles with his label not allowing him to drop any new music for many months before this song was released. Back in the December of 2018, Uzi already claimed that his album, Eternal Atake, was ready for release, later claiming that the label won’t let him release it, with DJ Drama and Cannon both claiming that Uzi has actually had their consent to release the project for a long time.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BvYvmQ6H9tH/?utm_source=ig_embed\n\nUzi is saying that while Drama and Cannon may want to make it seem like dropping the album is entirely up to Uzi, he says that they are lying, or in other words, capping.", "annotation_id": "16818088", "url": "https://genius.com/16818088", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Gave me head ’til my shit, um, decapitate Look me in my eye and do, um, that nasty face (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Gave me head 'til my shit, um, decapitate"], "meaning": "Uzi explicitly describes himself ejaculating as a result of getting oral sex, comparing it to decapitation.\n\n\n\nThe result of decapitation — viewer friendly edition\n\n\nWhen the head is removed from the body, the heart will continue to pump out blood for a while, gushing it out the neck, something that Uzi think is similar to him climaxing.\n\nUzi also mentions oral sex in the second verse on the song:\n\nShe was suckin' my dick right on her knees\nHer mama bust her, she said, “Girl, what is happenin'?”\nShe said, “Baby, you know your dad a pastor”\nShe said, “Mama, I’m just doin' the Kaepernick”", "annotation_id": "16818060", "url": "https://genius.com/16818060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Make it rain in the club, like a nasty day Told ’em that I’m comin’, oh, no ejaculate", "vault_lines": ["Make it rain in the club, like a nasty day"], "meaning": "Uzi makes this wordplay when talking about clubs.\n\nUzi refers to this as a nasty day, which means it could be raining, but he is making it rain money in a club, not water.\n\nBut “cumming,” (pronounced ‘coming’) is a common term for ejaculation.", "annotation_id": "16818041", "url": "https://genius.com/16818041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Yeah, I remember when that girl didn’t need me I didn’t have no money, and I couldn’t find out what’s the reason (Why?) Now that ho back on my team, ’cause my neck wet like a squeegee (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Back in 2016, Uzi was in a relationship with fashion designer Brittany Byrd. Uzi and Brittany seemingly parted their ways before the release of Uzi’s album Luv Is Rage 2, for that reason Uzi says that she “didn’t need him.” It seems that Uzi realized that Brittany didn’t seem to want him back then, because he didn’t have as much money.\n\nDuring their relationship, Uzi put out the song titled “Team Rocket” which was thought to be about Uzi’s relationship with Brittany comparing their bond to Team Rocket from the Pokémon universe.\n\n\n\nUzi’s neck looks like a squeegee, because it is “wet” due to all of the expensive diamonds around it. Diamonds and diamond-encrusted jewelry are both often referred to as “water” in the rap game and because Uzi has a lot of diamond chains, his neck is “wet.”\n\n\n\nBrittany posted a photo of her together with Uzi on her Instagram page a few days before the release of this track, meaning that they might both once again be part of the “team,” as Uzi now has more money.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Uzi has used “squeegee” in his raps. On his July 2016 song, “You’re Lost,” Uzi raps:\n\nAnd she wetter than a squeegee", "annotation_id": "16818038", "url": "https://genius.com/16818038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "I’m not tall, but I ball like a athlete Count my money, yeah, I turn to a mathlete", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert stands at 5'4\", which makes him lower than the average adult male. Despite his lack of height, Uzi still claims to “ball” at a professional level—players in the NBA have an average height of 6'7\" or 200.4 cm.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i_txu7U7oLw\n\nThere’s a double entendre in these lines, as “ball” is a slang term for being affluent—Uzi has an estimated net worth of $17 million. This isn’t the first time Uzi compensates for his height with his money either; on Zaytoven’s 2017 track “A Lot,” Uzi raps:\n\nStand on my money, I’m 7'10\" (Damn)", "annotation_id": "16818024", "url": "https://genius.com/16818024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "Free Uzi, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "“Free Uzi” is a hashtag which started on Twitter and Instagram following trouble Uzi had with his record label.\n\nLeading up to this track, Uzi was re-posting several pictures from fans which included the hashtag on his Instagram stories, despite his label having recently said that he is completely free to release his long-awaited second studio album, Eternal Atake, whenever he wants.", "annotation_id": "16817962", "url": "https://genius.com/16817962", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "I still watch Big Bang Theory, that’s the nerd in me", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "The Big Bang Theory, a comedy TV series which started in 2007, is a sitcom about two extremely smart but socially awkward physicists working at Cal Tech in California. They are often referred to as ‘nerds,’ since the definition of the word is both “a person who is awkward or socially embarrassing” and “a person who is extremely interested in one subject.", "annotation_id": "16817946", "url": "https://genius.com/16817946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "(Oh my God, what is this? An L beat?)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Uzi is rapping over the instrumental of G Herbo’s June 2012 track, “Gangway,” which was produced by DJ L Beats.", "annotation_id": "16817922", "url": "https://genius.com/16817922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "She was suckin’ my dick right on her knees Her mama bust in, she said, “Girl, what is happenin’?” She said, “Baby, you know your dad a pastor?” She said, “Mama, I’m just doin’ the Kaepernick”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "Uzi compares the girl’s knee stand while giving him oral sex to the former NFL quarterback, Colin Kaepernick.\n\n\n\nEric Reid (left) & Colin Kaepernick (right)\n\n\nKaepernick received huge publicity for taking a knee during the national anthem which made many other NFL players follow this action. These were acts of protest against racial discrimination and the Donald Trump presidency.\n\nUzi also mentions oral sex in the song’s chorus:\n\nGave me head ‘til my shit, um, decapitate\nLook me in my eye and do, um, that nasty face", "annotation_id": "16817877", "url": "https://genius.com/16817877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "I just popped a G6, I’m in my happy place", "vault_lines": ["I just popped a G6, I'm in my happy place"], "meaning": "A G-6 is an ecstasy pill stamped with a G-6 logo — Uzi is known to be a fan of ecstasy, jokingly asking Nardwuar if it was legal in Canada after a show.\n\nHe said a fan had given him “legal” ecstasy and jokingly grilled Nardwuar on Canadian drug laws.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fS0CkTtPgOM", "annotation_id": "16817875", "url": "https://genius.com/16817875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "free uzi", "line": "We served them packs in the net, we get them racks like Serena, uh (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sun out, so my boys gonna trap today"], "meaning": "The whole line serves as a play on words with ‘served,’ ‘net,’ and ‘racks.’\n\nFirst, Uzi implies that they sold the stuff online and got large amounts of money doing so. Then he goes on to compare himself to Serena Williams due to the money he has earned. Serena Williams is a very successful tennis player with a very large amount of money won from tournaments only.\n\n\nthe word ʼservedʼ is also used to refer to tennis as one serves the ball.\nthe word ʼnetʼ is used to describe the internet, but also refers to the net that’s used in tennis courts.\nʼracksʼ refers to racquets used in tennis, while also referring to a rack of cash.\n\n\n\n\n\nPictured: Serena Williams", "annotation_id": "16817830", "url": "https://genius.com/16817830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
