{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "We got that 5, we let it spray", "vault_lines": ["We got that 5, we let it spray"], "meaning": "A threat masked in street talk. “That 5” likely refers to a .45 caliber handgun. Uzi implies he and his crew won’t hesitate to retaliate if disrespected or threatened.", "annotation_id": "36329430", "url": "https://genius.com/36329430", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "How you gonna be my mans If you wanna talk on the gang?", "vault_lines": ["How you gonna be my mans"], "meaning": "Uzi questions loyalty. Calling someone “my mans” implies brotherhood or close friendship, but talking down on the “gang” (his circle or crew) is an act of betrayal, which completely contradicts that trust.", "annotation_id": "36329418", "url": "https://genius.com/36329418", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "My heart done gone like Kanye", "vault_lines": ["My heart done gone like Kanye"], "meaning": "This is a clever reference to Kanye West’s 808s & Heartbreak era, known for its emotional vulnerability and heartbreak themes. Uzi compares his emotional state to Kanye’s during that time, suggesting he’s equally broken or detached. Could also imply emotional numbness or instability.", "annotation_id": "36329410", "url": "https://genius.com/36329410", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
