{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "She wanna tell the world I did wrong", "vault_lines": ["She wanna tell the world I did wrong"], "meaning": "This could definitely be a reference to Brittney Byrd, Uzi’s longtime ex and someone fans often associate with emotional tension in his music.", "annotation_id": "36329383", "url": "https://genius.com/36329383", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "I hopped in that Jag, I’m gone", "vault_lines": ["I hopped in that Jag, I’m gone"], "meaning": "This line shows Uzi physically and mentally distancing himself, literally driving off in a Jaguar (a luxury car brand), symbolizing escape and success. It fits the theme of moving on, detachment, or fleeing emotional pain.", "annotation_id": "36329374", "url": "https://genius.com/36329374", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "Look at how I swag, Ricky on", "vault_lines": ["Look at how I swag, Ricky on"], "meaning": "This references Rick Owens, a high-end fashion designer known for dark, grungy aesthetics, perfectly aligned with Uzi’s visual style. It reinforces the luxury and individuality in his fashion game.", "annotation_id": "36329342", "url": "https://genius.com/36329342", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "Yeah, I ain’t felt this way in so long", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I ain’t felt this way in so long"], "meaning": "Uzi expresses vulnerability here. Whether it’s pain, love, or nostalgia, this line suggests a deep emotional shift caused by the return or presence of someone important (or damaging).", "annotation_id": "36329331", "url": "https://genius.com/36329331", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "d3mons (Interlude)", "line": "Demons in my head when she come", "vault_lines": ["Demons in my head when she come"], "meaning": "This line introduces the theme of internal struggle, “demons” referring to mental battles or emotional pain. The presence of “she” triggers these demons, suggesting Uzi associates this person with trauma or emotional chaos.", "annotation_id": "36329308", "url": "https://genius.com/36329308", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
