{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "Size 29 my jeans, but my clip is a thirty", "vault_lines": ["Size 29 my jeans, but my clip is a thirty"], "meaning": "He does a wordplay on his guns magazine. Lil Uzi is known to be 5'4, which means that he doesn’t have large clothing sizes. Furthermore his gun’s magazine/clip is a .30 or a .30 round. However, he is more likely referring to a 30 round magazine, since .30 are typically used by handcannons or carbines. He means that he keeps a gun with a large magazine wherever he goes despite him being short in contrast to the latter.", "annotation_id": "22728060", "url": "https://genius.com/22728060", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "Size 29 my jeans, but my clip is a thirty", "vault_lines": ["Size 29 my jeans, but my clip is a thirty"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is no stranger to the street life and often references guns in his songs. In this line, Uzi says that he wears size 29 waist jeans but he owns a gun with a 30 round clip.\n\nHis name Uzi, also is a name of an Israeli submachine gun that can also hold a 30 round ammunition clip as well.\n\nAlso, he may be referring to a diamond chain he owns that resembles a uzi gun with a detachable clip.", "annotation_id": "17816780", "url": "https://genius.com/17816780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "(Wheezy outta here)", "vault_lines": ["No, I will not answer, please do not do call my phone"], "meaning": "This is one of the numerous tags for Atlanta producer Wheezy, and most likely his most used tag. The producer is most known for his work with other fellow Atlanta artists Gunna and Young Thug, but most importantly for his two hit connections with Drake on Lil Baby’s 2018 song “Yes Indeed” and on Meek Mill’s song “Going Bad.”\n\nThis track is not the first collaboration between Uzi and Wheezy, the two artists previously teamed up on Uzi’s 2015 track “Queso” and on the two 2019 leaked songs “Harden” and “Big Watch”.", "annotation_id": "17812771", "url": "https://genius.com/17812771", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "Pull up, my car, it go, “Vroom” This a coupe, no, no legroom Pull up on your bitch like, “Zoom”", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, my car, it go, \"Vroom\""], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert juxtaposes the power and speed of his car with how quickly he can steal someone else’s girlfriend. In January 2019, he displayed his large collection of luxury vehicles in a picture on Instagram. The image depicts a Bentley coupe, a Lamborghini, and a Rolls Royce, among others.", "annotation_id": "17791188", "url": "https://genius.com/17791188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "Double cup, it’s Styrofoam", "vault_lines": ["Double cup, it's Styrofoam"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert alludes to lean- a recreational concoction made of promethazine, Sprite, and flavorful candy. According to Nova Recovery Center, the illicit substance is addictive and can lead to serious health concerns.\n\nLil Uzi’s January 2014 mixtape Purple Thoughtz Ep. Vol. 1 explicitly dives into the consequences of his incessant drug usage and his “rockstar” lifestyle, as the title itself references lean.\n\nUzi used similar terminology on his January 2014 track, “Puff”:\n\nDouble Cup full of mud mouth full of dirt\nIf it ain’t xanny them I’m on the purp", "annotation_id": "17791155", "url": "https://genius.com/17791155", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Zoom", "line": "No, I will not answer, please do not do call my phone Mr. Do-Not-Answer-Phone Please, oh, girl, oh, leave me ’lone", "vault_lines": ["No, I will not answer, please do not do call my phone"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is known for being antisocial and reclusive. His preference to be alone and unhinged from society is a common topic throughout his discography. On the song “Erase Your Social”, Uzi raps:\n\nI ain’t got no Snapchat, homie\nI think it’s too personal\n\nUzi was also famously video recorded saying that he wouldn’t immediately purchase another phone, despite his estimated net worth of $17 million.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qUaQi349NR0", "annotation_id": "15292460", "url": "https://genius.com/15292460", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
