{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Young Nigga", "line": "I don’t drive no Charger, I beat all my charges", "vault_lines": ["I don't drive no Charger, I beat all my charges"], "meaning": "Lil Yachty alludes to the controversies he’s faced throughout his early life, stemming from his frequent felonies and stints in jail. Yachty previously references his acquittal on his January 2016 track, “Minnesota”:\n\nAlmost had a lifetime sentence, but I beat it, shout out to Pat!\nPat, that’s my lawyer, he got me off them charges\"\n\nYachty boasts his newfound freedom and exorbitant wealth, which allows him to purchase more expensive cars than Dodge Chargers.", "annotation_id": "13373338", "url": "https://genius.com/13373338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Young Nigga", "line": "I’m not 21 but I’ll slaughter your daughter, bitch", "vault_lines": ["I'm not 21 but I'll slaughter your daughter, bitch"], "meaning": "This is reference to 21 Savage’s song “Slaughter Ya Daughter”.", "annotation_id": "11329816", "url": "https://genius.com/11329816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Young Nigga", "line": "Ballin’ so hard, change my name to Vince Carter", "vault_lines": ["Ballin' so hard, change my name to Vince Carter"], "meaning": "“Balling” is slang for living a wealthy lifestyle, as well as for playing basketball, hence the comparison to Grizzlies player Vince Carter.", "annotation_id": "11265574", "url": "https://genius.com/11265574", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Young Nigga", "line": "Now I do commercials, I’m so controversial Everytime they see me, they hatin’ They hate when I win but they love when I sin These niggas gon’ wake the man that’s within", "vault_lines": ["Now I do commercials, I'm so controversial"], "meaning": "In October 2016 Lil Yachty starred in a Sprite commercial alongside LeBron James, parodying his song “Minnesota”.\n\n\n\nSince Yachty gained popularity, he has been a frequent target of criticism from old school hip-hop enthusiasts, such as Pete Rock and Hot 97’s Ebro Darden. Lil Boat is known for being a “nice guy” that doesn’t like to take things too seriously, but he wouldn’t hesitate to show his dark side if his detractors ever got to him.", "annotation_id": "11262946", "url": "https://genius.com/11262946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
