{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "I shot at him once, shoot that boy, he said, “Oh, no”", "vault_lines": ["I shot at him once, shoot that boy, he said, \"Oh, no\""], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert references the infamous 2021 incident in which he was accused of threatening the rapper SAINt JHN with a firearm while he was on a date with his ex-girlfriend Brittany Byrd.\n\nLater, the rapper pleaded no contest to the charges, receiving three years of probation and other court-ordered conditions.\n\nAdditionally, the phrase “Oh, no” sound like “Ono”, the surname of Yoko Ono.", "annotation_id": "40893114", "url": "https://genius.com/40893114", "state": "accepted", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "Poured up a six, this ain’t Tris on the scale", "vault_lines": ["Poured up a six, this ain't Tris on the scale"], "meaning": "“Poured up a six” means he poured 6 ounces of lean (codeine/promethazine syrup) into his drink. Tris is a specific brand of that cough syrup.", "annotation_id": "40890644", "url": "https://genius.com/40890644", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "I’m really The Rock, this ain’t promo", "vault_lines": ["I'm really The Rock, this ain't promo (Uh)"], "meaning": "The Rock refers to Dwayne “The Rock” Johnson, the famous wrestler-turned-actor.", "annotation_id": "40890614", "url": "https://genius.com/40890614", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "I’m so fresh, you dressed like hobo (Ah, hobo)", "vault_lines": ["I'm so fresh, you dressed like hobo (Ah, hobo)"], "meaning": "A hobo is an old slang term for a homeless person or someone wearing ragged, dirty, or very low-effort clothes.", "annotation_id": "40890608", "url": "https://genius.com/40890608", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "I hope JT don’t think she Yoko (No)", "vault_lines": ["I hope JT don't think she Yoko (No)"], "meaning": "JT is his girlfriend (the rapper from City Girls). Yoko refers to Yoko Ono, the artist and widow of John Lennon who has long been blamed by some Beatles fans for breaking up the band.", "annotation_id": "40890594", "url": "https://genius.com/40890594", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "Throw up the rock like it’s promo", "vault_lines": ["Throw up the rock like it's promo (Promo)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert recently signed to Roc Nation Distribution. “Throwing up the Roc” means making Roc-A-Fella’s signature diamond hand symbol.", "annotation_id": "40889142", "url": "https://genius.com/40889142", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yoko", "line": "My jewelry all real, I ain’t Ocho (Huh? Ocho)", "vault_lines": ["My jewelry all real, I ain't Ocho (Huh? Ocho)"], "meaning": "Uzi jabs at former NFL player Chad Johnson, better known as “Ochocinco,” who has gone on record admitting to frequently wearing fake jewelry during his playing career despite earning nearly $50 million:\n\nNever bought real anything when I was playing, never. What was the point? I went to Claire’s.", "annotation_id": "40889062", "url": "https://genius.com/40889062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
