{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yes Yes (Patek Swag)", "line": "(Yo, Pi’erre, you wanna come out here?)", "vault_lines": ["Look at my wrist, yes, yes"], "meaning": "This is the tag for the song’s producer, Pi'erre Bourne. The line is sampled from an episode of ’90s sitcom The Jamie Foxx Show.\n\nIn the opening scene of the show’s fourth episode, Jamie is waiting tables in his hotel’s restaurant. After a patron complains about his french toast, Jamie says that they have a chef directly from France, and yells out, “Yo, Pierre, you wanna come out here?” Jamie also makes the door-creaking sound that follows the tag.\n\nPi'erre and Uzi have collaborated numerous times on this record, as seen on “Wassup,” “Bean (Kobe),” and “Money Spread.”", "annotation_id": "25560417", "url": "https://genius.com/25560417", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yes Yes (Patek Swag)", "line": "(Yo, Pi’erre, you wanna come out here?)", "vault_lines": ["Look at my wrist, yes, yes"], "meaning": "This is the tag for the song’s producer, Pi'erre Bourne. The line is sampled from an episode of ’90s sitcom The Jamie Foxx Show.\n\nIn the opening scene of the show’s fourth episode, Jamie is waiting tables in his hotel’s restaurant. After a patron complains about his french toast, Jamie says that they have a chef directly from France, and yells out, “Yo, Pierre, you wanna come out here?” Jamie also makes the door-creaking sound that follows the tag.\n\nPi'erre and Uzi have collaborated numerous times on this record, as seen on “Wassup,” “Bean (Kobe),” and “Money Spread.”", "annotation_id": "25560407", "url": "https://genius.com/25560407", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
