{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yea Yea (Bankroll Original)", "line": "Ayy, ayy Pull up, wait, ayy On a date, ayy Countin’ cake, ayy Play with my cake, ayy Break your face, ayy Countin’ cake, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Play with my cake, ayy"], "meaning": "In these bars, Lil Uzi Vert is bragging about pulling up in a lavish car with his date and counting his money while he is out with her. He is subtly trying to portray himself as a successful and wealthy individual. Additionally, the line “Play with my cake/Countin' cake” implies his desire to have his date engage with him on a sexual level, and possibly that he will bring her back to his luxurious house or apartment. He is essentially inviting the girl to have her world “broken” by his luxuries and charm.", "annotation_id": "30561386", "url": "https://genius.com/30561386", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Yea Yea (Bankroll Original)", "line": "Told that bitch to call my phone Then she text my phone with upset face, and I look like yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Told that bitch to call my phone"], "meaning": "In this bar, Lil Uzi Vert describes ignoring a female’s phone call and then responding casually to her text message with an emoticon representing a nonchalant or care-free attitude. His tone reflects a dismissive or arrogant attitude towards the female, indicating that he is not impressed with or affected by her display of emotion. This line portrays his attitude towards women as dismissive and inconsiderate, and illustrates his portrayal of his “player” persona.", "annotation_id": "30561379", "url": "https://genius.com/30561379", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
