{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "And we ain’t gon’ give these niggas fame, but my nigga Ikey had that nigga bitch out in LA", "vault_lines": ["And we ain't gon' give these niggas fame, but my nigga Ikey had that nigga bitch out in LA"], "meaning": "Uzi shouts out Ike, better known as Ike Beats.\n\nIke is from Philadephia and has been working with Uzi on multiple tracks, most notably “The Way Life Goes” and “444+222”.", "annotation_id": "14210520", "url": "https://genius.com/14210520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "(DP on the beat)", "vault_lines": ["We gettin' money, man, fuck all that hatin' shit"], "meaning": "The producer tag for DP Beats. DP Beats has worked closely with Lil Uzi on multiple songs, such as “7AM” and “Ready, Set, Go”. He is also well known for working closely with artist Chief Keef very frequently.", "annotation_id": "13155072", "url": "https://genius.com/13155072", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "I was just with my grandma sleeping on futons", "vault_lines": ["I was just with my grandma sleeping on futons"], "meaning": "Uzi’s parents were separated, so he frequently stayed at his grandma’s house. By purchasing Uzi his first CD from a thrift store by the Ying Yang Twinz, she helped contribute to his interest in music. Uzi even explained in an interview that his grandma bought him his very first pair of platinum grills and having to repay her.", "annotation_id": "11643624", "url": "https://genius.com/11643624", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Put Spikey and Ikey in Dior, yeah, that suit tie Ikey smilin’ like, “No more, I don’t gotta move dimes”", "vault_lines": ["Put Spikey and Ikey in Dior, yeah, that suit tie"], "meaning": "Christian Dior is a high fashion brand based out of Paris, France. Among other celebrities, A$AP Rocky modeled for the brands summer 2017 ad campaign.\n\n\n\nSpiky and Ike are two of Uzi’s close friends. Uzi explains that due to his new found fame and fortune he can afford to share his wealth with his day one homies by dressing them in expensive clothing (Dior). LUV adds that the wealth he has accumulated has provided stability for the lives of his friends as well as his own, they no longer have to rely on street hustling or moving dimes just to simply get by.", "annotation_id": "11601735", "url": "https://genius.com/11601735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Got a red dot Got a blue dot", "vault_lines": ["Got a red drop (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here Uzi is explaining the different types of holographic weapon sights he attaches to his guns. Non-magnifying reflector sights project a reticle (most commonly a colored dot) on a special peice of glass that acts as an aimpoint to assist in the aiming of a firearm. They are used as the industry standard for most modern militaries around the world. However, due to their harmless nature and relatively cheap cost, they are available for civilian purchase", "annotation_id": "11440710", "url": "https://genius.com/11440710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Got a red drop (Yeah) Got a blue drop (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Got a red drop (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Here, Uzi refers to drop top cars. A slang classification of a convertible vehicle. The term drop top (shortened to simply drop in this context) is a very common term within the hip-hop community. One famous example being in the chorus of Migos smash hit track, Bad and Boujee, off of their 2017 album CULTURE which also featured a verse from LUV himself.\n\nRaindrop (drip), drop top (drop top)\nSmokin' on cookie in the hotbox (cookie)", "annotation_id": "11429827", "url": "https://genius.com/11429827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "She talked to me when she right on her knees, said, “I can’t believe I blew ya” That girl, she like to come kick it with me ’cause her boyfriend is a loser", "vault_lines": ["She talked to me when she right on her knees, said, \"I can't believe I blew ya\""], "meaning": "In this line, Lil Uzi Vert is insinuating that he has received oral sex from the aforementioned cougar.  Due to Uzi’s fame and social status, said cougar is surprised that she was awarded the opportunity to please Uzi. LUV then adds that the girl is more than ready to hang out with Uzi rather than her boyfriend due to Uzi’s interesting and fun lifestyle, which her boyfriend lacks.\n\nThis concept of stealing committed women is one that is prevalent in many of Uzi’s tracks.", "annotation_id": "11422500", "url": "https://genius.com/11422500", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "I can’t be the shooter right now ’cause I’m smoking Moon Rock", "vault_lines": ["I can't be the shooter right now 'cause I'm smoking Moon Rock"], "meaning": "Uzi can’t shoot straight at the moment because he is high off of moon rock. Moonrock refers to marijuana buds soaked in hash oil then sprinkled with keef. Moonrock is considered to be some of the strongest cannabis in the world.", "annotation_id": "11422094", "url": "https://genius.com/11422094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Countin’ them blue stacks Yeah, that’s them blue racks Yeah, that’s them blue racks Yeah, that’s them blue racks", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them blue stacks"], "meaning": "“Blue racks” and “Blue stacks” are referencing the newer version of the $100 dollar bill. These new bills have a blue security strip on them. Uzi is just counting his riches.", "annotation_id": "11421562", "url": "https://genius.com/11421562", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Just talked to Future, he in Dubai", "vault_lines": ["Just talked to Future, he in Dubai"], "meaning": "Future recently filmed his music video for “Poppin' Tags” in Dubai. Uzi probably talked to Future over the phone during this time.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxKFI7FONNw\n\nIn 2014, DJ Esco, a frequent Future collaborator, was arrested and sentenced to serve jail time after being caught possessing marijuana by airport officials in Dubai. After spending 56 nights in prison, Esco was finally released. Future and Esco later dropped a mixtape titled 56 Nights inspired by the terrifying ordeal.", "annotation_id": "11420997", "url": "https://genius.com/11420997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "In Vegas I stay at Venetian with a cougar", "vault_lines": ["In Vegas I stay at Venetian with a cougar"], "meaning": "When Uzi is in Vegas he stays at the Venetian, a five diamond luxury hotel. He stays there with a cougar (an older woman seeking a sexual relationship with a younger man.) This shows how Uzi has the money to afford luxurious things and the ability to attract women through his wealth.", "annotation_id": "11418503", "url": "https://genius.com/11418503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "YSL", "line": "Doin’ good for yourself, they wanna shoot ya Stop tryna finesse me out my mula (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Doin' good for yourself, they wanna shoot ya"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert feels that because of his recent success and popularity, people or possibly old friends have began targeting him out of jealousy. This is a common theme in hip-hop outlining the way fame and success can effect an individuals social life, most prominently described in Kanye West’s, Real Friends, off of his 2016 album, The Life of Pablo. LUV’s success has also drawn the  attention of fake friends or gold diggers that are simply trying to benefit from his wealth. Uzi urges them to stop trying to deceive him just to get at his money or moolah.", "annotation_id": "11417798", "url": "https://genius.com/11417798", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
