{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Xan Today (Butter)", "line": "Peanut butter my seats, can’t get jammed today", "vault_lines": ["Peanut butter my seats, can't get jammed today"], "meaning": "Uzi calls his seats peanut butter because they are brown", "annotation_id": "39677976", "url": "https://genius.com/39677976", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Xan Today (Butter)", "line": "Got the Glock on my side (Ayy), it stick to me like butter (Ayy) Gun on my right and got one on my other It was just me and my motho’ fuckin’ brotha’ We don’t trust y’all, so why would you trust us? We saw an opp, he ran away We shot his man, in plain day", "vault_lines": ["Got the Glock on my side (Ayy), it stick to me like butter (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Being one of the most-streamed artists of all-time, Lil Uzi Vert maintains a Glock—an automatic gun, used for self-defense—on their side, most likely due to the deaths of numerous rappers surrounding him due to gun-related violence.\n\nHowever, throughout their decade career, Lil Uzi has also received their fair share of gun-related allegations. In July 2021, they were charged and accused of assaulting and aiming a gun at their ex-girlfriend, Brittany Byrd. Shortly after the incident, Brittany would go onto Twitter to state her disapproval of the situation:\n\nDon’t y’all say protect black women right? I’m a black woman", "annotation_id": "29511723", "url": "https://genius.com/29511723", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Xan Today (Butter)", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-xan-today-butter-lyrics", "genius_title": "Xan Today (Butter)", "genius_id": 6744746, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "My cousin G-Wayne got off of manslaughter last week", "vault_lines": ["My cousin G-Wayne got off of manslaughter last week"], "meaning": "I heard that the G' and G-Wayne, stand for ‘Gremlin.’", "annotation_id": "28943908", "url": "https://genius.com/28943908", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Gave my dog a buck fifty, that nigga brought me back three", "vault_lines": ["Gave my dog a buck fifty, that nigga brought me back three"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to a drug deal. A “buck fifty” means 150 (whether that is hundreds or thousands is unknown). The “nigga” is his drug dealer who brings back “three” which is double the amount he gave him ($150 times 2 = $300).", "annotation_id": "27738006", "url": "https://genius.com/27738006", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Young Savage, man, I got my car washed up", "vault_lines": ["Young Savage, man, I got my car washed up"], "meaning": "Here, 21 Savage is saying that he got his car washed at a car wash.  He is expressing his appreciation for the beauty of the American free market.\n\nA car wash, or auto wash, is a facility used to clean the exterior, and in some cases the interior, of cars. Car washes can be self-service, full-service, or fully automated. Car washes may also be events where people pay to have their cars washed by volunteers, often using less specialized equipment, as a fundraiser.\n\n21 Savage is from Atlanta, where there are MANY car washes available.", "annotation_id": "25212413", "url": "https://genius.com/25212413", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "[Verse 5: Kodak Black]", "vault_lines": ["Rest in power, it's all about power"], "meaning": "Lil Yachty shared that Kodak was the only rapper to do his verse once. All four other rappers did multiple takes.", "annotation_id": "24051095", "url": "https://genius.com/24051095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Denny Cascade, what the fuck is the halves", "vault_lines": ["Denny Cascade, what the fuck is the halves"], "meaning": "“Denny Cascade” is a track off of Curry’s debut studio album, Nostalgic 64.\n\nCurry has also had many nicknames throughout his rap career. At the time of the release of Nostalgic 64, Curry’s nickname, or character, was “Denny Cascade.”", "annotation_id": "17419307", "url": "https://genius.com/17419307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "I just smoke them woods (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I just smoke them woods (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A “backwood” is a brand of cheap cigars that are commonly used to roll blunts of marijuana. The tobacco is removed from the wrap and them is refilled and resealed after putting marijuana in them.\n\n\n\n21 has previously mentioned the brand on “No Peace,” off of his second mixtape Slaughter King:\n\nBackwood full of grams", "annotation_id": "17418025", "url": "https://genius.com/17418025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Fuckin’ around with the up echelon", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' around with the up echelon"], "meaning": "In this line Denzel describes himself hanging around with the upper class members of society. 2011 was when Denzel’s career was beginning, as well the year he joined the Raider Klan. This could be a reference to the other members of the Raider Klan already having been successful, hence why Denzel believes he is hanging around and interacting with the upper class members of society.", "annotation_id": "16901159", "url": "https://genius.com/16901159", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "You a old nigga, man, you washed up", "vault_lines": ["You a old nigga, man, you washed up"], "meaning": "In sports and music, people will hit their prime and the graph looks like a bell curve, meaning they start to decline in terms of musical ability. The players/artists that don’t get better and decline are called washed-up.\n\nExamples of washed-up players/artists are: Michael Vick (NFL), Saintvicious (NALCS), and Jermaine O'Neal (NBA), and controversially LL Cool J.\n\nHe has also called out these “old niggas” by dissing them on twitter.\n\n\n\nWith people like Funkmaster Flex targeting newer artists like Lil Pump, Nicki Minaj, and G-Eazy, Joe Budden starting controversy with Migos, and Joe Budden’s consistent line of beef with newer artists, it’s not surprising for one of the artists of the new generation of rappers to call it out.\n\nFellow cypher artist Lil Yachty even called out some of the older rappers who have criticized the turn hip-hop took with the emergence of artists like Future and Young Thug.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kzsZzkvMqRs", "annotation_id": "13374304", "url": "https://genius.com/13374304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Diesel, niggas’ll smoke your ass to have the juice", "vault_lines": ["Diesel, niggas'll smoke your ass to have the juice"], "meaning": "Denzel continues from the previous line to form “Sour Diesel”, a popular strain of marijuana. Consequently, he plays on “smoke” to show that people will kill in order to gain respect or “juice.” This is a term that originated from the 1992 film of the same name which noticeably starred 2Pac.", "annotation_id": "12701317", "url": "https://genius.com/12701317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Squeeze two lemons together and really all you’ll have is sour", "vault_lines": ["Squeeze two lemons together and really all you'll have is sour"], "meaning": "This is a take on the popular phrase, “When life gives you lemons, make lemonade”. It means to remain optimistic even when faced with a misfortunate or strenuous situation.\n\nDenzel flips the phrase to “all you’ll have is sour” to show that people don’t always get what they deserve.", "annotation_id": "12775428", "url": "https://genius.com/12775428", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Bitch, I’m from the hood (Yeah) Zone 6, Bouldercrest Road, you can’t go there", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, bitch, you know that"], "meaning": "The Atlanta PD is divided to six distinct patrol zones, with Zone 6 covering Atlanta’s East Side, including Savage’s home of Bouldercrest Road.\n\n\n\nZone 6 has earned a reputation as a trap hub due to how many rappers  call the area home (21 Savage, Gucci Mane, and Future, to name a few), and its history of drug and gang activity. Take it from Savage, keep out.", "annotation_id": "12406176", "url": "https://genius.com/12406176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "21, 21, 21, 21, 21, 21", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, wait, 21, Lil Boat, yeah (Win)"], "meaning": "21 is the first part of 21 Savage’s name and is the name of his gang. He frequently uses this style of repetition as an ad-lib in his songs.", "annotation_id": "10982411", "url": "https://genius.com/10982411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 157, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Youngin and restless, return with a past", "vault_lines": ["Youngin and restless, return with a past"], "meaning": "The Young and the Restless is a soap opera that older people watch. Characters often leave the show and come back with a whole new backstory or additons .", "annotation_id": "10776232", "url": "https://genius.com/10776232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Pulled up on your bitch, she sucked my dick And then you kissed her (Goddamn, 21)", "vault_lines": ["Pulled up on your bitch, she sucked my dick"], "meaning": "21 Savage is letting a specific hater know that he’s been hitting his girl up and hooking up with her.\n\n21 got oral from the girl and is laughing now because her partner gave her a kiss, meaning by association that he sucked 21 Savage’s dick.\n\nThis lyric was first used by The Game on the hook of his 2014 single “T.H.O.T.”.\n\nSavage has a similar line on “No Heart,” off of his 2016 collaborative tape with Metro Boomin, Savage Mode, where he says:\n\nYeah, nigga, fuck all that, ask your bitch how my dick tastes", "annotation_id": "10621300", "url": "https://genius.com/10621300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "I’m from the ugly corner, man, them lil’ sour ass streets", "vault_lines": ["I'm from the ugly corner, man, them lil' sour ass streets"], "meaning": "Kodak’s block is referred to the 1800 ugly corner in Pompano Beach, Florida. This area is a very poverty stricken area full of crime and gang life.", "annotation_id": "10256655", "url": "https://genius.com/10256655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Young Savage, bitch And I don’t play ’round with them swishers (Hmm?)", "vault_lines": ["And I don't play 'round with them swishers (Hmm?)"], "meaning": "Swisher is a brand of cigar that’s commonly utilized to create blunts.\n\n21 has stated before in interviews that he does not smoke Marijuana because it makes him very paranoid; however, the next line says otherwise.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=50MZXWGh-wc", "annotation_id": "10238518", "url": "https://genius.com/10238518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Tied, they dead flies", "vault_lines": ["Tied, they dead flies"], "meaning": "This may be a callback to Kodak’s 2015 Institution cut, “Me, Myself & I,” where he rapped:\n\nProject baby paper chasing, tied, they dead flies", "annotation_id": "10098861", "url": "https://genius.com/10098861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 556, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Young nigga in the Gucci Stans", "vault_lines": ["Young nigga in the Gucci Stans"], "meaning": "A reference to Gucci brand shoes which resemble the popular “Stan Smith’s” by Adidas", "annotation_id": "10087331", "url": "https://genius.com/10087331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Pull up in a Rover, then I pulled off on a Fisker", "vault_lines": ["Pull up in a Rover, then I pulled off on a Fisker"], "meaning": "21 names two luxurious cars here, a Range Rover as well as a Fisker Karma. A Fisker Karma is a range-extended electric vehicle luxury sports sedan that was produced by Fisker Automotive between 2011 and 2012. And a Rover is a full-sized four-wheel drive SUV produced by Land Rover. Although a Fisker is definitely a popular car for rappers to boast about, the Range Rover is one of the most iconic hip-hop vehicles of all time, with numerous rappers using them as a way of showcasing their lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "10083448", "url": "https://genius.com/10083448", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Wasn’t no food but rice", "vault_lines": ["Wasn't no food but rice"], "meaning": "Rice is a staple food, meaning that it is eaten routinely and makes up a large part of the diet of many people around the world. As such, rice is a very common and cheap food to come across, especially in Asia.\n\nBack in the day Yachty was struggling – he had to rely on very basic foods in order to avoid going hungry.", "annotation_id": "10081283", "url": "https://genius.com/10081283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "[Verse 1: Denzel Curry]", "vault_lines": ["Rest in power, it's all about power"], "meaning": "This verse was taken from the 2012 song, “Power” by Denzel Curry and Mike Dece.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bETTRdy6KUg", "annotation_id": "10081179", "url": "https://genius.com/10081179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "I sent my bitch to the store ’cause we ran out of soda (What?) Bitch, I’m tryna cook this yola (21)", "vault_lines": ["I sent my bitch to the store 'cause we ran out of soda (What?)"], "meaning": "“Yola” is slang for crack cocaine, and baking soda is a critical ingredient when creating crack cocaine, as crack cocaine is made by mixing water, cocaine, and baking soda, then boiling it.\n\n\n\nHe’s too busy to get some himself so he needs to send his girl over to go get some more, otherwise, he won’t be able to make it.", "annotation_id": "10052860", "url": "https://genius.com/10052860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 178, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Ayy, wait, 21, Lil Boat, yeah (Win) Denzel Curry cut your throat, yeah (Yeah) Kodak do the most, yeah (Win)", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, wait, 21, Lil Boat, yeah (Win)"], "meaning": "Uzi gives a shoutout to the rest of the freshmen in the cypher.\n\n\n\nLil Uzi may also be referencing Denzel Curry’s viral hit “Ultimate” from his double-EP 32 Zel / Planet Shrooms. On the first verse of “Ultimate” Curry raps, “Stop this shit, chop your esophagus”, Lil Uzi references this by saying “Denzel Curry cut your throat.”", "annotation_id": "10052650", "url": "https://genius.com/10052650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 243, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "That boy not gang, no, that boy not my friend I hang with my gang, the same gang that felt all of my pain When I was strugglin’ through the rain When I had no guap with no ice", "vault_lines": ["That boy not gang, no, that boy not my friend"], "meaning": "Yachty keeps his circle small and only affiliates with the people who have been with him since day one. He’s loyal to his gang and will never switch up.\n\nNever switch up\nNever switch up on gang, no", "annotation_id": "10052330", "url": "https://genius.com/10052330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 99, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Then I pulled up in a motherfuckin’ Brink’s truck (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Then I pulled up in a motherfuckin' Brink's truck (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "The Brink’s Company is a security and protection company. The company’s vans, which are used to transport goods – generally large quantities of money – are armored and heavily protected.", "annotation_id": "10051706", "url": "https://genius.com/10051706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "I’m ’bout it, chains on my neck cost me twenty Look at your diamonds Your diamonds look cloudy, they fake", "vault_lines": ["I'm 'bout my fetty"], "meaning": "While your jewelry is fake, Yachty spends tens of thousands on his chains to ensure he get the real thing and to show off that he is getting money.\n\nCheck out my diamonds they polar, my wrist getting colder, my neck lookin frozen", "annotation_id": "10051662", "url": "https://genius.com/10051662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Who the fuck picked this lil’ sorry ass beat?", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck picked this lil' sorry ass beat?"], "meaning": "Kodak begins his verse by surprising everyone and calling out the beat used for the entire cypher. Apparently he wasn’t feeling the beat, even though all of his companions had just gone in on it.\n\nDJ Drama did not create the beat, as many people assumed. The beat was created by the producer SikWidIT.\n\nKodak wasn’t the first person to express his displeasure with XXL’s beat selection, Anderson .Paak also tweeted “I hated that beat.”", "annotation_id": "10051286", "url": "https://genius.com/10051286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 456, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Sailing Team armored, we ready", "vault_lines": ["Sailing Team armored, we ready"], "meaning": "Lil Yachty’s whole boat-themed persona is just a part of something much bigger—The Sailing Team squad. According to a video Boat posted to Instagram which has been since deleted, he claimed the squad would be releasing a compilation mixtape titled “Meet the Sailing Team”.", "annotation_id": "10051254", "url": "https://genius.com/10051254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Planet shrooms, planet shrooms,", "vault_lines": ["Planet shrooms, planet shrooms,"], "meaning": "Denzel Curry released a double EP in 2015 titled 32 Zel/Planet Shrooms, the latter being half of the album.", "annotation_id": "10051249", "url": "https://genius.com/10051249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "All of these bitches they want me but they get one night", "vault_lines": ["All of these bitches they want me but they get one night"], "meaning": "Lil Boat is saying that he is wanted by girls but he only wants to stay with them for one night. This is a reference to his most popular song, “1Night”.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=251cxou3yR4", "annotation_id": "10051241", "url": "https://genius.com/10051241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Yeah, bop on that bitch like Kodak", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, bop on that bitch like Kodak"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi shouts out fellow XXL Freshman Kodak Black’s infamous dance, the Kodak Bop.", "annotation_id": "10051238", "url": "https://genius.com/10051238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 251, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshmen 2016 Cypher - Part 2", "line": "Rest in power, it’s all about power", "vault_lines": ["Rest in power, it's all about power"], "meaning": "Denzel Curry is all about power. Denzel’s signature ad-lib is ULT which is short for ultimate, but it is also an acronym. He believes everyone should be able to reach their full potential and be ultimate.\nhttps://twitter.com/RavenxMiyagi/status/747473105883439104", "annotation_id": "10051236", "url": "https://genius.com/10051236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
