{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshman Freestyle: Lil Uzi Vert", "line": "Forty shots for Lil Uzi, boy, I don’t believe that Huh, come into your hood, boy, yeah that’s where we at", "vault_lines": ["Forty shots for Lil Uzi, boy, I don't believe that"], "meaning": "Response to Reese’s diss song 180 Secs.\n\nThirty rounds for them dirty niggas\nThis that ‘'fuck ya momma’‘ have your brother missing\n\n\n\nUzi is mocking him and saying nothing will happen even if he comes to his hood, meaning he doesn’t believe Reese is really about that action.", "annotation_id": "10014639", "url": "https://genius.com/10014639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XXL Freshman Freestyle: Lil Uzi Vert", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-xxl-freshman-freestyle-lil-uzi-vert-lyrics", "genius_title": "XXL Freshman Freestyle: Lil Uzi Vert", "genius_id": 2715068, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Rain on ’em, thunderstorm, rain on ’em (Ooh, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "“Thunderstorm” is a mostly aggressive form of the “rain” (basically a storm,a basic one), according to the central theme of the song,and the high rage of the 2nd verse,it probably means that he’s soooo fed up of “them”", "annotation_id": "37726148", "url": "https://genius.com/37726148", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "She say, “You’re the worst, you’re the worst”", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi had some history with his ex,  Brittany Renne, and she kept on being toxic to Uzi for having girls in his music videos and shi.", "annotation_id": "37357263", "url": "https://genius.com/37357263", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Medicine, lil’ nigga, take some", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi often refers to drugs as medicine, especially in the context of coping with emotional pain. It also fits in the emo-rap vibe of this song, as in emo-rap drugs are potrayed as a way to deal with depression, anxiety or heartbreak", "annotation_id": "35208720", "url": "https://genius.com/35208720", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "In the club, ain’t got no ones, then we would beg them (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi talks about his past, explaining how he didn’t have ones to throw in the clubs and would beg strippers to perform acts.\n\nThrowing ones (one dollar bills) are a common act performed in a strip club by many people. It’s kind of like a new “wave” the people have caught on to. Another artist close to Uzi, NAV, also talks about throwing ones on his song “NAVUZIMETRO#PT2” which coincidentally features Uzi. NAV explains,\n\nThrew so much ones on that bitch I gave her paper cuts and a rash, yeah\n\nThis verse leads to the next verse on which he talks about this present life, having plenty of money.", "annotation_id": "12641980", "url": "https://genius.com/12641980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "That is not your swag, I swear you fake hard", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi is accusing other rap artists that steal his style in music and fashion as a result of his recent mainstream popularity. He talks about this on “Two®”, the opening track to Luv Is Rage 2.\n\n‘Cause you know I’m the one\nYes, I’m the one that really started all this\nAnd you know I changed a lot of you niggas\nIn a matter of months, I raised a lot of you niggas\n\nAnother source where Uzi would rap about this subject is in his collaboration with popular Atlanta rap group, Migos, “Bad and Boujee”.\n\nAyy, wait, these niggas watchin'\nI swear to God they be my clones", "annotation_id": "12641933", "url": "https://genius.com/12641933", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Countin’ them bands all way to the top ‘til they be fallin’ over (Yeah, yeah, yeah) Countin’ them bands on my way to the top ‘til it’s fallin’ over", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "One “band” is a thousand dollars. Uzi is “stacking” their money, which means “saving.” They hinted on their song “444+222” that their net worth was $4 million.", "annotation_id": "12534194", "url": "https://genius.com/12534194", "state": "accepted", "votes": 149, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Everybody got the same swag now Watch the way that I tear it down", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi claims that nowadays, everyone is trying to emulate him and dress and act how he does.  In his XXL 2016 Freshman Class Interview, in regards to the new-school form of rapping that he personifies, Uzi explains:\n\nEverybody wanna be in your lane.  They know you ain’t nothing but a clone.", "annotation_id": "11591442", "url": "https://genius.com/11591442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 152, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "My bracelet Hermès, her bracelet Hermès now", "vault_lines": ["My bracelet Hermès, her bracelet Hermès now"], "meaning": "Although Uzi and Brittany were in love in the past, their love is fading now and they are arguing and having relationship issues: Brittany may be threatening to commit suicide, while Uzi is struggling with substance abuse.\n\n\n\nNote: Uzi and Brittany broke up in June of 2016, so it is assumed that this song is describing the end of their relationship and shows an argument that took place in the past.", "annotation_id": "11555749", "url": "https://genius.com/11555749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 285, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Now these niggas wanna take my cadence (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "A “cadence” is a rhythm that rappers use to flow on a beat.\n\nUzi used a cadence on his 2015 song “Super Saiyan Trunks” that has become popular amongst other artists.", "annotation_id": "11521632", "url": "https://genius.com/11521632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 232, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Fast car, NASCAR, race on ’em", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "NASCAR stands for National Association for Stock Car Auto Racing.  It’s a sport where top athletes race vehicles for hundreds of miles in a closed loop circuit.\n\n\n\nUzi mentions racing and coincidentally has a new song called, “Go Off,” featured in the film, The Fate of The Furious.", "annotation_id": "11514515", "url": "https://genius.com/11514515", "state": "accepted", "votes": 113, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "I cannot die because this my universe", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi is known to be very philosophical. He has expressed on Twitter that the universe is a figment of his imagination and he considers himself “not from this Earth”:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/837481519534964737\n\nHe has also tweeted an image referencing solipsism, or the belief that only one’s own mind is sure to exist; the only thing we can known to be real if what we perceive with our own mind.", "annotation_id": "11506613", "url": "https://genius.com/11506613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 545, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "She say I’m insane, yeah, I might blow my brain out (Hey) Xanny, help the pain, yeah Please, Xanny, make it go away I’m committed, not addicted, but it keep control of me All the pain, now I can’t feel it, I swear that it’s slowin’ me, yeah", "vault_lines": ["She say I'm insane, yeah, I might blow my brain out (Hey)"], "meaning": "Xanax or Xanny is a prescription benzodiazepine that treats anxiety and panic disorders. It’s often abused as a relaxant and stress reliever.\n\nIn a 2016 interview with Sway, Uzi said that he’s trying to slow down or stop using Xanax:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4QYfD43mJSU?t=19m53s\n\nIn November 2017, rapper Lil Peep died of a Xanax-related drug overdose, which prompted Uzi to go on Twitter and re-iterate that he was trying to kick his habit. He struggled with anger issues while trying to quit.", "annotation_id": "11447688", "url": "https://genius.com/11447688", "state": "accepted", "votes": 470, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Are you alright? I’m alright, I’m quite alright And my money’s right", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "These are questions Uzi and Brittany ask each other after their argument, outlined throughout this song, is over.\n\nIn a similar fashion, Uzi assures Brittany and their listeners that they’re doing good since they have a lot of money.", "annotation_id": "11447601", "url": "https://genius.com/11447601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 510, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Clothes from overseas Got the racks and they all C-Notes, you is not a G though Lookin’ at you stackin’ all your money, it all green though I was countin’ that and these all twenties, that’s a G-roll", "vault_lines": ["Got the racks and they all C-Notes, you is not a G though"], "meaning": "C-note is a slang term for an American $100 bill. The “C” in C-note refers to the Roman numeral for 100, which was printed on $100 bills, and it can also refer to century.\n\nA “G-roll” refers to a wad of cash mostly formed of smaller bills.\n\nAs he has said on past songs, like “Right Now” or “$ub Zero”, Uzi has a preference for blue notes, the new $100 bills that feature a prominent blue ribbon as a security feature.", "annotation_id": "11447471", "url": "https://genius.com/11447471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 210, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Every time that you leave your spot Your girlfriend call me like, “Come on over” I like the way that she treat me, gon’ leave you, won’t leave me, I call it that Casanova", "vault_lines": ["I like the way that she treat me, gon' leave you, won't leave me, I call it that Casanova"], "meaning": "This may call back to one of Uzi’s older songs “Ps & Qs,” which was featured on his Lil Uzi vs. The World mixtape, where he talks about stealing his former girlfriend Brittany Byrd from another guy.\n\nGiacomo Girolamo Casanova lived during the 18th Century. He was an Italian adventurer and author. His last name is synonymous with “ladies man” due to his ability to seduce women. Many women also took advantage of Casanova’s benevolent and sensual nature, using him for their personal benefit.", "annotation_id": "11428801", "url": "https://genius.com/11428801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 256, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "She said, “Baby, I am not afraid to die” Push me to the edge All my friends are dead, push me to the edge All my friends are dead, push me to the edge All my friends are dead, push me to the edge", "vault_lines": ["Push me to the edge, yeah, all my friends are dead"], "meaning": "His girlfriend isn’t afraid to kill herself if he dumps her or she isn’t afraid of his threats.\n\n“Push me to the edge,” is an idiom that expresses extreme frustration. He could also be urging and daring her to keep doing it.\n\nIn an exclusive Genius interview, the producer of the track, TM88, confirmed that “All my friends are dead,” is referring to dead presidents, which is slang for money:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/lH5ROxbKig4?t=5m54s\n\nUzi raps about his friends that were killed in his hometown of north Philly in songs like “YSL” and “LUV SCARS K.o 1600.” He often claims to have no friends, due to his fame and fortune.\n\nUzi may have drawn inspiration from punk rock band, Turbonegro’s 2005 track, “All My Friends Are Dead.”\n\nOn December the 17th, Pitchfork named these lines one of the fifteen year-defining lyrics of 2017.", "annotation_id": "11419951", "url": "https://genius.com/11419951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1273, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "I don’t really care if you cry On the real, you should’ve never lied Should’ve saw the way she looked me in my eyes", "vault_lines": ["Should've saw the way she looked me in my eyes"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Uzi and Brittany Byrd’s 2016 breakup. Rumors started surfacing that Byrd had cheated on Lil' Uzi, which he quickly denied:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/746871874370560000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\n\nHowever, he did confirm the breakup:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/746739042818101249?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\n\nTheir relationship seems to still be on good terms, as he frequently brings her on stage and references her on his tracks.", "annotation_id": "11418845", "url": "https://genius.com/11418845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 807, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "(8) Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "This is the tag of TM88 of 808 Mafia, which samples the stuttering “8” from the “808 Mafia” tag to sound like “88.” 808 Mafia is a group of producers which includes TM88, the producer of this song, as well as Southside, Tarentino and other trap producers.\n\nTM88 explained the production behind this song in a June 2017 Deconstructed interview with Genius.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lH5ROxbKig4", "annotation_id": "11417869", "url": "https://genius.com/11417869", "state": "accepted", "votes": 330, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "line": "Phantom that’s all red, inside all white Like somethin’ you ride a sled down, I just want that head", "vault_lines": ["Countin' them bands all way to the top 'til they be fallin' over (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "A Phantom Rolls Royce is an expensive luxury vehicle with a starting price of $417,825. This particular 2016 Rolls Royce Dawn, owned by Gucci Mane, is worth $500,000.", "annotation_id": "11417374", "url": "https://genius.com/11417374", "state": "accepted", "votes": 280, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "XO Tour Llif3", "status": "done", "targets": 19, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-xo-tour-llif3-lyrics", "genius_title": "XO Tour Llif3", "genius_id": 3003630, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X0 T0UR LIif 3.", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-x0-t0ur-liif-3-lyrics", "genius_title": "X0 T0UR LIif 3.", "genius_id": 10298736, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "If you got hurt, yeah, I got hurt, yeah, I got bruised too (Yeah) That’s the main reason why I had to choose you", "vault_lines": ["If you got hurt, yeah, I got hurt, yeah, I got bruised too (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi says the shared pain he and another person feel is why he chose them. Their similar experiences and emotional wounds created a connection between them.", "annotation_id": "40748692", "url": "https://genius.com/40748692", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "VLONE", "vault_lines": ["Didn't care too, I was all alone ('Lone, VLONE"], "meaning": "Vlone is a prominent streetwear fashion brand based on the mantra “Live Alone, Die Alone. Mainly founded by Jabari Shelton (known as A$AP Bari)", "annotation_id": "38884017", "url": "https://genius.com/38884017", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "She got ass just like a zebra on a zoo too", "vault_lines": ["She got ass just like a zebra on a zoo too"], "meaning": "She has stretch marks on her ass that make it look striped like a zebra. Stretch marks are a sign that someone has gained weight, implying the woman either got fit in the gym or just got a big ass", "annotation_id": "37602563", "url": "https://genius.com/37602563", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "Grandma don’t like diamonds, she say “Make sure that my rent’s paid,” yeah", "vault_lines": ["Grandma don't like diamonds, she say \"Make sure that my rent's paid,\" yeah"], "meaning": "uzi states how him grandmother doesn’t want diamonds as a gift but instead just for her rent to be paid", "annotation_id": "34019080", "url": "https://genius.com/34019080", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "If you got options I got options, baby, who you?", "vault_lines": ["If you got options I got options, baby, who you?"], "meaning": "“if you got options I got options” Uzi says, he can get a girl, if you get a boy. He has another girls than you he could go too, if u cheat or pick someone else", "annotation_id": "24733878", "url": "https://genius.com/24733878", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "(Metro)", "vault_lines": ["Take off in a jet (I don't want my ex)"], "meaning": "This is one of producer Metro Boomin’s many producer tags. This particular one is said by Young Thug and was first introduced in his 2015 song “Hercules”.", "annotation_id": "12793000", "url": "https://genius.com/12793000", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "Bitch, you know I’m flooded, then you know my momma wrist straight (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you know I'm flooded, then you know my momma wrist straight (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Artists often use water related phrases as to brag about their possession of highly expensive jewelry or “ice”. In his track “Malfunction” on his new album he claims to have “more diamonds than your jeweler.”\n\nFurthermore, Uzi’s mom supplies him with ample support and love so you know he returns the favor and showers her in gifts. In his new song “Dark Queen” Uzi says “Momma love me so I can do no wrong”, thus demonstrating that she loves Uzi unconditionally.", "annotation_id": "12632246", "url": "https://genius.com/12632246", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "(Yo, yo, Pi’erre, you wanna come out here?)", "vault_lines": ["Take off in a jet (I don't want my ex)"], "meaning": "This is the tag of producer Pi'erre Bourne, who made the beat with Metro Boomin and Maaly Raw.\n\nThe tag first came to prominence on the song “Magnolia” by Playboi Carti, and was originally a sample spoken by Jamie Foxx on an episode of  The Jamie Foxx Show. In this song, though, the tag is said through the voice of Young Nudy, an up and coming rapper from Atlanta, Georgia, who is a frequent collaborator with Pi'erre Bourne.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/MCG5_AtRp24?t=49", "annotation_id": "12595724", "url": "https://genius.com/12595724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "I cannot believe that I made this shit from a mixtape (Tape, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I cannot believe that I made this shit from a mixtape (Tape, yeah)"], "meaning": "It was the first installment of the Luv Is Rage series that truly set Uzi’s career in motion. It featured hits such as “Top,” “7AM,” and “All My Chains.”\n\nHe also released the mixtapes, Lil Uzi Vert vs. The World and The Perfect LUV Tape, before the eventual release of his proper debut studio album.", "annotation_id": "12590281", "url": "https://genius.com/12590281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "Leonardo DiCaprio (Yeah, swag) Watch out, boys, I might bag your ho (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Leonardo DiCaprio (Yeah, swag)"], "meaning": "In the 1997 film Titanic, Leonardo DiCaprio’s character, Jack Dawson, steals a woman from her rich fiancé.\n\n\n\nInterestingly, Uzi blazed a spliff during Celine Dion’s performance of the Titanic theme song at the 2017 Billboard Music Awards.", "annotation_id": "12585887", "url": "https://genius.com/12585887", "state": "accepted", "votes": 134, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "I got one that’s on my line that look like new new", "vault_lines": ["I got one that's on my line that look like new new"], "meaning": "Uzi’s texting a new girl that looks like Lauren London, an American actor known for her role as Erin “New New” Garnett in the 2006 film ATL.", "annotation_id": "12585288", "url": "https://genius.com/12585288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "Walkin’ with a check (With a check) Take off in a jet (I don’t want my ex) So I just never stress", "vault_lines": ["Take off in a jet (I don't want my ex)"], "meaning": "Uzi further clarifies why he doesn’t need his ex-girlfriend. He already has another girl on his arm and he’s taking off with her in a jet. He’s got all the fame and money he could want. Why would he need to stress about her or anything when he’s living this kind of life?\n\nThis could also be a reference to Uzi’s track “SideLine Watching”, on which he discusses flexing his money to diss Brittany.\n\nLet me count these checks (what?)\nFlex on my ex (yeah)\n\nThis line is a bit of a contrast from really the rest of the album. We hear in several other tracks, including “XO Tour Llif3” and “The Way Life Goes”, about his loneliness and sorrows. But in this line, Uzi seems to have come about his senses and realizes he’s going to be just fine.", "annotation_id": "12584187", "url": "https://genius.com/12584187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "I don’t know what’s next, yeah I don’t want my ex, no Break up with a text", "vault_lines": ["Take off in a jet (I don't want my ex)"], "meaning": "These lines are in reference to Uzi’s long-term girlfriend Brittany Byrd. They were on and off again multiple times between 2014-2016, and she heavily influenced his life and music. Brittany is mentioned in a decent amount of Uzi’s songs, with his hit XO TOUR Llif3 dedicated to their breakup.\n\n\n\nUzi doesn’t know what’s next in his love life but he knows he doesn’t want Brittany anymore. While their breakup was difficult, Brittany and Uzi seem to still be friends. Brittany endorsed Luv is Rage 2 on her Instagram. It was posted on August 24th, 2017, the day Uzi announced he was dropping the album, with the caption “Luv, I suppose. 2🦇🥀”\n\nHe also used the line “Break up in a text” in “SideLine Watching”.\n\nI don’t got no respect (I don’t, I don’t)\nBreak up in a text (what?)\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/746739042818101249", "annotation_id": "12583236", "url": "https://genius.com/12583236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "line": "Yeah, my life’s a mess (Pew, pew, pew) But I’m also blessed (Blessed)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my life's a mess (Pew, pew, pew)"], "meaning": "At the time of release, Uzi had been very open about his struggles with loneliness and drug addiction. We see these themes throughout the entire album, and on the album’s lead single XO TOUR Llif3 it is especially prevalent.\n\nThrough the struggles however, he recognizes that his success is a blessing.", "annotation_id": "12580925", "url": "https://genius.com/12580925", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "X", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-x-lyrics", "genius_title": "X", "genius_id": 3209337, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wrong Way", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-wrong-way-lyrics", "genius_title": "Wrong Way", "genius_id": 11870518, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wrong", "line": "OOH!!", "vault_lines": ["But she don't give a shit, nah, she just want this OOH!!"], "meaning": "In the music video, this “OOH!!” is accompanied by a wolf-like gesture from MAX, like he is throwing his head back to howl. This also ties into the stalker/hunter idea in the annotation for “It’s better when it feels wrong”.", "annotation_id": "21665219", "url": "https://genius.com/21665219", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wrong", "line": "It’s better when it feels wrong", "vault_lines": ["It's better when it feels wrong"], "meaning": "MAX (or the person he is representing in the song) is saying that though they know that public/near-public sex is risky or unacceptable, they find that it increases their pleasure.\nIn the music video as well, MAX is portrayed as a dangerous and mysterious man who seems very interested in the blond woman. However, we never see the woman’s face, and when we do see her body, it is like we are looking at her from MAX/the man’s point of view.\nThis reminds me of Maroon 5’s “Animals” music video in some ways because they both seem to portray the men in them as obsessive. The “Animals” music video is a lot more explicit about the relationship it is describing but there are several common themes in the two music videos.\nThis leads to another interpretation of the line: The woman doesn’t want MAX/the man and MAX/the man is aware of this so he is stalking her. However, he enjoys the hunt too much to stop stalking her. He is saying “I know what I’m doing is wrong but it turns me on more than anything”.\nThe second interpretation of this line gives the song a more sinister feel. It begins to sound like the rest of the song is the stalker going mad and managing to convince himself that the woman he is following truly wants him.", "annotation_id": "21665085", "url": "https://genius.com/21665085", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wrong", "line": "She says “Pull over and don’t lock the doors” She doesn’t care who sees anymore", "vault_lines": ["She doesn't care who sees anymore"], "meaning": "The woman in the song has gotten so desperate for sex that she asks the person driving the car to pull over and have sex with her in the car. Also, she asks that the door not be locked, making her seem a to be a bit of an exhibitionist.", "annotation_id": "21665065", "url": "https://genius.com/21665065", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wrong", "line": "Making that “Damn it feels so good” face", "vault_lines": ["Making that \"Damn it feels so good\" face"], "meaning": "He is describing the females face during sex.", "annotation_id": "15860639", "url": "https://genius.com/15860639", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
