{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "I might hit up Tuddie", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Uzi says he might hit up one of his ex-girlfriends, Tuddie.", "annotation_id": "32043116", "url": "https://genius.com/32043116", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "My chain so tight like a noose (My chain tight, tight, tight, tight)", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Uzis chains have alot with them and how he wears them. This is saying, Lil Uzi would wear a type of a tight chain called a choker around his neck.", "annotation_id": "27324107", "url": "https://genius.com/27324107", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "Ayy, get the money, snooze you lose", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Uzi often cites those who hate due to jealousy in his music. In this line, he’s criticizing those who hate him for his music while at the same time not doing anything about it. Instead of going out there and trying to make money on their own, they “snooze” or sleep.\n\nUzi later describes a similar theme of ignoring his haters on the track “Erase Your Social”, where he raps:\n\nLike, flex on you haters, huh, hi haters (yeah)\nThis is my world so it’s all in my favor", "annotation_id": "16825672", "url": "https://genius.com/16825672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "By the way, who’re you waitin’ for anyway? I’m waitin’ for Dolemite For who? Dolemite, motherfucker, you heard her", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "The movie quote and excerpt from Dolemite, a 1975 feature film action-comedy produced by, written by, and starring Rudy Ray Moore.\n\n\n\nRudy Ray Moore is well-versed in music as well having been considered the “Godfather of Rap”. He has released numerous albums that have reached genres from Comedy, R&B/Soul, to even Rock and Hip-Hop/Rap, often incorporating the Dolemite character and themes.\n\nThis sample has also been used and seemingly created by a low-lying youtube channel by the name of swagmeoutable back in 2011, 4 years before the release of Lil Uzi Vert’s album, Luv Is Rage.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DzjoWikiAVw", "annotation_id": "13090047", "url": "https://genius.com/13090047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "Spent a hundred on my jewels (Spent a hundred on my) Feel like Santana with my Jewels (Woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert references Juelz Santana, a rapper from Harlem, New York, that was popular in the early 2000’s. Juelz Santana was part of a east coast rap group called The Diplomats (Dipset) with rappers Cam'ron and Jim Jones.\n\nA little word play here from Lil Uzi Vert, as ‘Juelz’ sounds like ‘Jewels’.", "annotation_id": "9040367", "url": "https://genius.com/9040367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "Oh, getting money like a Jew", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Playing off of the stereotype that Jewish people are stingy and will pick up pennies off the ground, Uzi is saving up his cash. But unlike the stereotypical Jew, Uzi is actually spending his money!", "annotation_id": "8322697", "url": "https://genius.com/8322697", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "Ayy, counting these bills, they be blue (Countin’ these hundreds, these hundreds)", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, counting these bills, they be blue (Countin' these hundreds, these hundreds)"], "meaning": "Since October 2013, the U.S. Mint has been printing and issuing redesigned 100 dollar bills, with a blue 3D security strip to Franklin’s right, and a blueish tint to the bill.\n\nIt has become commonplace for artists to refer to the bills as ‘blue faces’ or some play on the words now that the money has a distinguishing quality.", "annotation_id": "8270465", "url": "https://genius.com/8270465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "I might get high off of codeine (Codeine)", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Codeine is a narcotic pain reliever that is often combined with Promethazine in cough medicine. Cough syrup medicine is used to make of Uzi’s favorite drink, lean, he just mentions Codeine the main ingredient.\n\nI’m just working off the lean now I’m swervin'", "annotation_id": "8222925", "url": "https://genius.com/8222925", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "Ayy, lil’ bitch, I pity the fool (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Mr. T is a character in the 1980’s TV Show called “The A-Team”\n\nI Pity The Fool\n\nWas a Phrase Mr.T was commonly saying all the time back then and still till this day sometime has rants about it .", "annotation_id": "8105247", "url": "https://genius.com/8105247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wit My Crew X 1987", "line": "She kinda look like, um, YesJulz (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["By the way, who're you waitin' for anyway?"], "meaning": "Julz is a popular party organizer (director of Vibes) & blogger (@YesJulz) with a banging body. Lil Uzi compares his girl’s body to Julz’s in this line.", "annotation_id": "8095959", "url": "https://genius.com/8095959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
