{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Who you think you ahead of? Not us", "vault_lines": ["Who you think you ahead of? Not us"], "meaning": "U not ahead G HERBO", "annotation_id": "33110503", "url": "https://genius.com/33110503", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "This shit’s got the most views out of everything I’ve ever put up on my shit That little clip, that shit got a million views I ain’t never got no views on some shit out", "vault_lines": ["I ain't even on that, period (period)"], "meaning": "‘Brendon Madeit’ uploaded a clip from K104FM in which Herbo was freestyling over Three 6 Mafia’s “Who Run It”, and the video got a million views. At the time, this was the most views that he has ever gotten.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5h8bCCHRBko", "annotation_id": "15897825", "url": "https://genius.com/15897825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "I put the VV’s everywhere (everywhere)", "vault_lines": ["I put the VV's everywhere (everywhere)"], "meaning": "“VV” refers to Very Very Slightly Included (VVS1 and VVS2) diamonds. VVS diamonds are high on the GIA diamond clarity grading scale, and are only bested by Flawless (FL) and Internally Flawless (IF) diamonds. Herbo is no stranger to spending money on expensive jewelry, as evidenced by his 150 Dream Team pendant which is laced with 50 VVS diamonds.", "annotation_id": "14343361", "url": "https://genius.com/14343361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Lovin’ my city like Chano, I swear", "vault_lines": ["Lovin' my city like Chano, I swear"], "meaning": "“Chano” is the nickname for popular Chicago rapper, Chance the Rapper. He has been known to represent his city constantly such as in his 2015 single, “Angels”:\n\nI got my city doing front flips\nWhen every father, mayor, rapper jump ship\nI guess that’s why they call it where I stay\n\nHerbo is also a Chicago native and takes pride in his city similar to Chance in his lyrics. Additionally, they both have developed a strong artistic relationship, having collaborated on tracks such as “Everything (Remix)” which also features Lil Uzi Vert.", "annotation_id": "14328658", "url": "https://genius.com/14328658", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Boy you trippin’, SI diamonds on your neck", "vault_lines": ["Boy you trippin', SI diamonds on your neck"], "meaning": "Diamond quality is determined through close examination as seen in microscopes, and sometimes through the naked eye if it’s extremely imperfect. In this line, it can be inferred that Uzi on the other hand apparently wears diamonds of VVS quality on the clarity scale, which is higher in quality than SI diamonds.\n\nOn “Left, Right”, Uzi boasted in a similar fashion:\n\nVVS all in my ring", "annotation_id": "14316618", "url": "https://genius.com/14316618", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Rich, mad ‘cause your bitch ate my kids or somethin’", "vault_lines": ["Rich, mad 'cause your bitch ate my kids or somethin'"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert directly calls out Rich, Rich The Kid, in response to Rich The Kid’s diss track “Dead Friends”.\n\nRich The Kid, an artist who had his debut studio-album, The World Is Yours, release on March 30, 2018, two weeks before the release of this remix. On Rich The Kid’s album, the outro track, “Dead Friends”, calls out and disses Uzi.\n\nThis feud began from a series of tweets between Rich The Kid and Lil Uzi Vert that began from Uzi’s tweet about his regrets to signing to DJ Drama and Don Cannon.", "annotation_id": "14310832", "url": "https://genius.com/14310832", "state": "pending", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Me no broke, Akademiks, yeah, that’s where you get your news at", "vault_lines": ["Me no broke, Akademiks, yeah, that's where you get your news at"], "meaning": "DJ Akademiks is a YouTube personality who shares his opinions on events in the hip-hop community. He is also a co-host of Everyday Struggle, a show on the hip-hop based media outlet, Complex.\n\nLil Uzi Vert has previously had some beef with DJ Akademiks when Uzi accused Ak of spreading Uzi’s lyrics off of an unreleased album and hittin' up Uzi’s manager for news.\n\nHere, Uzi states that Rich The Kid, previous collaborator with Uzi, a rapper and the CEO of Rich Forever, follows Akademiks for news, a negative spotlight to be put on because of the rumors and drama Akademiks often covers.", "annotation_id": "14310665", "url": "https://genius.com/14310665", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "I take out my hair and I stand on my money, your bitch think I’m Julius Erving", "vault_lines": ["I take out my hair and I stand on my money, your bitch think I'm Julius Erving"], "meaning": "Julius Erving is a former NBA athlete that played with the Philadelphia 76ers, Uzi’s home team for 11 years. He was best known for his iconic afro and “alley-oops”.\n\nTo prove a point on how much money he has, Uzi claims he’ll stand on his cash, raising his stature from 5'4\" to that of Julius Erving, 6'7\".", "annotation_id": "14307159", "url": "https://genius.com/14307159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "Ask your bros, Grammy-nominated songs just to prove that, uh", "vault_lines": ["Ask your bros, Grammy-nominated songs just to prove that, uh"], "meaning": "Uzi continues to diss Rich the Kid telling him that his “bros,” the Migos, long-time friends of Rich and labelmates at one point, know what success is like, referring to the quadruple platinum by Migos featuring Lil Uzi Vert “Bad and Boujee”.\n\nThe track was nominated for “Best Rap Performance” at the 60th Annual Grammy Awards (2017).\n\nAdditionally, Lil Uzi Vert was nominated for “Best New Artist” the same year “Bad and Boujee” was nominated, poking Rich The Kid’s success and his inadequate title for a Grammy.", "annotation_id": "14306936", "url": "https://genius.com/14306936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Who Run It (Remix)", "line": "You know that my Rollie got XO diamonds in it, so that’s that Perfect Timing", "vault_lines": ["You know that my Rollie got XO diamonds in it, so that's that Perfect Timing"], "meaning": "This is a reference to NAV’s album with Metro Boomin, Perfect Timing in which Uzi features on two of the album’s songs: “A$AP Ferg” and “NAVUZIMETRO#PT2”. He also shouts out a label that NAV is currently signed to, XO. Although Uzi isn’t a part of XO, he associates with the label’s founder, The Weeknd and has dedicated his hit song, “XO Tour Llif3”, towards them.\n\nUzi uses wordplay between both references by claiming that his Rolex luxury has “XO diamonds” on it, as if it is the figure of speech, “perfect timing.”", "annotation_id": "14306703", "url": "https://genius.com/14306703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
