{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "You get a purse from me Eighty thousand dollars for her Birkin", "vault_lines": ["You get a purse from me"], "meaning": "Young Thug details buying expensive handbags for his partner, specifically, a Birkin bag. Made by the designer brand Hermès, the accessory has no problem charging $80,000 per bag. The most expensive Birken ever sold was the Matte Himalaya Niloticus crocodile diamond purse, which sold at auction for $206,111 in late 2018.\n\n\n\nThug has rapped similar lines before, like on the thirty minute leak “Thug N 30”:\n\nI wanna buy them purses, yeah (Purses)\nYou make me mad, I’m gettin' the Birkin, yeah (Yeah, ayy)", "annotation_id": "18389725", "url": "https://genius.com/18389725", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "Made it from the soil, made it from the Rex", "vault_lines": ["Made it from the soil, made it from the Rex"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert grew up in North Pennsylvania where he didn’t have much to start off with, but after being inspired by artists like Marilyn Manson, Kanye West, Young Thug, and more, Uzi decided to start his own music career. In 2015 and 2016, his career took off after he released hit singles like “Top”, “Money Longer”, and “You Was Right”, and now he’s one of the most wealthy and influential rappers in the game.\n\n\n\nThe Rex is short for Rexdale, a district in Toronto known for its high crime rates and gang violence. Uzi says he “made it from the Rex” to signify his come up from the streets. Additionally, fellow rapper NAV grew up in the Rex. NAV and Uzi are pretty good friends and are often seen with each other; one such occasion, specifically in Toronto, is the filming of the music video for NAV’s 2017 track “Good For It”, with a cameo from Uzi as well as cameos from Drake, The Weeknd, Derek Wise, and more.", "annotation_id": "17839632", "url": "https://genius.com/17839632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "(BL$$D)", "vault_lines": ["I just let lil' mama suck me up, girl"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for BL$$D, a multi-platinum producer from Atlanta. The producer is most known for producing Ayo & Teo’s 2017 viral dance song “Rolex.”\n\nThe producer has previously worked with Young Thug on several songs. Popular pieces of their collaborative work include Thug’s 2017 songs “Relationship” and “Cruise Ship.”", "annotation_id": "17835140", "url": "https://genius.com/17835140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "My jeans is so tight they don’t fit", "vault_lines": ["My jeans is so tight they don't fit"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert reflects on his fashion sense, which include boasting tight jeans, apparently jeans too tight.\n\n\n\nLil Uzi Vert is deemed for his fashion ethic: the rapper regularly posts fit pics, showing off his incredible wardrobe. Visit this page to learn more about Uzi’s everyday outfits.\n\nInterestingly, Young Thug reflected on his impact on the tight jeans trend during a 2018 Instagram live:\n\nI’m the drip god. I created this shit. I made the way for young niggas to open up and be they self. I did this. I got crucified. They call me gay; they ain’t call y’all niggas gay. I made y’all tighten y’all jeans up. I’m the wave god. I’m the master. I’m the founder.", "annotation_id": "17828683", "url": "https://genius.com/17828683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "VVS diamonds right behind my lip Don’t walk with less than fifty on my wrist Diamonds so cold on my neck, it got me sick Raf Simons, mix it up with the Rick", "vault_lines": ["VVS diamonds right behind my lip"], "meaning": "Here Uzi is talking about the diamonds he had implanted in his teeth.\n\n\n\nUzi goes on to brag about all the luxury brands he can afford, and name drops fashion designers Raf Simons and Rick Owens. During his 2019 album cycle he frequently posted fit pics of him sporting various designer pieces.\n\n\n\nLil Uzi has mentioned these two brands at the same time in songs like “Nuyork Nights at 21,” “The Way Life Goes,” and the 2019 song “Sanguine Paradise,” in which he says:\n\nMy pants, Raf Simons\nMy shoes, Rick-Rick", "annotation_id": "17827421", "url": "https://genius.com/17827421", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What’s the Move", "line": "LUV, know I got swag", "vault_lines": ["LUV, know I got swag"], "meaning": "“LUV” is an acronym that stands for Lil Uzi Vert. The abbreviation is frequently utilized by Lil Uzi throughout his discography, as he incorporated the moniker into his album titles since his October 2015 mixtape Luv Is Rage.\n\nUzi is also famously into fashion and frequently sports designer brands. Hypebeast famously broke down his trendsetting fashion statement and the different exotic brands he wears.", "annotation_id": "17827134", "url": "https://genius.com/17827134", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
