{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Whatchu Was On", "line": "I counted so high, don’t know what’s under me", "vault_lines": ["I counted so high, don't know what's under me"], "meaning": "Majority of the songs chorus consists of overlapping two vocal takes over each other, each with different cadences, a creative choice by both Uzi and Kesha Lee.\n\nOn this particular line however Uzi says two different things, the first take stating:\n\nDon’t know what’s under me\n\nAnd the overlapped take stating:\n\nCan’t see what’s under me", "annotation_id": "38333601", "url": "https://genius.com/38333601", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Whatchu Was On", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-whatchu-was-on-lyrics", "genius_title": "Whatchu Was On", "genius_id": 9797135, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Want", "line": "These niggas, they funny like Chris Tucker (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["These niggas, they funny like Chris Tucker (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Chris Tucker is a comedian and actor famous for his performances in movies like Rush Hour and Friday. He’s known for his rapid-fire delivery and exaggerated humor, which made him a memorable figure in Hollywood comedies.\n\nUzi’s line is saying some people around him act like a joke like Chris Tucker in his movies. Tucker’s known for his high-energy, funny roles and Uzi is using that reference to make it clear he thinks these people are putting on a show or just being extra for no reason.", "annotation_id": "35435671", "url": "https://genius.com/35435671", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
