{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Mean", "line": "Shawty, you a dub and I’m too focused on the beans (Moolah)", "vault_lines": ["Shawty, you a dub and I'm too focused on the beans (Moolah)"], "meaning": "Uzi is too focused on drugs to care about girls.", "annotation_id": "32338000", "url": "https://genius.com/32338000", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Mean", "line": "I remember when she used to play me in my teens (Moolah)", "vault_lines": ["I remember when she used to play me in my teens (Moolah)"], "meaning": "Uzi often refers to how many girls used to play him before the fame, and now they’re all on his dick.", "annotation_id": "32337979", "url": "https://genius.com/32337979", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Mean", "line": "I can’t understand, I was too focused on the green", "vault_lines": ["I can't understand, I was too focused on the green"], "meaning": "Symere Woods, primary known as Lil Uzi Vert, cannot comprehend as he is too focused on the money (the green).", "annotation_id": "27539485", "url": "https://genius.com/27539485", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Mean", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-what-you-mean-lyrics", "genius_title": "What You Mean", "genius_id": 3559156, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Know", "line": "No, this not a rented, it say 200 the limit Bitch, I went 205, you get money, that’s a lie, uh", "vault_lines": ["No, this not a rented, it say 200 the limit"], "meaning": "Having an exotic vehicle is expensive no matter how you look at it, even renting one can set you back thousands of dollars a day.  Breaking 200MPH is pretty extraordinary, since as of summer 2018, only 26 currently available cars have a top speed of 200+ mph.\n\nThe line could also be a reference to his 2018 song “200 My Dash”:\n\n200 my dash (skrr)\nI hope I don’t crash (woah)\nI’m driving too fast (slow down, slow down)", "annotation_id": "14991159", "url": "https://genius.com/14991159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Know", "line": "Stay drippin’ this swag, VVS, that’s what I’m drippin’", "vault_lines": ["Stay drippin' this swag, VVS, that's what I'm drippin'"], "meaning": "VVS refers to the clarity of a diamond. There are many levels of clarity, but the diamonds with the lowest traces of carbon are the rarest, and therefore the most expensive. Uzi evidently likes to wear a lot of VVS diamonds which prove his notion of wealth and influence.\n\nSimilarly, to have drip means to wear a lot of “iced” out accessories, but due to the immense popularity one gains, they become “fire” and start “melting” the so called ice. Therefore, they start “dripping” in fashion and hence, the word drip. Essentially it means you have swag and style.", "annotation_id": "14879604", "url": "https://genius.com/14879604", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Know", "line": "Cartier diamond on my eye, talk too slick, get fired, uh", "vault_lines": ["Cartier diamond on my eye, talk too slick, get fired, uh"], "meaning": "Cartier is an affluential French luxury company known for their jewelry and watches, founded by Louis-François Cartier in 1847. Worn by several prominent figures such as Duchess of Cambridge Kate Middleton, Cartier has established itself as one of the world’s leading jewelry brands.\n\n\n\nThis verse is a double entendre, serving as a both a nod to Uzi’s 2016 song, “Cartier”, and his love for the business and its glasses. Uzi references his Cartier eyewear in many of his songs, a prime example being in his 2016 track, “Team Rocket”;\n\nCartier all on my face", "annotation_id": "14823801", "url": "https://genius.com/14823801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Know", "line": "My Rollie never tickin’ and my boys, they all are hitmen", "vault_lines": ["My Rollie never tickin' and my boys, they all are hitmen"], "meaning": "Rolex is an expensive Swiss luxury watch brand founded by Hans Wilsdorf in 1905. This line is a reference to the Rolex Pearlmaster rainbow watch that Uzi acquired in January 2018. As diamonds are known as “ice” in the rap game, Uzi’s watch is covered with diamonds, and therefore frozen.\n\n\n\nUzi raps about his Rolex in many of his songs, such as his track “Grow Up”;\n\nYeah, flooded my Rollie, yeah\nDiamonds on solar\nDiamonds got colder\n Other words: diamonds got polar", "annotation_id": "14810260", "url": "https://genius.com/14810260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "What You Know", "line": "All hundreds, they blue, ooh, stuntin’ with my rich ass", "vault_lines": ["All hundreds, they blue, ooh, stuntin' with my rich ass"], "meaning": "Beginning on October 8, 2013, a newly-designed hundred dollar bill (featuring a blue, woven 3D security strip) was put into circulation.\n\n\n\nWhen the banknote is tilted back and forth, the bells on the blue ribbon change to 100s, a phenomenon which Uzi revels in.", "annotation_id": "14809308", "url": "https://genius.com/14809308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
