{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "What the fuck? Uh, Perc’", "vault_lines": ["What the fuck? Uh, Perc'"], "meaning": "Oxycodone and Paracetamol, sold under the brand name, Percocet, is a painkiller used to treat headaches, fevers, etc; however when abused can enduce a high, a temporary euphoria, Juice WRLD was addicted to Percocets, and used them up until his death on December 8th of 2019.", "annotation_id": "41828801", "url": "https://genius.com/41828801", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Got drugs in my hair, used the Perc’ for the lock up", "vault_lines": ["Got drugs in my hair, used the Perc' for the lock up"], "meaning": "Drugs like Percocet can stay in your hair for up to 90 days, Uzi is saying he crushed up Percocets to lock up his hair since he has dreads.", "annotation_id": "41731114", "url": "https://genius.com/41731114", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Perc’, mmm, mmm", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no, no, no, no, no, uh"], "meaning": "Oxycodone and Paracetamol, sold under the brand name, Percocet, is a painkiller used to treat headaches, fevers, etc; however when abused can enduce a high, a temporary euphoria, Juice WRLD was addicted to Percocets, and used them up until his death on December 8th of 2019.", "annotation_id": "41725820", "url": "https://genius.com/41725820", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Just another funeral for her, goddamn (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Just another funeral for her, goddamn (Huh)"], "meaning": "Juice WRLD expanded on this line on the official meaning & lyrics video on YouTube:\n\nIt’s like I die at the end of the story and then it’s like, it happens all the time so it’s just another funeral.", "annotation_id": "31578204", "url": "https://genius.com/31578204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Hatin’, but they’re still tryna take our cadence (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Hatin', but they're still tryna take our cadence (Woah)"], "meaning": "These lyrics are a callback to Lil Uzi Vert’s hit song “XO TOUR Llif3,” which featured the following lyric:\n\nNow these niggas wanna take my cadence (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "28003106", "url": "https://genius.com/28003106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Foreign with me, she a dominatrix (Woah) I love that girl and I do like her body", "vault_lines": ["Foreign with me, she a dominatrix (Woah)"], "meaning": "According to Huffington Post, a “dominatrix” is an authoritative woman who enjoys being in control during sexual intercourse. Juice previously discussed his exotic taste in women on his November 2018 track, “Where I Stay:”\n\nShe foreign, like she got a Visa (Uh-huh, oh)\n\nLil Uzi Vert, the featured artist, also has a preference for foreign women, a fact he frequently touches on, like on his August 2017 track, “Sauce It Up:”\n\nI already had that bitch, went and got a badder bitch\nPersian rug, Aladdin shit, nice foreign ho like a Latin bitch\n\nA “foreign” can also allude to a luxurious car brand from outside of the United States. Juice has used the term to describe his vehicles before, perhaps most notably on his unreleased track, “Porridge.”", "annotation_id": "17772823", "url": "https://genius.com/17772823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "She told me that she tryna get closer to Satan", "vault_lines": ["She told me that she tryna get closer to Satan"], "meaning": "His girl has naughty intentions for the night and would prefer to have sexual relations with the star.\n\nThis likely plays on the rockstar lifestyle that the two lives, which includes sexual intercourse and illicit substances. Juice previously discussed these fun seeking women on his February 2017 track “ROCKSTAR GIRL”:\n\nCoke in her nose ring\nMolly in her nails\nShe gon' die a rockstar\nRacing her to hell\n\nLil Uzi Vert, the featured artist, frequently discusses the devil in his music and he has been accused of being a “devil worshiper.” In the past, Uzi dedicated a song to Hell, entitled “444+222” and even labeled his second studio album Eternal Atake after the devilish Heaven’s Gate cult.\n\nIn addition, his name bears an eery resemblance to the word “Lucifer” when repeated quickly.", "annotation_id": "17765014", "url": "https://genius.com/17765014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "I hit from the back and my legs start to lock up", "vault_lines": ["I hit from the back and my legs start to lock up"], "meaning": "This line serves as a callback to Uzi’s hit “Erase Your Social” from his 2016 project The Perfect LUV Tape, where he spit a very similar line:\n\nHit from the back so long\nThat my own legs startin' to get numb", "annotation_id": "15893294", "url": "https://genius.com/15893294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "All that lean I sip on (Oh), now watch me pour it One cup on me, don’t got no friends (No friends)", "vault_lines": ["All that lean I sip on (Oh), now watch me pour it"], "meaning": "In times of depression and sorrow, Juice typically turns to drugs to cope with his emotions. For example, on his May 2018 track “Lean Wit Me” – purposefully titled in reference to the popular concoction which includes a prescription-strength cough syrup known as “lean” –specifically outlines his struggles with addiction in relation to heart break.\n\nJuice also addresses his lack of friends in a verified interview with Genius, he explains:\n\n“One cup on me,“ that means I’m not sharing shit, this is for myself. I don’t got nobody to share with. I have a lot of associates but I don’t consider them friends just due to different situations.\n\nOn his May 2018 track “Used To”, he also raps about his lack of actual friends:\n\nI don’t have no friends, goddamn\nI’m alone until the end, goddamn\n\nLil Uzi Vert, the featured artist on this track, is also famously known for struggling with a lack of friends due to death, fame, and fortune, which he expands on  in his track “XO TOUR LIF3”:\n\nAll my friends are dead\nPush me to the edge", "annotation_id": "15158331", "url": "https://genius.com/15158331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "CB on the beat, ho", "vault_lines": ["CB on the beat, ho"], "meaning": "The producer tag for CBMIX is voiced by Lil Pump.", "annotation_id": "15154166", "url": "https://genius.com/15154166", "state": "pending", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "And she don’t know that all her demons live in me, yeah (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["And she don't know that all her demons live in me, yeah (Woah)"], "meaning": "My biggest demon is laziness. Most definitely laziness, I think for me, that’s bigger than anything else for sure.", "annotation_id": "15134985", "url": "https://genius.com/15134985", "state": "verified", "votes": 117, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "Smoke until my eyes roll back like The Omen", "vault_lines": ["Smoke until my eyes roll back like The Omen"], "meaning": "That part, I was referring to ‘Omen.’ Remember that devil kid?", "annotation_id": "15134981", "url": "https://genius.com/15134981", "state": "verified", "votes": 190, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "She do cocaine in my basement (In my basement)", "vault_lines": ["She do cocaine in my basement"], "meaning": "I was just trying to create a visual image of kind of like suspicious activity, ‘cause you know, the next line, “She told me that she talking to Satan,” and it’s like, in my basement, so it’s sketchy type shit.", "annotation_id": "15134977", "url": "https://genius.com/15134977", "state": "verified", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "She be talkin’ to him when she in the matrix (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["She be talkin' to him when she in the matrix"], "meaning": "I feel like when you get so high, some people get so high, that they just like in a different place, and I was just compare that to being in ‘The Matrix,’ and for the people that don’t know what ‘The Matrix’ is, you’re un-cultured. It’s one of the greatest movies of all time, I heard they started getting corny around like four though. I only saw the first one and the second one.", "annotation_id": "15134972", "url": "https://genius.com/15134972", "state": "verified", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wasted", "line": "She told me that she tryna get closer to Satan She be talkin’ to him when she in the matrix", "vault_lines": ["She told me that she tryna get closer to Satan"], "meaning": "I feel like when you get so high, some people get so high, that they just like in a different place, and I was just compare that to being in ‘The Matrix,’ and for the people that don’t know what ‘The Matrix’ is, you’re un-cultured. It’s one of the greatest movies of all time, I heard they started getting corny around like four though. I only saw the first one and the second one.", "annotation_id": "15134968", "url": "https://genius.com/15134968", "state": "verified", "votes": 155, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
