{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "I’ma make sure that they feelin’ me So I walk around with a new lemon squeeze (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I'ma make sure they remember me"], "meaning": "It’s not easy to catch but they are referring to their enemies getting shot by his Uzi.", "annotation_id": "34101965", "url": "https://genius.com/34101965", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Uh, I’ma make sure they remember me ’Cause I walk around with lot of enemies (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I'ma make sure they remember me"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi vert grew up in north Philly and spent a lot of time in Jersey in his younger life, during that time he’s encountered some people who are not of interest of him, around this time he was very popular amongst his peers and they respect him.", "annotation_id": "34101952", "url": "https://genius.com/34101952", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "’Cause I can’t go back to the hood where them niggas could send at me", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I can't go back to the hood where them niggas could send at me"], "meaning": "Send at me is also another saying as in to send one or multiple people to kill somebody.", "annotation_id": "33849543", "url": "https://genius.com/33849543", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Now I got too much money, I could blow up your whole vicinity (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Now I got too much money, I could blow up your whole vicinity (Yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "There are two meanings to this line. The first, Uzi suggests that he has enough money to pay someone to take care of potential enemies. The second, he is famous enough to have fans and crowds anywhere i.e., “blow up” any area.", "annotation_id": "28501210", "url": "https://genius.com/28501210", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "I got Koreans, F&Ns", "vault_lines": ["I got Koreans, F&Ns"], "meaning": "Another mention of the chinese seemingly as buildup for his last COON bar\n\n“Drankin' yellow, feelin' like a tycoon”\n\nIn other words saying he’s feeling like a coon compared to the asians", "annotation_id": "27643734", "url": "https://genius.com/27643734", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "And I’m steppin’, I’m steppin’ in one-of-ones", "vault_lines": ["And I'm steppin', I'm steppin' in one-of-ones"], "meaning": "Future says that his shoes are one-of-ones, or one of a kind. Future has shown a passion for shoes in the past, and was a guest on Complex’s Sneaker Shopping series.", "annotation_id": "27340696", "url": "https://genius.com/27340696", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "You see these blue face Benjamins", "vault_lines": ["You see these blue face Benjamins"], "meaning": "“blue face Benjamins” are $100 United States dollar bills, characterized by their distinctive blue strip and portrait of U.S. founding father Benjamin Franklin on the front.", "annotation_id": "27340683", "url": "https://genius.com/27340683", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Play that trumpet for the real niggas (What’s up?) What’s up? Play that trumpet for the real niggas", "vault_lines": ["What's, what's, what's up?"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert played the Trumpet back in middle school. He’s said in a few interviews that he only did it to get his GPA up, and to have an easy A. Also fun fact, Hot Cross Buns was the first song uzi ever played.", "annotation_id": "22436408", "url": "https://genius.com/22436408", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Drankin’ yellow, feelin’ like a tycoon", "vault_lines": ["Drankin' yellow, feelin' like a tycoon"], "meaning": "This a play on words. Tycoon is derived from the Japanese word ‘Taikun’ which means ‘Great Lord’. However, in terms of business meaning a ‘tycoon’ is a wealthy, powerful person in business or industry. I can’t help but feel that Future has used “Drakin yellow” to emphasize the Asian meaning behind ‘tycoon’ and wanting the listener to know that he holds a powerful position in the music industry.\n\nFuture has also released a song called ‘TYCOON’ ahead of his highly anticipated eighth studio album. In that song he highlights his wealth and success so far in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "19584723", "url": "https://genius.com/19584723", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Hit a new mistress every day", "vault_lines": ["Hit a new mistress every day"], "meaning": "Future has been always forward with his relationship with women.  Future has made numerous songs about his past relations with these women. Songs such as ‘My Collection’,  ‘Neva Missa Lost’ & ‘Stick to the Models’ are a few out of many that describe his complex relationship with these women. Its also known that Future has 7 kids.", "annotation_id": "19584514", "url": "https://genius.com/19584514", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Said we roll a ’Wood, I roll like fifty L’s", "vault_lines": ["Said we roll a 'Wood, I roll like fifty L's"], "meaning": "A “wood” is a term referring to a Backwood which is a popular cigar around the world that is usually gutted and filled with weed to smoke a blunt.\n\nRoll fifity L’s\" most likely means Uzi rolled fifty L shapes joints which is two papers stuck together in the shape of an L in order to roll bigger amounts of weed than one paper could fit. It is also possible Uzi is calling a blunt and ‘L\" which is an uncommon but not unheard of term for a blunt to keep it on the down-low when talking in public. “Yo you tryna smoke a L”", "annotation_id": "19576972", "url": "https://genius.com/19576972", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Rose gold diamonds same color Hen’", "vault_lines": ["Rose gold diamonds same color Hen'"], "meaning": "Future is saying that his diamonds are the same color as his Hennessy. He is referring to the first of the “Privilege Collection by Hennessy” The Hennessy V.S.O.P Helios which comes in a rose gold bottle and now sells for approx $600 USD per bottle.", "annotation_id": "19576835", "url": "https://genius.com/19576835", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "You know that Richard Mille cost me a Benz", "vault_lines": ["You know that Richard Mille cost me a Benz"], "meaning": "Here, future mentions that his Richard Mille, a Swiss luxury watchmaking brand , cost him the price of a Mercedes Benz.\nRichard mille watches usually cost at least $80,000, with some watches costing 100,000-500,000.", "annotation_id": "19423757", "url": "https://genius.com/19423757", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Everybody know I come from outer space", "vault_lines": ["Everybody know I come from outer space"], "meaning": "Future has several projects relating to outer space, including the mixtape “Astronaut Status”, his debut album “Pluto”, and “Pluto 3D”.\n\nStarting off his professional rap career in 2011-12 with these space themed projects, “Pluto” was a nickname he adopted early on. Teasing his collaborating with Future as well as the release of EA, Lil Uzi refereed to himself as “Baby Pluto” in the days leading up to the drop.", "annotation_id": "19334428", "url": "https://genius.com/19334428", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "Yeah, let’s do it (Yo, Pi’erre, yo, Pi’erre)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, let's, let's do it"], "meaning": "This is one of the many tags of rapper and producer Pi'erre Bourne. As a producer, he is well-known for working with Carti on iconic tracks like the 2017 cut “Magnolia” but has also worked with other popular rappers such as Kanye West and Travis Scott.\n\nThis tag is an audio recording of Pi'erre’s fans. It was first used on Pi'erre’s 2018 single “Planet Namek.”", "annotation_id": "19276232", "url": "https://genius.com/19276232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wassup", "line": "You know we comin’ in number one You know we gon’ kill the whole summer too", "vault_lines": ["You know we comin' in number one"], "meaning": "Future could be talking about Eternal Atake (Deluxe) – LUV vs. The World 2 debuting at number or his next project doing the same. Then saying that him and Lil Uzi are going to be played all summer long, taking over the music industry.\n\nFuture has 2 possible projects releasing this year with WATTBA2 with Drake and his 8th solo project which is why he is saying him and Uzi will kill the summer.", "annotation_id": "19275297", "url": "https://genius.com/19275297", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
