{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Where you get the money for them shoes, girl?", "vault_lines": ["Where you get the money for them shoes, girl?"], "meaning": "NAV questions how his girlfriend got enough money to afford these expensive Christian Louboutin heels, He’s starting to feel unsure towards her loyality to him. Possibly indicating that she’s with another man behind his back.", "annotation_id": "40109349", "url": "https://genius.com/40109349", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Said she love me, don’t believe her, mhm", "vault_lines": ["Said she love me, don't believe her, mhm"], "meaning": "Despite this girl showing love and affection to NAV, He doesn’t believe her and knows she’s giving him meaningless attention.", "annotation_id": "40109315", "url": "https://genius.com/40109315", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Where you at? At my house Let me see that ass What you say? I said “let me see that ass” That ass? Oh, you on some naked shit Hahaha I’m on my way Stop lyin’ I’m on my way, bye", "vault_lines": ["Let me see that ass"], "meaning": "This is a conversation between Uzi and Brittany Renner, his girlfriend at the time. These are the type of conversations people have with their significant other, asking where they are. However, it is very uncommon to ask a girl to look her buttocks in the way Uzi is asking Brittany.\n\nAdditionally, this song is about girls, money, and relationships ruined by cheating. However, Uzi flips the mood and is in the total opposite tone in this dialogue. He is more happy than regretful and Brittany, on the other hand, is in a joking mood.\n\nBefore Brittany, Uzi dated Brittany Byrd and the two, however, broke up after cheating rumors, but Uzi later shut the rumors down. Most of Uzi’s relationships that end do so because of cheating speculation.", "annotation_id": "19776445", "url": "https://genius.com/19776445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Said that she there ’cause she know promoters in the club (Yeah) Come to find out that my homeboy hit her up (Woah, woah, woah)", "vault_lines": ["Said that she there 'cause she know promoters in the club (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This line further describes Nav’s time at the club and illuminates his surprise seeing the Instagram thottie described in the earlier lines of the verse.\n\nWhen Nav wonders why the girl is at the club without hitting him up first, she makes up a lie about knowing a club promoter. However, this lie is exposed in the next line when Nav’s boy lets him know that he was the one who hit her up to come through.\n\nThese lines reinforce the general theme of the song, that it makes no sense for Nav to trust a materialistic girl who only wants to use him and his crew for clout and money. Although she claims to love him, he no longer believes her and regrets giving her any type of special attention at all. The girl getting caught in a lie proves that she’s dishonest and not worth any sort of effort, even if she’s good in bed.", "annotation_id": "15965152", "url": "https://genius.com/15965152", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Just to eat, Louboutins all on her feet (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Just to eat, Louboutins all on her feet (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Louboutins are a Brand of Designer Shoes.\nThey were designed by Christian Louboutin.\nA lot of rich and famous people wear Louboutins to show off their wealth. The cost of these shoes ranges from $495 to $6000 USD for custom models.", "annotation_id": "14587455", "url": "https://genius.com/14587455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "What would she do for a purse? (Huh?) She said she’ll give me a Perc’ (Thirty)", "vault_lines": ["What would she do for a purse? (Huh?) She said she'll give me a Perc' (Thirty)"], "meaning": "Uzi’s girl says she’ll give him a Percocet, a common pain-relieving drug that is often abused, in exchange for a purse. The most common Percocet dose is 30 mg.", "annotation_id": "13154619", "url": "https://genius.com/13154619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Twenty on her choker, mhm", "vault_lines": ["Twenty on her choker, mhm"], "meaning": "“Twenty” in this case refers to $20,000. The price most likely comes from the fact that the choker in question is diamond encrusted. These can go from anywhere between a couple hundred to the hundreds of thousands.\n\n\n\nNav cares about this girl so much that he is willing to drop tens of thousands of dollars on an accessory for her\n\nAnother way this could be interpreted is that 20 different guys had sex with her and choked her during it.", "annotation_id": "13057486", "url": "https://genius.com/13057486", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Uzi, they used to make fun of you (dress it up)", "vault_lines": ["Uzi, they used to make fun of you (dress it up)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi is addressing the fact that he tends to stand out from the general crowd, especially in terms of his clothing and his childhood. Being that he grew up in the rougher Francisville neighborhood where his dad lived, he had trouble making friends and being accepted.\n\nIn an article with noisey, Uzi harps on the fact that he was “the only one that look like this,” while gesturing at his hair and outfit: colorful locs, a leather jacket, asymmetrical hoodie, and track pants. In an interview with XXL, Uzi comments, “Don’t no one look like me in Philly,” going on to explain his particular interest in diverse “fashion.”\n\nHe in fact claims to still have no friends at all. On megahit track “XO TOUR Llife”, he sings, “all my friends are dead,” a double entendre in that “dead presidents” (a slang term for money) are his only friend, thus all the friends and family members who he used to be able to trust are now dead, which he raps about on tracks like “YSL”  and “LUV SCARS K.o 1600”. However, as he establishes a prominent presence in the rap game and gains fans who appreciate his diversity, he probably feels more secure about himself.", "annotation_id": "13049749", "url": "https://genius.com/13049749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "No, no, no, no, I don’t need you (I don’t need you) No, no, no, no, I don’t need you (I don’t need you)", "vault_lines": ["No, no, no, no, I don't need you (I don't need you)"], "meaning": "This sounds like a direct shot at Uzi’s notorious ex girlfriend Brittany Byrd. After Brittany supposedly cheated on Uzi, the breakup was announced on twitter on June 26, 2016 along with the release of the breakup song called “Stole Your Luv”. He also also raps about Brittany in many of his tracks from his recent album LUV is Rage 2, like his song “X”.\n\nI don’t know whats next, yeah\nI don’t want my ex, no\n\n\n\nIn correlation with the theme of the song–relationships ruined by cheating–Uzi ensures that he no longer needs his ex.\n\n“Murked” is a slang term that essentially means to kill. Uzi cleverly plays on the word to say that he killed the verse and his relationship with Brittany when he found out she cheated.", "annotation_id": "13040432", "url": "https://genius.com/13040432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Speakin’ of sweater, my neck is so frozen it lookin’ just like an iceberg", "vault_lines": ["Speakin' of sweater, my neck is so frozen it lookin' just like an iceberg"], "meaning": "In rap culture, diamonds are frequently addressed as “ice”, based on the way they shine. “Iceberg” therefore signifies a very large amount of diamonds on a piece of jewelry. A great example of this is Lil Uzi Vert’s Marylin Manson chain.", "annotation_id": "13033537", "url": "https://genius.com/13033537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "You hit me on my DM like a fangirl (Woah, woah) Did you want me or did you want these bands, girl? (Woah, woah)", "vault_lines": ["You hit me on my DM like a fangirl (Woah, woah)"], "meaning": "NAV is expressing his realization of how his fame and fortune has got in the way of him being able to find a real partner. The line conveys how these girls approach him through Instagram, indicating that their real intention was never to connect with NAV, but rather to take advantage of him for their personal gain.\n\nNAV has made a similar reference in the past on his 2016 track, “Fell in Love”:\n\nHit me, DM, told she was a fan", "annotation_id": "13029527", "url": "https://genius.com/13029527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "I’m ashamed of all the things that I was doin’ for you Should’ve known that all these girls the same and they ain’t loyal", "vault_lines": ["I'm ashamed of all the things that I was doin' for you"], "meaning": "Since his rise to fame and popularity, NAV has gotten a lot of fame and money. He has been spending his time with groupies who fuck with him because of his fame and influence. He regrets leaving his girl because all these new girls only want money.\n\nHis regret for leaving his old girl was expressed in “Call Me,”, in which he sadly raps:\n\nI’ll try to come back to you, girl, I’m sorry\n\nThe same girl he talks about above is also talked about in “Held Me Down”:\n\nGirl, all this money, all these things don’t feel the same without you", "annotation_id": "13026037", "url": "https://genius.com/13026037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "23, but I had her when I was 22 (What?)", "vault_lines": ["23, but I had her when I was 22 (What?)"], "meaning": "Although Lil Uzi’s 2017 album LUV is Rage 2 revolves around his ex girlfriend Brittany Byrd, it seems as though he as moved on to rapping about his new girlfriend, Brittany Renner.\n\nOn July 31, 2017, Uzi celebrated his 23rd birthday, and though he didn’t celebrate it publicly, model Brittany Renner took to Instagram to show him love and wish him a happy birthday.", "annotation_id": "13023474", "url": "https://genius.com/13023474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Yeah, all my hundreds blue", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, all my hundreds blue"], "meaning": "Any U.S. $100 bills printed since October 3, 2013 have a blue 3-D security strip running down the center to prove authenticity, as well as a blue tint. This might signify that he has only recently started to get big amounts of money.", "annotation_id": "13023413", "url": "https://genius.com/13023413", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Fuck her, I don’t know her, yeah Give me face, like poker", "vault_lines": ["Fuck her, I don't know her, yeah"], "meaning": "Here, NAV is referring to a sexual interaction with another girl in which he doesn’t want to understand the girl’s personality, traits, qualities, or emotions.\n\nPoker is a game that amalgamates gambling, strategy, and skill. An important skill of the game is a poker face–an inscrutable face that reveals no hint of a person’s intentions or thoughts. “Face” is one of many slang terms for oral sex. NAV plays on the phrase “poker face” to say that he wants the girl to give him emotionless oral sex.", "annotation_id": "13023340", "url": "https://genius.com/13023340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Now I know you just another Instagram girl (Woah, woah)", "vault_lines": ["Now I know you just another Instagram girl (Woah, woah)"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to the song “Instagram Girls” by Cadet. An “Instagram girl” is someone who tends to be very popular on Instagram, revealing or provocative with their posts, and likes to lead guys on to boost their own confidence and ego. NAV, however, clarifies that the girl he was trying to get with or was with, is just another popular girl who was pretending to love him and most likely wanted him just for his money.", "annotation_id": "13023245", "url": "https://genius.com/13023245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "I can’t text her back, these Franklins what I’m thumbin’ through (Blue hundos)", "vault_lines": ["I can't text her back, these Franklins what I'm thumbin' through (Blue hundos)"], "meaning": "“Franklins” is slang for $100 bills—in 2013, a blue 3D security ribbon was added to the US hundred bill.", "annotation_id": "13022262", "url": "https://genius.com/13022262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "All this ice, I need a freezer, mhm", "vault_lines": ["All this ice, I need a freezer, mhm"], "meaning": "In hip hop, diamonds are commonly referred to as ‘ice’ due to the way in which they shine. Using a freezer as a metaphor for jewelry has been popularized by fellow rapper Rich The Kid, who made a song called “New Freezer.” In a lyric breakdown with Genius, he explains the meaning of ‘new freezer’.\n\nNew freezer is basically some new ice. When you just copped some new ice. You might’ve got a new pinky ring. A new motherfucking watch. A new diamond chain. You know this shit cost. Get some new ice. That’s the new freezer, you know what I’m saying? Really my whole neck, that’s a fucking new freezer.", "annotation_id": "13019803", "url": "https://genius.com/13019803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Off-White on my Prestos, all these girls I’m runnin’ through (I’m runnin’ through it)", "vault_lines": ["Off-White on my Prestos, all these girls I'm runnin' through (I'm runnin' through it)"], "meaning": "Uzi is referring to the OFF-WHITE x Nike Presto collaboration, which got released in late 2017. Original Prestos are classified as running shoe so he can also be implying that he is running through the girls like his shoes.\n\n\n\nOFF-WHITE is an up-and-coming fashion brand founded by Virgil Abloh, who has great ties with Uzi. He created the cover art for Luv Is Rage 2 and directed the videoclip to Uzi’s breakout hit, “XO TOUR Llif3.”", "annotation_id": "13019378", "url": "https://genius.com/13019378", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "Stevie Wonder, I can’t see you (Can’t do this)", "vault_lines": ["Stevie Wonder, I can't see you (Can't do this)"], "meaning": "Uzi is paying homage to Stevie Wonder, a blind musician and multi-instrumentalist.\n\nUzi is essentially describing Stevie Wonder’s conditions and metaphorically possessing his blindness, playing on the previous line/incorporating the literal meaning of “see-through.”\n\nUzi has already mentioned Stevie Wonder previously, in the song “Pretty Mami” from his debut album Luv Is Rage 2, where he raps:\n\nGirl, you took a L and we can see that\nStevie Wonder, Ray Charles, Daredevil could see that?", "annotation_id": "13018411", "url": "https://genius.com/13018411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Wanted You", "line": "She a freak, took her to Nobu, on a beach (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["She a freak, took her to Nobu, on a beach (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Nobu is a high-end restaurant owned by Nobuyuki “Nobu” Matsuhisa, a Japanese celebrity chef.\n\nThe only Nobu restaurant on a beach is in Malibu, California which in relevance to Toronto (where NAV stays), is considerably far. This just shows you what NAV is willing to spend just to enjoy a meal with a girl.\n\n\n\nThis isn’t the first time that NAV has made reference to Nobu in a song. In his first collaboration with Lil Uzi Vert, “A$AP Ferg”, from his collaborative mixtape with Metro Boomin, Perfect Timing, NAV said:\n\nTook your bitch to Nobu, fuck me for some sushi now", "annotation_id": "13016698", "url": "https://genius.com/13016698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
