{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Walk Down", "line": "Casamigos, Lil Uzi, no, I am not a Migo’", "vault_lines": ["Casamigos, Lil Uzi, no, I am not a Migo'"], "meaning": "This line is a direct jab at Migos, the popular rap trio from Lawrenceville, which features Quavo, Takeoff, and Offset.\n\nThe Philly icon and Migos did not always have such a pessimistic relationship though. Previously from the start of their connection, Migos and Lil Uzi have collaborated before on track Bad and Boujee, which is a 4x Platinum RIAA certified track released in 2016 that amassed over 1.38 billion views on YouTube as of August 1, 2026.\n\nThe animosity initially started brewing when Offset, a member of the trio Quavo, posted a video criticizing artists who wore upside-down crosses, a common symbol of Satanism, by saying that those who did looked ‘lame’.\n\nA few rappers, such as XXXTENTACION & SahBabii, were quick to reply with regards to this. Shortly after, Lil Uzi posted an Instagram story of him dancing with a greyscale filter and a doodled upside-down cross overlayed on the video while wearing an upside-down cross necklace.", "annotation_id": "40895455", "url": "https://genius.com/40895455", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
