{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Trap, he smoking on midnight gas Finessing a nigga with pounds of the swag", "vault_lines": ["Trap, he smoking on midnight gas"], "meaning": "Rich The Kid is smoking on “gas” aka marijuana at his trap late night. While there, he persuades somebody to make a deal that is more beneficial to himself by selling them “Schwag”, or low quality weed.", "annotation_id": "9472527", "url": "https://genius.com/9472527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "You don’t want problems Bitch I got choppers, Afghanistan", "vault_lines": ["You don't want problems"], "meaning": "You don’t want to fuck with Rich. He’s probably packing heat down in GA. A “chopper” is a street term for an automatic rifle. Usually associated with an AK-47, hence the reference to Afghanistan – they are so abundant there due to the Soviet Invasion of Afghanistan from 1978–1980. At the end of December 1979, the Soviet Union sent thousands of troops into Afghanistan and immediately assumed complete military and political control of Kabul and large portions of the country.", "annotation_id": "8965222", "url": "https://genius.com/8965222", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Nigga better tell him my uncle OG with a motherfuckin’ felon He’ll dead him in a second if I tell him", "vault_lines": ["Nigga better tell him my uncle OG with a motherfuckin' felon"], "meaning": "Disrespect, especially to an “OG” is not taken well in the streets. Ferg explains that his uncle was an Original Gangsta, someone who is held with respect and carries a lot of weight in the name. It would be a mistake to cross Ferg and his crew and it wouldn’t be an issue for his uncle to step out and murder for his nephew, who already has a felony or two.", "annotation_id": "8965180", "url": "https://genius.com/8965180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Fergy gonna get ‘em, youngin’ doin’ better", "vault_lines": ["Fergy gonna get 'em, youngin' doin' better"], "meaning": "At only age 27, Ferg has quickly gain popularity through the ranks and has been featured on many new singles such as New Level with Atlanta rapper, Future. Ferg and the rest of the A$AP Mob have established that they’re here to stay.", "annotation_id": "8965157", "url": "https://genius.com/8965157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty", "vault_lines": ["I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty"], "meaning": "It’s just about, like, changing everything to another level. Building up your level, you know? Like, money. You’re turning money into bigger bills. I’m starting to relate to it now. Everything is starting to work its plan.", "annotation_id": "8748238", "url": "https://genius.com/8748238", "state": "verified", "votes": 115, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Forty-forty hit your woadie shorty", "vault_lines": ["I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty"], "meaning": "I learned that word “woadie” by listening to rap music. Lil Wayne said it. Everybody said it. In high school, we said it a lot, because it was a cool word to say. All the cool people said it. You know. All the people that could dress and stuff. I had grills in high school.", "annotation_id": "8748232", "url": "https://genius.com/8748232", "state": "verified", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "[Verse 3: Rich The Kid]", "vault_lines": ["Tryna jump at Rich the Kid, diamonds dancin' like Diddy"], "meaning": "That’s my bro. He hit me up earlier. He cool. He spends a lot of money on clothes and jewelry and stuff.\n\nI really wanted Young Thug on there, because the original song was called “Thugger Boys.” But he didn’t have no contact info and this was before me and Young Thug was cool. So we just got Rich The Kid on there. We’re all cool, now. It’s cool now. Carnage wanted to change the name. I guess he didn’t wanna get sued or anything. I told Young Thug about it later in life, when we met, and he was surprised. He was like “for real?” He said we definitely should have kept it.", "annotation_id": "8747999", "url": "https://genius.com/8747999", "state": "verified", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "[Produced By: Charlie Heat & Carnage]", "vault_lines": ["I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty"], "meaning": "I made that back when I was recording in Philly. I put it out that first day and that’s how Carnage heard it. Carnage hit me like, “Take that down. We’re gonna make that big.” Carnage  hit me up on SoundCloud. I gave him my number, then it went from there.\n\nMe and Charlie are still cool. I see him around. He’s working hard. I’m working real hard. We always run into each other. When you work really hard in hip-hop, you run into each other, because it’s not that big. Around the time that he got signed is when Kanye was paying attention to me—which he still is.", "annotation_id": "8747921", "url": "https://genius.com/8747921", "state": "verified", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Balmain, Saint Laurent with the Fendi", "vault_lines": ["I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty"], "meaning": "I really have no favorite, because I love ‘em like my children. Everybody gets their equal time. But I don’t know. I just named them because they were cool clothes. Those are cool ones. If it would’ve flowed right, I would’ve said other designers.", "annotation_id": "8731464", "url": "https://genius.com/8731464", "state": "verified", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Spoke to NumbaNine ’fore he went to jail and He was on his way to his dreams Then his dreams started derailing from a weapon", "vault_lines": ["Spoke to NumbaNine 'fore he went to jail and"], "meaning": "Rondonumba Nine is a Chicago rapper who was arrested at age 17 for murder. In December 2013, months before his arrest, he posted this picture of himself holding a rocket launcher:\n\n\n\nThe picture tipped off Chicago police and they issued an alert that referenced Rondonumba Nine by name. His dreams were derailed by run-ins with the law. Before he was in jail, he’d been cosigned by Lupe Fiasco, Meek Mill, and Jeezy.", "annotation_id": "8719393", "url": "https://genius.com/8719393", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "[Verse 2: A$AP Ferg]", "vault_lines": ["I turn five to a ten, I turn twenty to a fifty"], "meaning": "Critics have noted that the beat on this song sounds a lot like A$AP Ferg’s “Work.”", "annotation_id": "8715800", "url": "https://genius.com/8715800", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "I trap in the kitchen with Whitney", "vault_lines": ["I trap in the kitchen with Whitney"], "meaning": "These lyrics echo Quavo (from Migos) on Gucci Mane’s  “Jackie Chan.”\n\nWhitney is another name for cocaine—a slang that comes from the late singer Whitney Houston, whose death was due in part to cocaine use.\n\n\n\nActavis created the now-discontinued promethazine and codeine syrup used in lean. He’s drinking so much it’s destroying his kidneys.", "annotation_id": "8715696", "url": "https://genius.com/8715696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "I got your bitch on me and your mama on me and she birthed you Blowin’ Uzi, I’m just off the shits Got your bitch on me, she all up on the dick", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I got choppers, Afghanistan"], "meaning": "This is what Uzi considers different about himself. He told Complex:\n\n“The thing that makes me different from any other rapper is that I usually talk real crazy in my songs. …I’m talking about girls and stuff, it’s usually the truth…When I’m talking crazy about girls—like I’ll talk about my girlfriend, and then talk about having like a threesome right after. It’s true. It’s usually true. I’m not gonna lie to you.”", "annotation_id": "8715647", "url": "https://genius.com/8715647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Whatchu want, tell me whatchu want (what do you want?) Like whatchu want, like what do you want? (what do you want?) Whatchu want? Let a nigga know Let a nigga know, let a nigga know", "vault_lines": ["Let a nigga know"], "meaning": "Uzi is in to flipping money and as a good businessman he has got whatever you need to get your day going. He has all the drugs anyone could want, so if you want something let Uzi know and he will supply it to you.\n\n\n\nWhat Do You Want is the phrase that makes the acronym WDYW. The concept is to make money by any means necessary.", "annotation_id": "7932367", "url": "https://genius.com/7932367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "These kids I try to tell ’em, don’t get caught with the weapon Hip-hop police on the ’Gram and they can’t wait to get ’em", "vault_lines": ["These kids I try to tell 'em, don't get caught with the weapon"], "meaning": "Law enforcement and Federal Investigators monitor sites like Instagram for illegal activity and gun trafficking. Just ask Neno Best\n\n\n\nTelling all sides of the story is what makes Ferg real, so when he raps about hustling, he’s gonna rap about getting caught. He described his wholistic approach in an interview with NPR:\n\nI feel like you have to have all the elements. If you just telling ‘em one part of the story — if you telling 'em how to slip some cocaine or whatever in a song, you better be telling 'em what it feel like to get caught or what it feel like, the aftermath. ..It’s got to be real… You can’t just give them this hustle life. Hustle hustle. You gon’ be hustling forever. Ain’t no drug dealer hustling forever without getting caught.", "annotation_id": "5116330", "url": "https://genius.com/5116330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Migo Gang, A$AP Mob, he might fuck around get robbed", "vault_lines": ["Migo Gang, A$AP Mob, he might fuck around get robbed"], "meaning": "The Atlanta-crew Migos is how Rich the Kid got his start in rap. RTK and Migos are currently label-mates on Quality Control.\n\nA$AP Mob is the other crew represented on this track—they hail from Harlem.", "annotation_id": "5001240", "url": "https://genius.com/5001240", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "I trap out the bando, them onions", "vault_lines": ["I trap out the bando, them onions"], "meaning": "Fairly standard trap talk. Trapping refers here to the production or selling of cocaine and an onion is an ounce. Bando refers to an abandoned house where such activities take place.\n\nA very Migos-ian line.", "annotation_id": "4852552", "url": "https://genius.com/4852552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "WDYW", "line": "Black Panther party, Huey with the leather", "vault_lines": ["Black Panther party, Huey with the leather"], "meaning": "Huey P Newton cofounded Black Panthers, along with Bobby Seale, in 1966.\n\nHe’s often pictured in a black leather jacket. His rallying cry was: “We’re coming from Oakland, we’ve got our leather jackets on, we’ve got our rifles, and we’re going to walk into the legislature with guns. See what happens.”\n\n\n\nFerg is in the business of making high-quality leather goods, including belts for clients like Swizz Beats and Chris Brown. He’s been in fashion since before he was even rapping, following in the footsteps of his dad, who had a shirt-printing business and boutique in Harlem.", "annotation_id": "4852533", "url": "https://genius.com/4852533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
