{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vibe*", "line": "Got you on tape, now a hoe can’t duck me", "vault_lines": ["Got you on tape, now a hoe can’t duck me"], "meaning": "“Got you on tape, now a hoe can’t duck me” has a double meaning. On the surface, Uzi says he has a recording or evidence of a woman that she wouldn’t want revealed, meaning she can’t avoid or ignore him (“duck me”). At the same time, “on tape” and “duck me” combine to sound like “duct tape,” creating a wordplay where the two phrases phonetically resemble the common adhesive tape.\n\nthe wordplay works because “duck” is often pronounced similarly to the first syllable of “duct” in casual speech, making the phrase sound close to “duct tape” when heard quickly.", "annotation_id": "40148280", "url": "https://genius.com/40148280", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vibe*", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-vibe-lyrics", "genius_title": "Vibe*", "genius_id": 12849424, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Niggas, they be mad, ’cause I’m walking with the cash", "vault_lines": ["Niggas, they be mad, 'cause I'm walking with the cash"], "meaning": "When a person gets a lot of fame or money, many will often be envious or jealous of that person. Some will even be angry that a person, who might not even deserve their fourtune, has a greater amount or fame and status than themself. Uzi describes feeling as though multiple people are mad that he has more money then them.", "annotation_id": "35529625", "url": "https://genius.com/35529625", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
