{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Pull up in a Lambo’, did the digi’ dash", "vault_lines": ["Pull up in a Lambo', did the digi' dash"], "meaning": "Strictly speaking, a “digi' dash” (digital dash) is an electronic dashboard that you typically find in high-end cars such as the Lambo' (Lamborghini) Lil Uzi is talking about.\n\nTo pull up means to approach someone or to go somewhere (in a vehicle).", "annotation_id": "29775870", "url": "https://genius.com/29775870", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Space Coupe, huh, yeah, Justin Bieber, huh", "vault_lines": ["Space Coupe, huh, yeah, Justin Bieber, huh"], "meaning": "In 2021, Justin Bieber was introduced to his custom-made 2018 Rolls-Royce ‘spaceship’ Wraith, which took over three years to build. The process was documented on West Coast Customs' YouTube channel.", "annotation_id": "29746740", "url": "https://genius.com/29746740", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Me and Carti, yeah, huh, we like AP, Rollie", "vault_lines": ["Me and Carti, yeah, huh, we like AP, Rollie"], "meaning": "This sentence suggests that Uzi and Carti appreciate luxury watches, particularly Audemars Piguet (AP) and Rolex (Rollie), indicating their preference for high-end timepieces.", "annotation_id": "29735689", "url": "https://genius.com/29735689", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Yeah, 308, yeah-yeah, Heaven’s Gate, huh-huh", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, 308, yeah-yeah, Heaven's Gate, huh-huh"], "meaning": "Heaven’s Gate was a cult founded in 1974 whose members infamously committed mass suicide in 1997.\n\nIn 2018, Lil Uzi Vert posted the cover art for then upcoming album, Eternal Atake. The cover art contained a logo identical to the Heaven’s Gate logo and the remaining group members threatened legal action against Uzi, causing them to change it", "annotation_id": "29726857", "url": "https://genius.com/29726857", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Look like rockstars, my bitches wanna mosh", "vault_lines": ["Look like rockstars, my bitches wanna mosh"], "meaning": "A moshpit is an area in front of a stage where very physical and rough dancing takes place. In this line Carti compares moshpits at his concerts, to the ones at concerts of rockstars, because both his and rockstar moshpits are known for being very violent and wild.", "annotation_id": "29723772", "url": "https://genius.com/29723772", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Blowing up your block like my name was Little Kim (Kim Jong Un)", "vault_lines": ["Blowing up your block like my name was Little Kim (Kim Jong Un)"], "meaning": "kim jong un reference\n\nyou can hear  uzi say “kim jong un” if you listen closely", "annotation_id": "29629186", "url": "https://genius.com/29629186", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "I ain’t hit the lick, but I’m wearing my black mask, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I ain't hit the lick, but I'm wearing my black mask, yeah"], "meaning": "This line reffers to Playboi Carti’s fashion choices. Inspired by the grammy winning and critticly aclaimed ex-billionare Kanye West, Carti is often seen wearing a black mask just for the look of it.", "annotation_id": "29582752", "url": "https://genius.com/29582752", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Gotta keep it on me, Draco on me, gotta protect myself", "vault_lines": ["Gotta keep it on me, Draco on me, gotta protect myself"], "meaning": "“Draco” reffers to the Draco Pistol which is a gas operated semi-automatic pistol sold by Century Inernational Arms. It takes heavy insipration from the deisgn of AK-47.", "annotation_id": "29581888", "url": "https://genius.com/29581888", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "I just popped a blue, uh, uh, got me leaning, uh", "vault_lines": ["I just popped a blue, uh, uh, got me leaning, uh"], "meaning": "“Popped a blue” might reffer to M30’s. M30’s are blue pills containing 30mg of oxycodone, which is one of the strongest opioid pain medication. Although, the intended use of oxycodone is as a pain killer, a lot of people use it as a drug due to it’s high euphoric and relaxing effects.", "annotation_id": "29564010", "url": "https://genius.com/29564010", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "(That be Maaly Raw)", "vault_lines": ["Better call the paramedics, yeah-yeah, get the hit bitch, just by myself (That be Maaly Raw)"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for Philadelphia producer Maaly Raw, said by fellow Philly artist Lil Uzi Vert. Uzi has worked with Maaly since the start of his career, working with him on hits such as “Money Longer” and “Do What I Want.”\n\n\nThis is the second official Carti x Uzi collaboration that Maaly has produced, with the first being 2018’s “Shoota,” which appeared on the former’s debut studio album, Die Lit.\n\nIt should be noted Maaly produced this beat in 2021 on an Instagram livestream, 2 years prior to the release.", "annotation_id": "29559688", "url": "https://genius.com/29559688", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Pull up in a Lambo’ with no license, Lil’ Kim", "vault_lines": ["Pull up in a Lambo' with no license, Lil' Kim"], "meaning": "Uzi notably owns a Lamborghini Urus, which he had wrapped in an Anime-inspired livery.\n\nOn August 30, 2007, rapper Lil Kim was pulled over for driving without any license plates on her Lamborghini Gallardo.", "annotation_id": "29555519", "url": "https://genius.com/29555519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Give me head, diploma", "vault_lines": ["Give me head, diploma"], "meaning": "This could be a possible reference to “Fire Alarm”, where Uzi says a similar line:\n\nShe gave me head like that bitch got diploma", "annotation_id": "29552851", "url": "https://genius.com/29552851", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "VETEMENTS-VETEMENTS jeans, put your stylist right on blast", "vault_lines": ["VETEMENTS-VETEMENTS jeans, put your stylist right on blast"], "meaning": "VETEMENTS is a popular luxury fashion brand and design collective founded in 2014. It’s mainly known for their avant garde jeans and well made jackets.\n\nCarti has been seen wearing VETEMENTS clothes a few times throughout his career.\n\n\n\nPictured: Playboi Carti wearing a VETEMENTS hoodie in 2022.", "annotation_id": "29551098", "url": "https://genius.com/29551098", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "Twenty nine, sixteen, yeah-yeah, yeah, we made that by ourselves", "vault_lines": ["Twenty nine, sixteen, yeah-yeah, yeah, we made that by ourselves"], "meaning": "Twenty nine sixteen reffers to Lil Uzi Verts and Playboi Carti’s infamous scrapped joint project, 16*29.\n\nIn 2017 Carti and Uzi were making plenty music togheter and were teasing a project. Soon project was scrapped and most of the songs made for it were either shelved or reworked and placed on Die Lit.\n\nLater, in 2020 Uzi and Carti gave one more shot at making a joint album. They flew together to London and made about 40 songs for the project. Not much is known about this version of 16*29, because neither of them have songs from these sessions.", "annotation_id": "29551047", "url": "https://genius.com/29551047", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Vetements Jeans", "line": "We like Jay and Nas, we be popping bars", "vault_lines": ["We like Jay and Nas, we be popping bars"], "meaning": "This line appears to be a reference to two prominent figures in the world of hip-hop music: Jay-Z and Nas\n\nJay-Z and Nas are both highly respected and influential rap artists who have had a long history of rivalry and competition in the hip-hop scene. Their feud, often referred to as the “Jay-Z vs. Nas beef,” involved diss tracks and lyrical sparring between the two artists. The line mentioned could be a nod to their music and their reputations as lyricists, suggesting that Uzi and Carti are similarly skilled in their craft and metaphorically . Or it could possibly be a play on words knowing they talk a lot about popping pills in this song", "annotation_id": "29537941", "url": "https://genius.com/29537941", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
