{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Valentine (Remix)", "line": "You just was with him last week, you can’t have my last name (No)", "vault_lines": ["You just was with him last week, you can't have my last name (No)"], "meaning": "In marriage, it is customary for the bride to take the groom’s last name.\n\n\n\nHowever, the prevailing unfaithfulness  shown by Uzi’s girl has prompted him not to give her this emblem.", "annotation_id": "14969812", "url": "https://genius.com/14969812", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Valentine (Remix)", "line": "You tellin’ me you love me ’cause I’m next to blow (Blow, blow) I kicked you out my life, you miss them checks the most (Most, most)", "vault_lines": ["You tellin' me you need me but I need you"], "meaning": "In this verse, Uzi details the working of all women around him, using his companionship for the popularity and cash being with him produces— a common theme throughout his music.\n\nA cardinal example of this attitude is produced in Uzi’s 2016 track, “Money Mitch”:\n\nYeah ‘member they ain’t love me, now these girls wanna hug me", "annotation_id": "14969569", "url": "https://genius.com/14969569", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
