{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Uzi Intro", "line": "Don’t let me get into my zone And if you do that, I swear you in trouble", "vault_lines": ["Don't let me get into my zone"], "meaning": "“Don’t let me get in my zone” is a massively quoted and referenced lyric from Kanye West and Jay Z’s “Niggas In Paris”.\n\nYou are now watching the throne, don’t let me get in my zone\nDon’t let me get in my zone, don’t let me get in my zone\n\nIf Uzi’s allowed to record and work on music without any setbacks, he’ll be coming for other rapper’s spots in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "8415264", "url": "https://genius.com/8415264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
