{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Uzi Gang", "line": "Harlem World got a hundred spittas", "vault_lines": ["Harlem World got a hundred spittas"], "meaning": "He is saying there are a lot of artists that came from Harlem, New York such as:\n\n40 Cal – rapper\nA-Mafia – rapper\nASAP Rocky – rapper from Harlem (member of ASAP Mob)\nAzealia Banks – rapper, singer, lyricist\nBlack Rob – rapper from Spanish Harlem\nCam'ron – rapper (owner of Diplomat Records) (Dipset)\nCannibal Ox – rap duo\nCharlie Clips – battle rapper\nCrash Crew – old-school rap group\nYaya DaCosta – America’s Next Top Model contestant/model\nDamon Dash – former CEO of Roc-A-Fella Records\nDJ Hollywood – VH-1 hip hop honoree; rap/hip-hop pioneer\nDJ Red Alert – DJ, hip hop pioneer\nKool Moe Dee – old-school rapper and one-third of the Treacherous Three\nRob Base and DJ E-Z Rock – rap duo best known for their hit “It Takes Two”\nFatman Scoop – Grammy and MTV Award winner; radio personality; reality TV star\nThe Fearless Four – pioneer rap group\nDoug E. Fresh – ‘80s rapper, runs a waffle house in Harlem\nSpoonie Gee – pioneer rapper\nCharles Hamilton – rapper\nIlacoin – hip hop artist, creator of the “Pause” game\nFreddie Jackson – singer\nJim Jones (rapper) – rapper (co-CEO of Diplomat Records) (Dipset)\nKelis – R&B singer and songwriter\nBig L – rapper (deceased)\nPuff Daddy – rapper, businessman, founder of Bad Boy Records\nDarlene Lewis – writer, lyricist, model, first female producer; host of hip-hop music video talk shows circa 1984–present\nFreekey Zekey – rapper (owner, CEO of 730 Dips Records)\nImmortal Technique – rapper\nKurtis Blow – rapper\nLil Mama – rapper; judge of America’s Best Dance Crew\nLoaded Lux – battle rapper\nBiz Markie – rapper, disc jockey owns a Waffle House\nMase – rapper\nJae Millz – rapper\nMurda Mook – battle rapper (member of Dot Mob)\nP-Star – rapper, singer, actress\nEbony Haith – America’s Next Top Model contestant, model\nTeddy Riley – producer, artist\nCarl Hancock Rux – writer, performer\nSheena Sakai – America’s Next Top Model contestant, model\nIsabel Sanford – actor; co-star of The Jeffersons\nJuelz Santana – rapper (owner, CEO of Skull Gang Records)\nBre Scullark – America’s Next Top Model contestant, model\nTupac Shakur – rapper, actor, poet (deceased)\nSmoke DZA – rapper\nDani Stevenson – singer\nKeith Sweat – singer\nTeyana Taylor – singer and rapper signed to Kanye West’s G.O.O.D. Music label\nTreacherous Three – old-school rap group\nT-Rex – battle rapper (member Of Dot Mob)\nVado – rapper (We The Best Records)\nBilly Dee Williams – actor\nJR Writer – rapper (Dipset member)\nDave East – rapper (Mass Appeal Records)", "annotation_id": "9067744", "url": "https://genius.com/9067744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Uzi Gang", "line": "If the bitch ain’t on me, she on Ferg Ask them niggas who they want Who they want?", "vault_lines": ["If the bitch ain't on me, she on Ferg"], "meaning": "This marks the third collaboration between Lil Uzi and the A$AP Mob,\n\nWe want A$AP Uzi!\n\nMarty Baller, who is featured on this track, just recently became part of the Mob himself: after years of collaboration, Marty was credited as “A$AP Marty” on the cover of “I Don’t Care.”", "annotation_id": "9036905", "url": "https://genius.com/9036905", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Uzi Gang", "line": "Watch that Uzi go ”blatt!”, lay him flat on his back With the pump, have an asthma attack They ain’t want to do that", "vault_lines": ["With the pump, have an asthma attack"], "meaning": "When Marty shoots at you with an uzi, it could cause an asthma attack, which would be even worse when he gets his pump shotgun.\n\nThis also refers to Ferg’s song “Didn’t Want To Do That,” specifically this line.", "annotation_id": "9036897", "url": "https://genius.com/9036897", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Uzi Gang", "line": "Marty Baller a mac I’ma talk about things that go down in the trap You can talk about rap, how I cooked up a flow Watch it rock while I’m spitting this crack", "vault_lines": ["Marty Baller a mac"], "meaning": "“Mac” is slang for pimp, can also stand for Mastered the Art of Communication.\n\nA trap house is a place where drugs are made and sold—Marty compares his flow to the process of cooking cocaine into crack.", "annotation_id": "9036262", "url": "https://genius.com/9036262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
