{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Unapologetic (Strike a Pose)", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-unapologetic-strike-a-pose-lyrics", "genius_title": "Unapologetic (Strike a Pose)", "genius_id": 11656927, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "And you might think she’s outstandin’", "vault_lines": ["And you might think she's outstandin'"], "meaning": "When The Weeknd says, “And you might think she’s outstanding,” it can be read as a commentary on first impressions, how people often fixate on someone’s looks or surface charm and mistake that immediate attraction for something deeper. In the context of an album centered on heartbreak, the line suggests that although this woman appears exceptional at first glance, that allure masks deeper issues. She may be “outstanding” in appearance or presence, but ultimately damaging within a relationship.", "annotation_id": "38554544", "url": "https://genius.com/38554544", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "You keep listenin’ to your mad friends", "vault_lines": ["You keep listenin' to your mad friends"], "meaning": "Uzi is basically saying a girl keeps listening to her friends who are jealous that she’s dating a celebrity", "annotation_id": "26630139", "url": "https://genius.com/26630139", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Pull up every which way in foreign cars", "vault_lines": ["Pull up every which way in foreign cars"], "meaning": "Here, Uzi references Kanye West’s “Hell of a life” from his 2010 album “My Beautiful Dark twisted Fantasy”:\n\nI think I just fell in love with a pornstar\nTurn the camera on, she a born star\nTurn the corners in a foreign car", "annotation_id": "22710045", "url": "https://genius.com/22710045", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "I’m unfazed (Woah), I’m unfazed (Woah) I’m unfazed (Woah), I’m unfazed (Woah) I’m unfazed, I’m unfazed I’m unfazed, I’m unfazed I’m unfazed, ooh, yeah (Woah), I’m unfazed, ooh yeah (Woah) I’m unfazed, ooh yeah (Woah), I’m unfazed (Woah, yeah, woah) I’m unfazed (Woah, yeah), I’m unfazed (Woah, yeah) I’m unfazed (Oh, yeah), I’m unfazed (Yeah, oh, woah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm unfazed (Woah), I'm unfazed (Woah)"], "meaning": "Throughout the song’s chorus, Abel effectively reiterates a simple message: he is not not disconcerted or perturbed by the distractions that face him on the road to success. Instead, he is able to enjoy himself responsibly, indulging in vices, such as drugs and women, whilst keeping his eyes on the ultimate prize.", "annotation_id": "21607667", "url": "https://genius.com/21607667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "I took his girl, yeah that’s Bogart", "vault_lines": ["I took his girl, yeah that's Bogart"], "meaning": "Uzi took his girl, because he doesn’t share; to “Bogart” means to selfishly keep something.\n\nThis is also a reference to Humphrey Bogart, who notoriously stole Ilsa from her husband as Rick Blaine In Casablanca.", "annotation_id": "12595847", "url": "https://genius.com/12595847", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Make that girl go through practice", "vault_lines": ["Make that girl go through practice"], "meaning": "This line hints to Abel’s song “Initiation,” in which he describes the process a girl has to go through to be with him. It involves staying up all night, doing drugs, drinking, and having sex.\n\nThis line also hints at the next one, where Abel compares his drug use to three consecutive goals. Football players practice quite extensively for their matches, so Abel makes his girl do the same, except for a different type of match.", "annotation_id": "12593964", "url": "https://genius.com/12593964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "I make it rain, you can have it (Woah) I make it disappear like magic (Woah) I, I met that girl right at Magic", "vault_lines": ["I make it rain, you can have it (Woah)"], "meaning": "“Making it rain” is the action of throwing your money over or at someone, one by one, creating a raining effect of bills. This is a common way to tip dancers at strip clubs.\n\nUzi is referring to “Magic City” a strip club in Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "12586842", "url": "https://genius.com/12586842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Yeah, it’s Starboy and a born star", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, it's Starboy and a born star"], "meaning": "Uzi is referring to The Weeknd as “Starboy” as he deemed himself in the title track of his latest album of the same name.\n\nLil Uzi has also claimed in an interview with noisey: “I’m legit a rock star”.", "annotation_id": "12585330", "url": "https://genius.com/12585330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "These models ’bout to get ratchet (Ooh yeah) These models ’bout to get ratchet Give a fuck about what a source say Don’t attach me to your name A-All they wanted was more fame All they wanted was more fame", "vault_lines": ["These models 'bout to get ratchet (Ooh yeah)"], "meaning": "In July 2017, a source for Irish model Ava Van Rose revealed that she and The Weeknd had spent time together before the singer’s appearance at the Longitude Festival in Dublin. After they met, he gave her a pass to see him at the festival.\n\nShe then took to Instagram, revealing that she and The Weeknd had sex that same night in a series of since-deleted posts. It turns out Van Rose had lied about sleeping with him, rather, she actually slept with one of his friends.\n\nIn these lines, Abel takes a jab at Van Rose, explaining that people will do anything to obtain the fame associated with his name.", "annotation_id": "12584060", "url": "https://genius.com/12584060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Turn that girl into a bad bitch Turn that girl into a savage", "vault_lines": ["Turn that girl into a bad bitch"], "meaning": "The girl in question is probably The Weeknd’s current girlfriend Selena Gomez, who has traditionally had a clean, “girl next door” image.", "annotation_id": "12581095", "url": "https://genius.com/12581095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "And you were always a distraction It was never gonna last, and they will always be the past", "vault_lines": ["And you were always a distraction"], "meaning": "The Weeknd might possibly be talking about a previous girlfriend. He dated Bella Hadid before ending things with her during the final weeks before the release of Starboy.", "annotation_id": "12581084", "url": "https://genius.com/12581084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Take three Xannies like a hat trick Take another pill for that magic", "vault_lines": ["Take three Xannies like a hat trick"], "meaning": "In sports such as football or hockey, a hat-trick occurs when a player scores three goals in a single game. Abel compares his Xanax usage to this.\n\nThe second line plays off the literal interpretation of “hat trick,” which is to pull a rabbit out of a hat. This emphasizes that he enjoys taking them so much he takes another in order to get fucked up and elevate his high to the next level. Magic is also a slang for the feeling one undergoes while on ecstasy.\n\nWhen I’m fucked up, that’s the real me, babe\n― The Weeknd – “The Hills”", "annotation_id": "12580434", "url": "https://genius.com/12580434", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UnFazed", "line": "Countin’ Washingtons, this Gilbert Arenas (That’s Arenas)", "vault_lines": ["Countin' Washingtons, this Gilbert Arenas (That's Arenas)"], "meaning": "Uzi is saying that he is getting rich and selling out his live arena shows.\n\nHe references Gilbert Arenas, a professional basketball player who played with the Washington Wizards from 2003 to 2010. Gilbert Arena’s jersey number was 0, Uzi is saying he’s counting up the 0’s.", "annotation_id": "12580415", "url": "https://genius.com/12580415", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
