{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UFO", "line": "She think that I dated her, but she only date me (Hahaha)", "vault_lines": ["She think that I dated her, but she only date me (Hahaha)"], "meaning": "Uzi is saying that he never dated the girl he was with as he didn’t consider her as something special, but the girl saw Uzi as someone significant.", "annotation_id": "37937693", "url": "https://genius.com/37937693", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UFO", "line": "I ain’t got no durag on but you know Uzi wavy", "vault_lines": ["I ain't got no durag on but you know Uzi wavy"], "meaning": "Durags are worn to preserve waves, a common hairstyle. Uzi is saying that even though he doesn’t have a durag on, everyone knows he’s wavy. (Slang for cool)", "annotation_id": "37937682", "url": "https://genius.com/37937682", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UFO", "line": "I can’t go 392, bitch, I’m a demon", "vault_lines": ["I can't go 392, bitch, I'm a demon"], "meaning": "392 refers to a Dodge Challenger 392, which is a slightly sportier model than the base model. By “demon”, Uzi refers to the limited model of Dodge Challengers, known as the Dodge Challenger Demon, which is far more powerful than all other models.", "annotation_id": "37935578", "url": "https://genius.com/37935578", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "UFO", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-ufo-lyrics", "genius_title": "UFO", "genius_id": 5932417, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "Hunnid bands now Lil Uzi be the target (Target, target)", "vault_lines": ["Hunnid bands now Lil Uzi be the target (Target, target)"], "meaning": "Band is a slang term for $1000, with one “band” being 10 hundred dollar bills fastened by a rubber band.\n\n\n\nIn the latter part of the line, Uzi is referring to verbal and physical threats he has received since his career took off, such as various diss tracks about him like Rich the Kid’s “Dead Friends” and Reese’s “180 Secs”.", "annotation_id": "14794133", "url": "https://genius.com/14794133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "’Cause my Uzi hold a 100 round cartridge", "vault_lines": ["'Cause my Uzi hold a 100 round cartridge"], "meaning": "The Uzi is a renowned Israeli submachine gun designed in the late 1940s by Major Uziel Gal, and is known for its compact size but high fire rate. This firearm is the namesake in which Lil Uzi Vert gained part of his rap identity from.\n\nThe self-proclaimed rockstar even recently worked with well known jeweler Elliot Avianne on a diamond Uzi chain that goes jointly with his rap name.", "annotation_id": "14791819", "url": "https://genius.com/14791819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "I got Glock, I got a drum on the Tommy (I do, I do)", "vault_lines": ["I got Glock, I got a drum on the Tommy (I do, I do)"], "meaning": "Glock is an esteemed Austrian firearms company known for their imposing pistols.\n\n\n\nThe world-renowned Thompson submachine gun was invented by John Browning in 1918. Known for its tremendous fire rate, the weapon earned the nickname “Annihilator”, and was primarily used in World War ll.  Although the Thompson normally held a 30-round stick clip, it could be fitted with a 100-round drum magazine fire maximum firing capability.\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcR8XIk0zKtCITqdF2kTk4SmKn4r_7GEy7axPndfyLerwqdhwCjNbA", "annotation_id": "14788556", "url": "https://genius.com/14788556", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "And my boxers be from Tommy (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["And my boxers be from Tommy (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi’s stunting in a pair of Tommy Hilfiger Boxers – it’s prices range anywhere from 20 to 40 USD. Tommy Hilfiger is an American fashion designer best known for founding the Tommy Hilfiger Corporation in 1985, which manufactures an array of apparel for men, women, and children.", "annotation_id": "8338090", "url": "https://genius.com/8338090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "She love a nigga ‘cause I’m flexin’ (My nigga, my nigga) Yeah, I flex, yeah I flex and I’m finessin’ (My nigga, my nigga)", "vault_lines": ["She love a nigga 'cause I'm flexin' (My nigga, my nigga)"], "meaning": "Flexin' is a term that mean to show off what you have in a boastful fashion. This girl loves Uzi because of his materialistic goods and such. Finessin' is slang for getting something (usually money) by doing the bare minimum of which is required to obtain said thing. It also means to get the most out of anything.", "annotation_id": "8323507", "url": "https://genius.com/8323507", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "U.Z.I", "line": "I’m grilled up like I’m from Texas (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm grilled up like I'm from Texas (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Texas has a reputation of popularizing grills, especially Houston where many Southern rappers in the 2000s spurred a nationwide grill trend. Many rappers still embrace this look such as RiFF RAFF and Paul Wall. You can see Uzi rocking a pair of diamond fronts in the picture below.", "annotation_id": "8300597", "url": "https://genius.com/8300597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
