{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Time’s up, I check my watch every hour", "vault_lines": ["Time's up, I check my watch every hour"], "meaning": "Uzi may be checking his watch every hour to avoid wasting time and to always stay ahead. Saying “time’s up” may be him telling his competition that they have run out of chances and time, and that he is now on top. It could also mean that the waiting period is over and that it is finally Uzi’s time to shine.", "annotation_id": "40747782", "url": "https://genius.com/40747782", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Time’s up, I check my watch every hour", "vault_lines": ["Time's up, I check my watch every hour"], "meaning": "Uzi may be checking his watch every hour to avoid wasting time and to always stay ahead. Saying “time’s up” may be him telling his competition that they have run out of chances and time, and that he is now on top. It could also mean that the waiting period is over and that it is finally Uzi’s time to shine.", "annotation_id": "40747720", "url": "https://genius.com/40747720", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah)"], "meaning": "yeah", "annotation_id": "36976465", "url": "https://genius.com/36976465", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "[Intro: Lil Uzi Vert & Kesha Lee]", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert begins this hotly anticipated album by letting us know he’s another another level. The piano notes and heart beat sounds sample Dragonball Z’s Super Saiyan transformation music. His roar, similar as Saiyans do when they reach a new level, marks Uzi’s ascention, and start of Luv Is RAGE 2®😔🔥", "annotation_id": "29287731", "url": "https://genius.com/29287731", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Lil Uzi Vert", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah)"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "22333971", "url": "https://genius.com/22333971", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Look for your bitch, you can’t find her I was the one right behind her (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Look for your bitch, you can't find her"], "meaning": "Uzi is suggesting that he took a persons girlfriend from them and ran off with her.", "annotation_id": "22080329", "url": "https://genius.com/22080329", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "I can’t fuck her, she a minor (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["I can't fuck her, she a minor (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Uzi seems to have a thing for young girls (“young enough to fuck on your niece”—Hi Roller, etc) but this line just clarifies he won’t go as far as to have sex with someone under the legal age of consent (which varies from 15-18) given that he’s now 24 and no longer young enough to legally meet age buffers with underage girls.\n\nBecause….. morals? (Gross either way)", "annotation_id": "12651962", "url": "https://genius.com/12651962", "state": "accepted", "votes": 128, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Two", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah)"], "meaning": "This is simply a tribute back to title of the album, Luv is Rage 2 and the name of the song itself.\n\n\n\nIn the cover art, Uzi also holds up 2 fingers to signify the milestone this album marks in his life as an artist.", "annotation_id": "12763406", "url": "https://genius.com/12763406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "And I ain’t gon’ lie, I got money and the power I ain’t gon’ lie, I got money and the power (Yeah) I ain’t gon’ lie, I got money and the power (Woah) I ain’t gon’ lie (Chee) I ain’t gon’ lie", "vault_lines": ["And I ain't gon' lie, I got money and the power"], "meaning": "Here, Uzi is acknowledging the level of fame and success that he has already reached in his young career. He then reaffirms this statement, either to convince himself that his newfound stardom is real or to make sure his detractors know how much he has succeeded.\n\nHe could also be referring to a scene from the 1983 film Scarface:\n\nIn this country, you gotta make the money first. Then when you get the money, you get the power. Then when you get the power, then you get the women.", "annotation_id": "12666423", "url": "https://genius.com/12666423", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "I will not give these bitches this dick, let them top it (Oh yeah) Woah, we’re ending that topic", "vault_lines": ["I will not give these bitches this dick, let them top it (Oh yeah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi doesn’t want to work and engage in sexual intercourse; he’d rather have oral sex be performed. Getting girls to give oral sex is a very common thing among the community. It is fast and essentially they’re not “wasting” their dick on the girl but still receiving pleasure through quick, minimal engagement with the girl.", "annotation_id": "12640721", "url": "https://genius.com/12640721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "In the industry with Dickies all on my pop shit (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["In the industry with Dickies all on my pop shit (Hey)"], "meaning": "Uzi makes reference to the late hiphop legend, Tupac Amaru Shakur’s famous pair of Dickies dungarees.", "annotation_id": "12633742", "url": "https://genius.com/12633742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "She saw me up in a picture, I thought they cropped it (Oh my God) Damn, she think I popped it (Oh my God)", "vault_lines": ["She saw me up in a picture, I thought they cropped it (Oh my God)"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Uzi getting caught with someone who he shouldn’t be with, most likely a side-chick. He thought he was cropped out of the picture and had nothing to worry about.\nAs a result, his main chick thinks that he had sex with her, a topic Uzi wants nothing to do with.", "annotation_id": "12622780", "url": "https://genius.com/12622780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "The reason I got all these bitches and got all these diamonds I can’t make my mind up (Chee) Mind up, she gave me head, gave that mind up", "vault_lines": ["The reason I got all these bitches and got all these diamonds"], "meaning": "While Uzi can’t “make his mind up” on which of his ladies he’ll choose to hit up or which diamonds he’ll rock, his girl gives “that mind up” when she gives him oral sex, a play on words with the slang term “head”.\n\nUzi is notorious for using “head” wordplay, as he’s used it on tracks such as “Erase Your Social”, “The Way Life Goes”, and “Feelings Mutual”.", "annotation_id": "12617236", "url": "https://genius.com/12617236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Tried to run off with the swag, I put ’em in pocket (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Tried to run off with the swag, I put 'em in pocket (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi has always been one to call out imitators. Similarly to theme of his Playboi Carti feature, “*wokeuplikethis”, he again confronts imitators of his distinct style in this line.\n\nThe phrase to be “out of pocket” means that one is getting out of control and merging into other lanes that they have no business being in. Uzi claims that he puts imitators back in check.", "annotation_id": "12587128", "url": "https://genius.com/12587128", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "Yeah, the famous life, it’ll eat you up alive It’s a game, had to put my feelings to the side (Put ’em to the side, ayy) Yeah, the famous life, it’ll eat you up alive It’s a game, had to put my feelings to the side", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the famous life, it'll eat you up alive"], "meaning": "In an interview with The FADER, Uzi relates his issues with his newfound fame:\n\nThis rap shit, I hate it…You wanna know what the curse is? I gotta take care of my family. That’s the curse right there. I gotta take care of my whole family. That’s why I can’t stop. If I ain’t have to take care of nobody, best believe I’d be regular as fuck.\n\nIn his interview with Zane Lowe on Beats 1 Radio, Uzi said he’s “not really with it,” when referring to fame, and says he truly does not like being famous.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/nN7tGEqUFJ8?t=8m56s", "annotation_id": "12586797", "url": "https://genius.com/12586797", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "’Cause you know, I’m the one (Yeah) Yes, I’m the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah) And you know, I changed a lot of you niggas In a matter of months, I raised a lot of you niggas (It’s true)", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm the one that really started all this (GOAT, yeah)"], "meaning": "In the final lines of the interlude, Uzi “sends a message” to rappers that tend to follow his style in music and fashion. He claims that his recent popularity as a result of Lil Uzi Vert vs. The World and The Perfect LUV Tape caused a lot of young rappers to follow his path in a short amount of time.\n\nUzi has said something similar in his verse on the first 2016 XXL cypher and on Migos' most popular hit, “Bad and Boujee”.\n\nAyy, wait, these niggas watchin'\nI swear to God they be my clones", "annotation_id": "12586369", "url": "https://genius.com/12586369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "And I just wanna let you know (Let you know) I really, really wanna let you know That I really don’t give a fuck what nobody say about me (I don’t)", "vault_lines": ["And I just wanna let you know (Let you know)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi has reached a point in his career where he doesn’t have to worry about the moves that other rappers are making or the hate they may be sending his way.\n\nA prime example of this is when Kodak Black hopped on Instagram live and said “I don’t even listen to Lil Uzi… these niggas dick in the booty”. Soon later Lil Uzi was asked about how he felt about this and he just shrugged and laughed.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IPE4FLMX7ZQ\n\nNow a days you have a lot of artists stacking their albums with big features to get streams but Lil Uzi has made a name for himself mainly off of songs with no features.", "annotation_id": "12585920", "url": "https://genius.com/12585920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "line": "GOAT (Yeah) That’s true Yeah Uzi? Uzi? Not again Uzi, wake your ass up", "vault_lines": ["Uzi? Uzi? Not again"], "meaning": "This is the voice of Uzi’s Engineer, Kesha Lee, playing the part of Brittany Byrd, Uzi’s ex-girlfriend. It mirrors part of the intro to “7AM,” the fourth song on Uzi’s 2015 mixtape Luv Is Rage:\n\nUzi, wake your ass up\n\n(G.O.A.T. translates to Greatest Of All Time)", "annotation_id": "12580111", "url": "https://genius.com/12580111", "state": "accepted", "votes": 241, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two®", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-two-lyrics", "genius_title": "Two®", "genius_id": 3209316, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Two Tone", "line": "Can’t kill my chakras (Never) I won’t smoke this shit if you don’t roll it proper Never went to high school, I went to school high", "vault_lines": ["I won't smoke this shit if you don't roll it proper"], "meaning": "Could be paying homage too Brooklyn Super group Pro Era. They were all about chakra flows & energy. The group had a song High School High and the hook was the same.\n\nR.I.P. Capital STEEZ", "annotation_id": "23850793", "url": "https://genius.com/23850793", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
