{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Diamonds drippin’, they so wet (Drip, drip), I gotta wipe my jewels, ayy (Ayy, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds drippin', they so wet (Drip, drip), I gotta wipe my jewels, ayy (Ayy, ayy)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is making a double entendre with the word “drippin.”\n\n On one level, his diamonds are “dripping,” meaning they shine so much they seem wet. On another level, “drip” is rap slang for having expensive style and luxury. The next line, “they so wet, I gotta wipe my jewels,” reinforces both meanings, making it a clever wordplay about his jewelry and his lavish lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "40909856", "url": "https://genius.com/40909856", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Never put it in her butt, ayy (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Hit the bitch all on her back, ayy (Yeah), never put it in her butt, ayy (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Wise words from Lil Uzi Vert.", "annotation_id": "28669462", "url": "https://genius.com/28669462", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Jump in the crowd at my show, fucked the bitch in the front row", "vault_lines": ["Jump in the crowd at my show, fucked the bitch in the front row"], "meaning": "Uzi always goes crazy at his performances, which includes crowd surfing, where the performer jumps into the crowd and the audience carries him.\n\nHe also brags he already had sex with a groupie, one of the girls in the front row at his concert.\n\nLil Uzi’s stage tactics have included larger stage dives off of various platforms at concerts.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/861642591611355136", "annotation_id": "9623503", "url": "https://genius.com/9623503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "I’m gonna knuck if I buck (Buck)", "vault_lines": ["I'm gonna knuck if I buck (Buck)"], "meaning": "I first heard that song when I was in Virginia when I was a kid. I didn’t know what it was. I was playing Streets, the basketball game, at one of my family members' crib when I heard it, and ever since then I was rocking with Crime Mob.", "annotation_id": "8580505", "url": "https://genius.com/8580505", "state": "verified", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Remember that bitch ain’t want fuck me Now that bitch wanna just fuck me Remember that bitch said I’m dusty (Yeah) Look at that ho, like, “You ugly” (Yeah), ayy", "vault_lines": ["Remember that bitch ain't want fuck me"], "meaning": "It’s a blessing and a curse. They didn’t fuck with me, but now they fuck with me. When I say stuff like that, that’s a real line. There’s girls that just played me before and now they’re all in my DMs and shit, on my dick.", "annotation_id": "8580491", "url": "https://genius.com/8580491", "state": "verified", "votes": 248, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "First I drop my top, ayy (Ayy), then I swerve my coupe, ayy (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["First I drop my top, ayy (Ayy), then I swerve my coupe, ayy (Ayy)"], "meaning": "The hook actually came from a Lil B song called Wonton Soup, and I just changed the flow of it and changed the words. He blesses me on Twitter because I asked him – I didn’t want the Based God Curse.\n\nI drive different cars everywhere I go. You can see em on my Instagram. My favorite is the Porsche 911. Drop top.", "annotation_id": "8580375", "url": "https://genius.com/8580375", "state": "verified", "votes": 390, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Brittany turned me to a slut (Slut) Brittany turned me to a slut (Yeah) Brittany turned me to a slut (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Brittany turned me to a slut (Slut)"], "meaning": "Brittney played with my emotions at the time and I didn’t know what to do – so I was acting all crazy and doing rockstar stuff.", "annotation_id": "8580350", "url": "https://genius.com/8580350", "state": "verified", "votes": 524, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Who the fuck are you? Ayy Who the fuck are you? Ayy Who the fuck are you—", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck are you? Ayy"], "meaning": "This song is about flexing on everybody.", "annotation_id": "8580345", "url": "https://genius.com/8580345", "state": "verified", "votes": 480, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Cannon, Cannon went crazy", "vault_lines": ["Cannon, Cannon went crazy"], "meaning": "Cannon’s like a legend in the game—he’s made beats for Jay Z and stuff. He heard my song on Philadelphia radio and said he was gonna fly me to Atlanta. And he did.\n\nIt was crazy. He made the beat on the spot. I got real high—I took a Xanny bar, smoked some weed, went in the booth and made the song without even thinking about it.", "annotation_id": "8580334", "url": "https://genius.com/8580334", "state": "verified", "votes": 263, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "I just be smokin’ the dope (Yeah), Skeme, he be smokin’ the clove (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I just be smokin' the dope (Yeah), Skeme, he be smokin' the clove (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi smokes weed, and Skeme—rapper from Inglewood, California—smokes clove cigarillos. The two rappers have collaborated on Don Cannon’s Big Money (C4 Remix) and on Skeme’s “The Man”", "annotation_id": "8554922", "url": "https://genius.com/8554922", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "[Chorus]", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck are you? Ayy"], "meaning": "This is the kind of repetition that happens throughout this track—also the kind of repetition you might see on a Mike Jones track. Lil Uzi Vert lists him (and his tendency to repeat lines) in an XXL interview:\n\n“…It was the repetitive stuff with Mike Jones when he would give out his number and I also like his style.”", "annotation_id": "8550037", "url": "https://genius.com/8550037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Treez, what up Treez? Ayy, ayy, ayy, ayy, uh Hotel party for these bad hoes For these bad hoes, that trip, haha Ayy, ayy, oh", "vault_lines": ["Treez, what up Treez?"], "meaning": "Treez Lowkey is a rapper from Virginia whose song “HOETEL” was sampled by Don Cannon for “Top,” Lil Uzi gives him a shout out and sings the hook of “HOETEL” as tribute.", "annotation_id": "8546319", "url": "https://genius.com/8546319", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Why you walk so cool? (Cool, cool, cool) Ayy, thousand dollar shoes, ayy (Shoes) Hunnid on my jewels, ayy, I got all these groupies (Groupies)", "vault_lines": ["Why you walk so cool? (Cool, cool, cool) Ayy, thousand dollar shoes, ayy (Shoes)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi loves his diamond jewelry, and so do his female fans. He’s willing to spend thousands of dollars on his diamonds just to show off his wealth.\n\nPoor guys should stop trying to show of their footwear; Uzi is walking in style with his expensive shoes, he’s been seen wearing designer Ronnie Fieg x Fracap Boots, Yeezy 950 boots, and more!", "annotation_id": "8379057", "url": "https://genius.com/8379057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Counting all these bands, ayy (Ayy), who the fuck are you? Ayy (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Counting all these bands, ayy (Ayy), who the fuck are you? Ayy (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Even though Lil Uzi’s been on the come up, making more money, he’s aware that his relationship with rap is about more than just money. In an interview with Complex, he says:\n\n“It’s got to be a bit more than just money. So, it’s kind of changing for me a lot now.”", "annotation_id": "8095226", "url": "https://genius.com/8095226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Fuck bitches in twos, ayy, fuck bitches in twos, ayy (Twos, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck bitches in twos, ayy, fuck bitches in twos, ayy (Twos, ayy)"], "meaning": "Uzi doesn’t care if his girls are related, he’ll still have sex with them—Future brags about about this in “Real Sisters”:\n\nOh, that’s your best friend? I’m tryna fuck her with you\nFirst met the bitch, they said they real sisters\nI don’t give a fuck if they was real sisters", "annotation_id": "8083524", "url": "https://genius.com/8083524", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "My brother whippin’ the stove (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["My brother whippin' the stove (Yeah)"], "meaning": "His brother is cooking up crack, a process that involves a lot of whipping over a stove.", "annotation_id": "8083425", "url": "https://genius.com/8083425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "I feel like I’m Dro, ayy, car ain’t got no roof, ayy", "vault_lines": ["I feel like I'm Dro, ayy, car ain't got no roof, ayy"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Atlanta rapper Young Dro’s “We In Da City.”\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vuUIoPVRpmk", "annotation_id": "8083366", "url": "https://genius.com/8083366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "Sometimes Fear of God, ayy Saint Laurent the boots, ayy (Saint)", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes Fear of God, ayy"], "meaning": "Uzi is a big fan of high-end fashion brands. Here he is mentioning well known brands “Fear of God” and “Yves Saint Laurent”, which are also worn by artists such as Kanye West and The Weeknd.\n\n\n\nLil Uzi tweeted a picture wearing the fit, Fear of God Skinny Jeans and Saint Laurent Boots:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/LILUZIVERT/status/741027238926131204", "annotation_id": "8083338", "url": "https://genius.com/8083338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Top", "line": "You is not gon’ do a thing, with my squad like Wu-Tang, ayy (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You is not gon' do a thing, with my squad like Wu-Tang, ayy (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The legendary Wu-Tang Clan is made up of 10 close-nit members, and as you know, the Wu-Tang Clan ain’t nothin' to fuck with!\n\nYou don’t want to mess with Uzi and his crew.", "annotation_id": "8083249", "url": "https://genius.com/8083249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
