{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "Bitch, I’m the Birdman, GTV", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm the Birdman, GTV"], "meaning": "Uzi says he is Birdman, an older rap icon and one who is considered to be close to rapper Young Thug, Uzis frequent collaborator, friend and who’s incarceration, prompted Uzi to publicly show support for his release and inspired Uzi to make Barter 16. Birdman also shows up earlier in the album on the song RIP Ms Connie. GTV or Grand Touring Vodka is a brand of liquor that Birdman owns.", "annotation_id": "35772833", "url": "https://genius.com/35772833", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "I got on Akiko, the boot with the double strap, no, this is not no Palladium", "vault_lines": ["I got on Akiko, the boot with the double strap, no, this is not no Palladium"], "meaning": "Uzi shows love for avant garde fashion, by bragging about boots and rejecting the idea that they might be palladium; a less obscure and cheaper brand.", "annotation_id": "35772800", "url": "https://genius.com/35772800", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "Tattoos, that’s all on my body, it’s only one piece, so this shit a graffiti (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Tattoos, that's all on my body, it's only one piece, so this shit a graffiti (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi is known for their large collection of body and face tattoos. a year prior to this recording, Uzi also got a massive full chest and back cover up tattoo done by the highly specialized tattoo artist Ganga. the tattoo reportedly costed over six figures and a took a total of 16 hours, which was broken up into two 8 hour sessions. additionally around pink tape they got a forehead cover up. these coverups could contribute to the analogy, as uzi states their body is one piece. in graffiti when an object runs out of space some graffiti artists may paint over older works, just as uzi might tattoo over older tattoos as space runs out on their body.\n\nhttps://www.complex.com/style/a/lei-takanashi/ganga-lil-uzi-vert-tattoo-interview", "annotation_id": "35772620", "url": "https://genius.com/35772620", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "Racks on my opps head, they know [?] first, so they throw in a treaty (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Racks on my opps head, they know [?] first, so they throw in a treaty (Yeah)"], "meaning": "uzi puts out an expensive bounty on an enemy’s head. when they find out they cower, and seek peace to protect their own life. this line verifies that uzi holds a high rank in the streets, while also showing that uzi is so rich that they just throw large amounts of money around as if it were nothing.", "annotation_id": "35772481", "url": "https://genius.com/35772481", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "Everytime I wear the skinny jeans, I got the thigh pads (Pads, racks, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Everytime I wear the skinny jeans, I got the thigh pads (Pads, racks, woo)"], "meaning": "uzi is known for their fashion, but the line also references the fact the uzi has a lot of money (a theme brought up frequently in uzi’s music), so much so that when they wear skinny jeans the amount of money they carry in their pockets makes it look like as if uzi were wearing thigh pads. this is confirmed by the ‘racks’ adlib.", "annotation_id": "35772431", "url": "https://genius.com/35772431", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Thigh Pads", "line": "Got a old cougar bitch, I just be pleading to her, just like, “Please don’t molest me”", "vault_lines": ["Got a old cougar bitch, I just be pleading to her, just like, \"Please don't molest me\""], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert states that he is in a sexual relationship with an older woman who purchases him luxury items, also known as a cougar. Due to their age difference, he pleads with her to not molest him, suggesting that he is a victim.", "annotation_id": "32961678", "url": "https://genius.com/32961678", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
