{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "The End Is Near", "line": "Never did heroin but Preston swagged my calves up (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Never did heroin but Preston swagged my calves up (Uh)"], "meaning": "Uzi is making a play on words about the drug heroin & the designer Heron Preston, who Uzi is friends with.\nUzi was photographed with Virgil Abloh and Heron Preston which was later used as the cover for his 2016 SoundCloud exclusive “Buy It” (although the latter was cropped out).\n\n3 years after this song was recorded Uzi modeled for Heron Preston’s line with Calvin Klein.", "annotation_id": "30075658", "url": "https://genius.com/30075658", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "The End Is Near", "line": "Oogie Mane", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, baby, grab your titties, hold your ass up (Oh, yeah)"], "meaning": "Oogie Mane is a Philadelphia producer in the collective Working on Dying, he produced this song as well as Brandon Finessin who is also in the same collective.", "annotation_id": "29396292", "url": "https://genius.com/29396292", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "The End Is Near", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-the-end-is-near-lyrics", "genius_title": "The End Is Near", "genius_id": 8585859, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "The End", "line": "You feel blue (Blue), have a pink day", "vault_lines": ["You feel blue (Blue), have a pink day"], "meaning": "Uzi may be saying that if you feel unhappy, you should try to have a day full of love and compassion regardless.\n\nThis line may be referencing “Endless Fashion” from earlier in the album, which interpolates the instrumental of Eiffel 65’s “Blue (Da Ba Dee),” which is about an alien named Zorotl, who is both literally blue-skinned and also depressed.\n\nPink Tape was released a week after National Pink Day, observed on June 23. The day is a celebration of the color pink and everything it represents; particularly love and compassion.\n\nAdditionally, the color blue is widely seen as an unhappy color, being associated with sadness, poor weather, and a variety of other things, explaining why people use the term “feeling blue.”", "annotation_id": "28938592", "url": "https://genius.com/28938592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "The End", "line": "I’m not from this earth, I’m from outer space I landed here just to drop the Pink Tape", "vault_lines": ["I'm not from this earth, I'm from outer spacе"], "meaning": "Uzi calls back to their last album Eternal Atake. The cover appears to be set on the moon, showing the earth with a UFO hovering above it.\n\n\n\nThey made direct references to outer space on multiple songs from the original and deluxe versions, starting with the intro of “Venetia.”\n\nLil Uzi Vert, to be exact (Oh)\nAnd I’m not from earth, I’m from outer space (Woah, let’s go)\nAnd I’m different (Uh), I’m wavy\nI’m somewhere I’m not even ‘posed to be ('Posed to be), yeah", "annotation_id": "28932967", "url": "https://genius.com/28932967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
