{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Four years, I ain’t touch no chicken", "vault_lines": ["Four years, I ain't touch no chicken"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi is a pescatarian and only eats fish.\n\n“Chicken” is a play off the previous line saying “can’t wife no bird\"", "annotation_id": "22272224", "url": "https://genius.com/22272224", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Lucien on my vision, that’s the only thing that’s tran (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Lucien on my vision, that's the only thing that's tran (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Lucien Carr was an author and member of the Beat Generation in the 1940s. Carr developed what he called the “New Vision”, a thesis recycled from emersonian transcendentalism- using some of the philosophical movements ideals.\n\nWhen Uzi says “Lucien on my vision” he could also be referring to revel Lucien eyewear.", "annotation_id": "19221258", "url": "https://genius.com/19221258", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "My boys whip work ’til the white turn all tan (Tan)", "vault_lines": ["My boys whip work 'til the white turn all tan (Tan)"], "meaning": "“Whipping work” is a common phrase that alludes to the process of cooking cocaine into crack. During the process, the pure white colour of the cocaine transitions into a more opaque tan colour.", "annotation_id": "17027139", "url": "https://genius.com/17027139", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Put a pause on that, you still broke, you ain’t back (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Put a pause on that, you still broke, you ain't back (Yeah)"], "meaning": "To “pause” a sentence is using the word to clarify that what someone said was homosexual, but wasn’t meant to be that way on purpose. This follows up from the last line:\n\nJust like his bitch ass, that fuck nigga will get clapped", "annotation_id": "16924216", "url": "https://genius.com/16924216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "June and July cold just like December", "vault_lines": ["June and July cold just like December"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is saying that they have so much ice, another name for jewelry, that he causes the hot summer months to be as cold as the winter months, such as December.", "annotation_id": "16922425", "url": "https://genius.com/16922425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Balmain jeans, on the front got the zipper", "vault_lines": ["Balmain jeans, on the front got the zipper"], "meaning": "Balmain is a French luxury fashion house founded in 1945 by Pierre Balmain. Balmain is known for their jeans, which Uzi references in songs like “Team Rocket” and “All My Chains.” In this line, Uzi is talking about the biker jeans, which have two pockets in the front with zippers.\n\nHere, Uzi is seen wearing a pair of Balmain biker jeans:", "annotation_id": "16915695", "url": "https://genius.com/16915695", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "I can’t talk on the phone, think my shit is tapped (Hello?)", "vault_lines": ["I can't talk on the phone, think my shit is tapped (Hello?)"], "meaning": "“Phonetapping” or “wiretapping” refers to secretly fitting a special device to someone’s phone in order to listen to their phone conversations without being noticed. Due to their celebrity status, Uzi would be a target for phone taps, hence leading them to take caution. On their 2016 single, “Buy It”, they rap:\n\nThey keep hackin' my iPhone, ‘bout to get a Sidekick\n\nHowever, phone taps also refer to prank calls. Radio stations around the world and especially in the U.S. prank call listeners and/or celebrities for entertainment. Listen to Real 92.3’s Big Boy phone tap comedian Kevin Hart:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B2EH8eYExTk", "annotation_id": "16913637", "url": "https://genius.com/16913637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "No, check my DMs, found out she was a man (No, no, no) I can’t DM, never, ever again (No)", "vault_lines": ["No, check my DMs, found out she was a man (No, no, no)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert talks about finding out that the person they had been DMing (direct messaging) was a transgender woman, contrary to their preference as they state on the preceding line. To play it safe, Uzi vows to never DM on his social medias, to ensure that he doesn’t accidentally connect with transgender people again.\n\nFollowing the release of the song, Uzi received a ton of backlash on Twitter for the alleged transphobic nature of these lyrics, prompting many to “cancel” him.", "annotation_id": "16913560", "url": "https://genius.com/16913560", "state": "accepted", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Stand on my money, I’m tall like ceiling", "vault_lines": ["Stand on my money, I'm tall like ceiling"], "meaning": "A “center” (also known as a “big man”) is a position in a basketball team, which is usually played by the team’s tallest player. The average center’s height is almost 6'9'‘ feet or 2.10 meters.\n\nLil Uzi Vert is 5'4'‘ feet or 1.63 meters tall. To become 6'9'‘ feet, Uzi would need an additional 1'5’‘ feet or 0.47 meters.\n\nAs the thickness of a $100 bill is .0043 inches, Uzi would need to have at least 3954 $100 bills, totaling up to around $395,400 (that is if Uzi manages to stand upright on only 1 stack of 2.61'‘ by 6.14’‘ bills).\n\nManaging to accumulate this amount of cash should not be too big of a problem for Uzi, as their net worth is estimated to be at around $17 million as of mid-January 2019.\n\n\n\nUzi has described their height when standing on money in many other songs. The list includes “You’re Lost,” “A Lot,” “Im A Star,” “Who Run It (Remix),” “Like Me” and “Sanguine Paradise.”", "annotation_id": "16899021", "url": "https://genius.com/16899021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "She a lil’ thot, can’t wife no bird", "vault_lines": ["She a lil' thot, can't wife no bird"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi could be throwing shade at their ex, Brittany Byrd. In mid-2016, Uzi officially announced their somewhat messy breakup on social media.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUzi and Brittany Byrd have recently been seen together, most notably when Uzi attended her birthday. The two have managed to salvage their friendship but Uzi makes sure to dispel any rumors of a returning romantic interest with this line.", "annotation_id": "16858809", "url": "https://genius.com/16858809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "I’m a Leo like lion, I’m Simba", "vault_lines": ["I'm a Leo like lion, I'm Simba"], "meaning": "Uzi belongs to the Leo astrological sign, as their birthday is on July 31st, making him fall in the category. The symbol for the Leo astrological sign is a lion.\n\nSimba is a lion from Disney’s Lion King movie series. Uzi likens themself to the lion as they state that they too are like a lion.\n\nhttps://imgix.ranker.com/user_node_img/102/2032052/original/simba-photo-u8?w=650&q=50&fm=pjpg&fit=crop&crop=faces\n\nThis may also be referencing a line on their 2015 track, “Super Saiyan,”, where they rapped:\n\nAyy, I am a Leo like lion (Ooh)\nAyy, better than me then he lyin' (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "16844313", "url": "https://genius.com/16844313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Saw a minivan followin’ my brand new Lamb’ (Lamb’) I had a F and an N in my hand (And an N)", "vault_lines": ["Saw a minivan followin' my brand new Lamb' (Lamb')"], "meaning": "Uzi is referring to a time when they got into a dangerous situation, as a white van, supposedly up to no good, had suspiciously been following their new Lamborghini Urus around for quite a while.\n\nUzi didn’t have to worry though, as they had an F&N gun on standby, ready to fire in their hand.\n\nUzi has showed off their car collection at the Philadelphia Auto Show, where their Lambo can be seen, as well as some of their other cars.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/nbQaeokgYiA?t=30", "annotation_id": "16844271", "url": "https://genius.com/16844271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Okay, my money sky blue, but my new coupe is slime green", "vault_lines": ["Okay, my money sky blue, but my new coupe is slime green"], "meaning": "Uzi’s money is comprised of all $100 bills, as the $100 bills have a signature blue tint and a blue security ribbon, which no other cash in the US has.\n\n\n\nUzi has showcased their car collection at the Philadelphia Auto Show, where it could be seen that all of their cars, including his coupes, were green, similar to the color of slime.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/nbQaeokgYiA?t=30\n\nThe idea to liken the color to slime might have come from the slang word, as made popular by some of Uzi’s collaborators, including Young Thug, Gunna and Playboi Carti. “Slime” is an acronym for “Street Life Intelligence and Money is Everything”. Slime is often used as a word referring to a good friend, a homie, or just a friendship in general.", "annotation_id": "16844210", "url": "https://genius.com/16844210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "I don’t want you back, you a thot, you a nat (A fuckin’ nat)", "vault_lines": ["I don't want you back, you a thot, you a nat (A fuckin' nat)"], "meaning": "Thot is the acronym for “That Ho Over There”, typically used to refer to wannabe posh women, who believe that they are sexy and tempting and act as if they are better than everyone else, yet no man pays attention to them.\n\nNat is a word used similarly to “thot”, it has the same meaning as “bitch” or “ho”.\n\nThis line could be referring to Uzi’s ex-girlfriend, Brittany Byrd.\n\nOn one song from Luv Is Rage 2, “The Way Life Goes”, Uzi raps:\n\nIf she ever call my phone you know I gotta dead her\nBut I like that girl too much, I wish I never met her\n\nmeaning Uzi wouldn’t pick up the phone and probably didn’t want to talk to her, yet they reminisced how much they liked her.\n\nThroughout the rest of the song, Uzi raps about how they wish they could’ve done things differently while they and Byrd were still together, yet Uzi concludes that they don’t need her. Here, they just reassure the point.", "annotation_id": "16085892", "url": "https://genius.com/16085892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Water on my neck, swim through that, that’s a lap (Water)", "vault_lines": ["Water on my neck, swim through that, that's a lap (Water)"], "meaning": "Water is slang for diamonds and jewelry.\n\nUzi has many pieces of jewelry covered with diamonds, especially around their neck. Some of their most famous pieces include their diamond-encrusted pendants featuring Marilyn Manson, the letters “LUV” (signifying Lil Uzi Vert), an upside-down cross, cartoon Lil Uzi Vert (also used on their Lil Uzi Vert Vs. The World album cover), and Vlone, among others.\n\n\n\nIn Olympic pools, swimmers have to swim laps, obviously through water. An Olympic pool’s lap’s length is 50 meters or 164.042 feet. Uzi is saying that if you were to line up all of their jewelry and swim through their “water,” you would definitely have to swim at least one lap’s length.", "annotation_id": "16085818", "url": "https://genius.com/16085818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Fuck from the back, hit her once, that’s a wrap (Let’s go) No strings attached, that’s a rack, that’s a rack (Rack, rack) No strings attached, that’s a rack, that’s a rack (Rack)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck from the back, hit her once, that's a wrap (Let's go)"], "meaning": "To have strings attached can mean two things.\n\nThe first meaning is for something to have special needs, limits or demands. For example, when taking a loan, interest would be the strings involved. Rack is slang for a large sum of money, usually $1,000. In Uzi’s case, though, they get their thousands without any strings attached. They directly get $1,000, without any money being cut off.\n\n\n\nThe second meaning of “no strings attached” is to have sex with someone, but do nothing with them in addition to that, this usually only occurs once. To hit someone in the form that Uzi uses the term, also means to have sex with someone. Uzi only has sex with a girl once without doing anything with her prior to or after that.", "annotation_id": "16085773", "url": "https://genius.com/16085773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "(I’m workin’ on dying)", "vault_lines": ["We tear it up, tear it up, tear it up"], "meaning": "This is the tag for the Philadelphia-based production group Working on Dying. Its members include producers Brandon Finessin, Oogie Mane, Loosie Man, Forza, and F1lthy.\n\nUzi has previously worked with some of the group’s members: Forza has produced “1600,” Loosie Man has produced “Bando” and Oogie Mane has produced “Like Me” and “Lotus,” Forza and Oogie Mane have worked together with Uzi on “Of Course.”", "annotation_id": "16085731", "url": "https://genius.com/16085731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Fendi knapsack, while I’m spittin’ Fendi facts (Facts)", "vault_lines": ["Fendi knapsack, while I'm spittin' Fendi facts (Facts)"], "meaning": "Fendi is an Italian luxury designer fashion house. Just like those of most luxury fashion houses, Fendi’s products can cost upwards of thousands of dollars.\n\nhttps://images.www.fendi.com/images/h7e/ha0/8900508090398/7VZ042A5N7F0CFM_01_large#product-medium\n\nFendi knapsack sold for $2,190\n\n\nUzi has previously mentioned Fendi on Carnage’s track “WDYW”:\n\nBalmain, Saint Laurent with the Fendi\n\nIn 2017, Uzi performed at a Fendi-sponsored event.\n\n\n\nUzi performing at a Fendi event while wearing a Fendi headband", "annotation_id": "16085504", "url": "https://genius.com/16085504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That’s a Rack", "line": "Yeah (Oogie Mane, he killed it)", "vault_lines": ["We tear it up, tear it up, tear it up"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for the producer Oogie Mane. Oogie is a part of the production collective Working on Dying, who, like Uzi, come from Philadelphia. This tag is voiced by Matt Ox, a young rapper from Philly, and originates from Matt’s breakout hit, “Overwhelming.”\n\nOogie has previously collaborated with Uzi on released songs like “Of Course Intro” and “1600,” as well as on various unreleased tracks, which fans have named “This Way” and “It’s Going Down.”\n\nIn additon to Uzi, Oogie Mane has collaborated with many similar artists. His credits include Juice WRLD and Future’s “WRLD On Drugs” and Young Thug’s unreleased track “Lotus” (also featuring Uzi).", "annotation_id": "16074622", "url": "https://genius.com/16074622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
