{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That Fiya", "line": ".44", "vault_lines": [".44 on my body, bitch, this shit, it hit like (.44 on my body)"], "meaning": "A .44, also known as .44 Magnum is usually a large handgun/revolver. This means that Uzi Vertical is dangerous for the opposition, and will have to be taken seriously.\n\nIn another words: He won’t take on you lightly if you mess with him.", "annotation_id": "28940052", "url": "https://genius.com/28940052", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "That Fiya", "line": "Money stretched out for a mile", "vault_lines": ["Money stretched out for a mile"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi has mentioned multiple times how big he becomes stacking himself on his money, now he is saying that his monet streches out for a mile, so let’s calculate how much money he is talking about if we take into consideration that he is using 100 dollar bills stacked sideways while only touching their permiters.\nNow let’s take the dollar and measure it’s dimentions:\nIt is 66.3 mm in height and 155 mm in lenght. Lets use it’s height so we give Uzi the benefit of the doubt.\nOne mile is equal to 1609.34 meters, so now let’s move on to the actual calculation:\n1609.34 / 0.0663 = 24273.6048265\nso in scenario A Uzi is talking about around 2427400 dollars.\nExtra: If we want to try a scenario where his money stretch is more of a money spread the money would most likely stack one on top of each other, so with that in mind lets avarage that half of a 100 dollar bill is stacked on top of each other, meaning that the money would be double.\nIn scenario B Lil Uzi is talking about 4854700 dollars.", "annotation_id": "28938590", "url": "https://genius.com/28938590", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
