{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Wheezy Beats", "vault_lines": ["Damn, no key just to start it"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for Wheezy, a producer Uzi has collaborated with many times.\n\n\n\nSome examples of Uzi’s and Wheezy’s collaborations include 2015’s “Queso”, 2018’s “.223” with Gunna and 2019’s “150K” with G Herbo.", "annotation_id": "17554242", "url": "https://genius.com/17554242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Love VLone, love Garçon, switchin’ clothes (Okay)", "vault_lines": ["Love VLone, love Garçon, switchin' clothes (Okay)"], "meaning": "Uzi references his two favorite fashion brands, VLone and Comme Des Garçons.\n\nVlone is an American brand established by A$AP Bari of the A$AP Mob. Uzi has collaborated with the Mob on many tracks, including 2016’s “Runner” and 2017’s “RAF”.\nIt should also be noted that Uzi has a track named “Ready Set Go (VLone)”.\n\n\n\nComme des Garçons is a Japanese brand founded by Rei Kawakubo.", "annotation_id": "17554158", "url": "https://genius.com/17554158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Diamonds in my Carti’, not a stalkin’ man (What? Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds in my Carti', not a stalkin' man (What? Ooh)"], "meaning": "Uzi references his Cartier glasses covered in diamonds.\n\n\n\nWhile stalkers would wear pale glasses with dark lenses as to not draw attention, Uzi always goes all-out flashy, proving he’s not a stalker.", "annotation_id": "17554132", "url": "https://genius.com/17554132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Damn, no key just to start it", "vault_lines": ["Damn, no key just to start it"], "meaning": "Many modern luxury cars do not need to have the key in the ignition in order to start the car, the key’s bare proximity is enough. This gives the impression of the car not needing a key to start.\n\nUzi has showcased many of his high-class cars at the Philadelphia Auto Show, many of which can be started without putting the key in the ignition, for example his Lamborghini Urus.\nhttps://youtu.be/nbQaeokgYiA?t=30", "annotation_id": "17554041", "url": "https://genius.com/17554041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Walkin’ in this water like the sea, watch how I part it (Okay, okay)", "vault_lines": ["Walkin' in this water like the sea, watch how I part it (Okay, okay)"], "meaning": "Water is a commonly utilized reference in hip hop, which serves as a comparison to jewelry, and the diamonds that usually cover or “flood” it. Uzi is describing the amount of diamonds that he has all over him, or the amount of jewelry.\n\nThe second half of the line is a clever reference to Moses, the prophet in the bible that parted the sea.", "annotation_id": "13067786", "url": "https://genius.com/13067786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "Got my pocket rocket, I feel like I’m Harden I’m so used to ballin’, you need to award this", "vault_lines": ["Got my pocket rocket, I feel like I'm Harden"], "meaning": "James Harden is a professional basketball player for the Houston Rockets. Harden has multiple accolades in his career and was the runner-up to the NBA Most Valuable Player Award in the 2016-17 season—many pundits argued that he was robbed of the award.\n\nIn January 2019, Lil Uzi Vert rooted for James Harden in a courtside video during a Philadelphia 76ers and Houston Rockets matchup.\n\n“Ballin'” is urban slang and means to have a lot of money. Uzi used the same term on the August 2017 track, “Sauce It Up”:\n\nEveryday I’m ballin', so you know I’m scorin'", "annotation_id": "14729470", "url": "https://genius.com/14729470", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Target", "line": "On her knees, that Voorhees, treat her like I’m Jason", "vault_lines": ["On her knees, that Voorhees, treat her like I'm Jason"], "meaning": "Jason Voorhees is an well-known fictional serial killer, best known from the “Friday the 13th” movie.\n\n\n\nThe girl Uzi is referring to would be hiding from Jason by getting on her knees, but in Uzi’s case the girl gets on her knees to give him oral sex.", "annotation_id": "13142636", "url": "https://genius.com/13142636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
