{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I don’t work for Lil Debbies, but I’m caked up", "vault_lines": ["I don't work for Lil Debbies, but I'm caked up"], "meaning": "Cymere in this lyric, states that they doesn’t need a company to maintain their own wealth, meanwhile braggadociously speaking about his money, otherwise known as “Cake”.\nwhich in itself is a reference to the company Little Debbie, the manufacturer of Little Debbie Cake Snacks.", "annotation_id": "28932717", "url": "https://genius.com/28932717", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "Wear dresses", "vault_lines": ["My right hand to God, I ain't never heard a Uzi Vert song that I can say, \"That's Uzi Vert\""], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert has not shied away from wearing feminine clothing during their career. In 2021, they arrived to the Met Gala wearing a suit and black skirt put together with the help of Thom Browne.", "annotation_id": "28938601", "url": "https://genius.com/28938601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
