{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah (Woah) Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah (Woo) Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah (Goddamn) Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah (Suicide doors)", "vault_lines": ["Suicide doors (Suicide doors)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert is no stranger to using the ad-lip: ‘Yeah, Yeah, Yeah,’ the most notable example is when he featured on Bad and Boujee and he opened the verse: “Yeah, Yeah, Yeah, Yeah.” Which brought the ire and hate of many rap listeners; most notably one, rap critic, who’s literally named: the Rap Critic.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/4X2V4IMd9Tg\n-[7:08]\n\nHe also had: ‘Yeah, Yeah, Yeah,’ as his Chorus for Uppin Downers.\n\nhttps://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-uppin-downers-soundcloud-rappers-only-lyrics", "annotation_id": "28934816", "url": "https://genius.com/28934816", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I’m reptilian, I’m not normal, my soul threw (Bitch) My mama don’t know me no more, ’cause I got new blood (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["I'm reptilian, I'm not normal, my soul threw (Bitch)"], "meaning": "Uzi is referencing a popular conspiracy theory in the weirder parts of the internet that claims many celebrities are actually part-reptilian aliens and disguise themselves as humans, meaning they would be cold-blooded. They also acknowledge another conspiracy theory about them selling their soul to acquire fame.", "annotation_id": "28934342", "url": "https://genius.com/28934342", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I ain’t satanist, but they say I am, so let’s do it", "vault_lines": ["I ain't satanist, but they say I am, so let's do it"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert has previously shown a lot of what people think are satanic symbols, like the upside down cross for example.\n\nThis has made people think he is satanist.\n\nIn this line the  rapper is saying that he is not satanist, however people are talking about it so he won’t stop.", "annotation_id": "28933393", "url": "https://genius.com/28933393", "state": "pending", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "He ain’t never shot no Uzi to call himself “Uzi Vert” He ain’t no Uzi-totin’ nigga He ain’t the nigga known in the neighborhood for the Uzis", "vault_lines": ["He ain't never shot no Uzi to call himself \"Uzi Vert\""], "meaning": "Charleston White is a well known hater of Lil Uzi Vert and in this is he is poking holes in Lil Uzi Vert’s credibility of them being a Gang banger and person who actually carries a Uzi sub-machine gun around, as well as claiming that Uzi does not have the street credibility that he(charleston) claims they(uzi) has.", "annotation_id": "28932635", "url": "https://genius.com/28932635", "state": "pending", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "Six-six-six, satanist, that’s why they hate us", "vault_lines": ["Six-six-six, satanist, that's why they hate us"], "meaning": "Recently Lil Uzi was criticized for a controversial line in an unreleased song performed at Rolling Loud in March 2023.\n“I make a city girl believe in Satan”.\n\nThey are no stranger to using satanic imagery for aesthetic purposes, famously wearing upside down cross chains and earrings, as well as a custom goat head chain at the 2018 Grammys that lead to them getting lots of publicity from conspiracy theorists.", "annotation_id": "28932174", "url": "https://genius.com/28932174", "state": "pending", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I’m so rockstar, I might try cocaine", "vault_lines": ["I'm so rockstar, I might try cocaine"], "meaning": "Many celebrities try drugs for the fun of it, and it is a very common trope to mention in music today,\n\nOf course, Uzi has mentioned drugs before, like in their 2017 smash hit, XO TOUR Llif3.", "annotation_id": "28932109", "url": "https://genius.com/28932109", "state": "pending", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "My Dominican bitch don’t speak English, but so fluent", "vault_lines": ["My Dominican bitch don't speak English, but so fluent"], "meaning": "Dominican Republic’s official language is Spanish. Most Latino immigrants in the us are not fluent in English.\nThe fluidity might be referring to the way that she moves.", "annotation_id": "28931831", "url": "https://genius.com/28931831", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "[Intro: Charleston White, Arca & Lil Uzi Vert]", "vault_lines": ["Thank you, Lil Uzi Vert"], "meaning": "“Suicide Doors” kicks off with a snippet of a SAY CHEESE! interview with Charleston White, which came after Uzi disassociated themself from Popp Hunna following a swarm of snitching allegations.\n\nBeing a reformed gangster, Charleston exclaims how Uzi has no right to judge Popp for ‘snitching’ because they aren’t involved with the street lifestyle.\n\nHowever, since that interview, after receiving a waver to use his voice on “Suicide Doors”, Charleston White and Uzi have been said by Charleston himself to be on good terms.", "annotation_id": "28927464", "url": "https://genius.com/28927464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "She looked at me in my eyes, said, “Be the old you”", "vault_lines": ["She looked at me in my eyes, said, \"Be the old you\""], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert entered the rap scene during the mid-2010s, establishing an audience with the 2017 hit “XO TOUR Llif3.” Being that “Suicide Doors” succeeds that track’s release by six years, many yearn for Uzi to dismiss their artistic growth and revert to an older style.", "annotation_id": "28925156", "url": "https://genius.com/28925156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I put spikes all on my head just like I’m Goku", "vault_lines": ["I put spikes all on my head just like I'm Goku"], "meaning": "In early 2022, Lil Uzi Vert debuted their liberty spikes, which have been associated with their brand as of 2023, even appearing on Pink Tape’s cover art.\n\nPictured: Lil Uzi Vert on March 26, 2022.\n\nGoku is the main character across well-received anime series, Dragon Ball. He most notably sports his hair spiked up, like Lil Uzi, across the entire series.\n\n A frame of Goku taken from Dragon Ball Z.", "annotation_id": "28924879", "url": "https://genius.com/28924879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I’m like Chief Keef, like Sosa, I’m Glo", "vault_lines": ["I'm likе Chief Keef, like Sosa, I'm Glo"], "meaning": "Glo Gang is a record label founded by Chicago Drill rapper, Chief Keef. Lil Uzi likens themself to Chief Keef to highlight how they’ll shine after releasing Pink Tape.", "annotation_id": "28924867", "url": "https://genius.com/28924867", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I eat Pop-Tarts, but I took that bitch to Nobu", "vault_lines": ["I eat Pop-Tarts, but I took that bitch to Nobu"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert has stated themself that they enjoy eating Pop-Tarts, breakfast toaster pastries. When asked what they were doing the night before they pulled up to the 2018 GRAMMY Award Show, Uzi said:\n\nI was in my hotel room eating Pop-Tarts\n\nWhile Pop-Tarts are an everyday snack for Uzi, they can still treat their date to a trip to Nobu, a luxurious restaurant that blends traditional Japanese dishes with Peruvian ingredients.", "annotation_id": "28924816", "url": "https://genius.com/28924816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Suicide Doors", "line": "I feel like, bitch, I’m The Crow (Woah) I feel like, bitch, I’m The Crow (I’m the—, ah) I feel like, bitch, I’m The Crow (I’m The Crow) I feel like, bitch, I’m The Crow", "vault_lines": ["I feel like, bitch, I'm The Crow (Woah)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi Vert compares themself to the titular character from the 1994 gothic superhero movie The Crow. The film is based on a rock musician who was murdered alongside his wife and has now been resurrected from the dead to seek revenge.", "annotation_id": "28892679", "url": "https://genius.com/28892679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 154, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
