{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "Yeah, um, Beat your ass Randy Couture", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, um, Beat your ass Randy Couture"], "meaning": "Randy Couture is a former decorated Ultimate Fighting Championship and  Mixed Martial Arts fighter, as well as being an honored veteran of the United States Army, serving with the 101st Airborne Screaming Eagles.\n\n\n\nPossibly versed as a nod to his 2016 track about another UFC fighter, “Ronda (Winners)”, Uzi likens himself to Couture to demonstrate his strong fighting ability.", "annotation_id": "14855352", "url": "https://genius.com/14855352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "Buy my momma a Rolls Royce skrt", "vault_lines": ["Buy my momma a Rolls Royce skrt"], "meaning": "Rolls Royce is an affluential luxury car company from Great Britain founded by Charles Rolls and Henry Royce in 1904.\n\n\n\nUzi has always shown a strong fondness for Rolls-Royce’s vehicles and has made several references to the group in his songs, such as in his 2016 track, “Today!!”.\n\nDriving in the Lamb but I’mma get the Wraith, yeah", "annotation_id": "14793939", "url": "https://genius.com/14793939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "I might just jump in the Porsche", "vault_lines": ["I might just jump in the Porsche"], "meaning": "Porsche is a notable German luxury automobile company founded by Ferdinand Porsche in 1931 specializing in  excellent sports cars and sedans.\n\n\n\n\n\nPorsche is a big name in the rap industry, popular with rappers such as Soulja Boy and Kanye West.", "annotation_id": "14792370", "url": "https://genius.com/14792370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "Banana clip right to the drama", "vault_lines": ["Lil Uzi contributes a song to TM88’s Sacii Lyfe mixtape, hosted by Ethan Sacii."], "meaning": "A banana clip is a high capacity magazine popularized with the extensive use of the AK-47 rifle.", "annotation_id": "14792255", "url": "https://genius.com/14792255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "I got the pole my style", "vault_lines": ["I got the pole I'm stylin'"], "meaning": "Pole is a slang term to describe a gun. This term is used by many rappers such as Trippie Redd and 6ix9ine especially in their collaboration “Poles1469”. The “pole” is a reference to the weapon’s barrel.\n\n1400, bitch, you know I tote a pole\n\nIn the second part of the line, Uzi is alluding to the customizations of his gun, for instance a gun skin or a bump stock to make the firearm fully automatic.", "annotation_id": "14792049", "url": "https://genius.com/14792049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stylin’", "line": "I’m going right back to the future I might jump right in DeLorean (Skrt)", "vault_lines": ["I might just jump in the Porsche"], "meaning": "A reference to the movie Back To The Future and the DeLorean MC12 turned into a time machine.\n\nThe drugs Uzi takes get him so high he’s travels and transcends time from popping some pills.", "annotation_id": "10243386", "url": "https://genius.com/10243386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
