{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strong", "line": "Zaytoven", "vault_lines": ["Gucci to the sock"], "meaning": "San Francisco-based producer Zaytoven’s tag is shouted on the track. Zay has worked with a wide range of notable Atlanta artists such as Soulja Boy, Future, Young Jeezy, and Usher. However, he is mainly known for his production work alongside Gucci Mane, contributing to the majority of the rapper’s solo projects.", "annotation_id": "18408080", "url": "https://genius.com/18408080", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strong", "line": "Gucci to the sock Gucci to the sock Gucci to the sock Gucci to the sock, I just talked to Zay", "vault_lines": ["Gucci to the sock"], "meaning": "Gucci is an Italian luxury brand of fashion and leather goods. Gucci was founded by Guccio Gucci in Florence, Tuscany, in 1921.\n\nUzi also shouts out Zaytoven, the producer on the track.", "annotation_id": "18192538", "url": "https://genius.com/18192538", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strong", "line": "AP on my wrist, ice my watch", "vault_lines": ["AP on my wrist, ice my watch"], "meaning": "AP refers to the luxury watch brand Audemars Piguet.\n\n\n\nUzi frequently mentions his expensive watches and AP in particular, mentioning the brand again on his unreleased song with Chief Keef, Rollie in which he delivers the line: “AP mil' on my Rollie”.", "annotation_id": "18046337", "url": "https://genius.com/18046337", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strong", "line": "Rockin’ Saint Laurent you got no clothes (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Rockin' Saint Laurent you got no clothes (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "Yves Saint Laurent is an extravagant French fashion company founded in 1961 by the man who holds the establishment’s name. Uzi recently shouted out the label on Twitter with a line from his song, “Top”:\n\nhttps://mobile.twitter.com/liluzivert/status/741027238926131204?lang=en\n\nOn top of having a track named after the brand, the Philadelphian artist’s strong admiration for Saint Laurent also carries onto his lyrics— a notorious line from Uzi’s hit “The Way Life Goes” represents this.\n\nWalk off my Saint Laurent, that leather\n\nAs Uzi’s costly attire vastly surpasses his opposition’s, they may as well have no clothing on.", "annotation_id": "14993928", "url": "https://genius.com/14993928", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strong", "line": "When I’m in the field bitch I ball like Romo, yeah", "vault_lines": ["When I'm in the field bitch I ball like Romo, yeah"], "meaning": "Tony Romo is a former NFL player who was the starting quarterback for the Dallas Cowboys.\n\nLil Uzi is making a simile that he plays as well as Tony Romo.", "annotation_id": "14933840", "url": "https://genius.com/14933840", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
