{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Street Sweeper", "line": "Now I be balling, just like Rogaine", "vault_lines": ["Now I be balling, just like Rogaine"], "meaning": "“Rogaine” refers to the hair loss treatment, famously promoted by NBA player Karl Malone in the 1990s.\nThe line “Now I be ballin', just like Rogaine” compares the artist’s rise in success to the way Rogaine restores hair, symbolizing a comeback or transformation. It also subtly touches on the vanity and image-consciousness often associated with sports and celebrity culture.", "annotation_id": "34495240", "url": "https://genius.com/34495240", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Street Sweeper", "line": "Now I be balling, just like Rogaine", "vault_lines": ["Now I be balling, just like Rogaine"], "meaning": "“Rogaine” refers to the hair loss treatment, famously promoted by NBA player Karl Malone in the 1990s. The line “Now I be ballin', just like Rogaine” compares the artist’s rise in success to the way Rogaine restores hair, symbolizing a comeback or transformation. It also subtly touches on the vanity and image-consciousness often associated with sports and celebrity culture.", "annotation_id": "34495112", "url": "https://genius.com/34495112", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
