{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "She off the boat and she came from Israel", "vault_lines": ["She off the boat and she came from Israel"], "meaning": "Young Thug confirms the widespread rumor of him being an IDF soldier.", "annotation_id": "37795553", "url": "https://genius.com/37795553", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "I need the beat, that’s just for the stems (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I need the beat, that's just for the stems (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Stems are individual track outs of vocal and instrumental sounds in a song (ex: kick, snare, guitar, piano, lead vocal, etc).\n\nHere, Lil Uzi Vert is saying he doesn’t want to use your weak-ass beats. He just wants the stems so he can use one of the sounds for his own beats.\n\nThis line could be referring to controversy around his track Sauce It Up, which was accused of plagiarizing a beat posted online by Beats By Saif. It turns out that both beats just used the same royalty free loop, and this line can then be interpreted as teasing clout chasers who accuse Uzi of stealing their beats.\n\nSource: https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.44529/title.lil-uzi-vert-accused-of-jacking-beat-from-twitter-troll-beats-by-saif#", "annotation_id": "21563233", "url": "https://genius.com/21563233", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "I bought an old Cutlass, I set it on fours (Set it on fours)", "vault_lines": ["I bought an old Cutlass, I set it on fours (Set it on fours)"], "meaning": "The Oldsmobile Cutlass was a range of automobiles produced by General Motors' Oldsmobile division between 1961 and 1999. At its introduction, the Cutlass was Oldsmobile’s smallest model; it began as a unibody compact car, but saw its greatest success as a body-on-frame intermediate.", "annotation_id": "21285921", "url": "https://genius.com/21285921", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Yeah, I’m on that drank, I’m ’bout to keel (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I'm on that drank, I'm 'bout to keel (Woah)"], "meaning": "Keel is a word for faint or fall over. Thugger is on that “drank” which is most likely “lean”, a combination of cough syrup and any other drink, commonly sprite.", "annotation_id": "21285894", "url": "https://genius.com/21285894", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Young Wunna, young Wunna, I can’t break the code (Young Wunna)", "vault_lines": ["Young Wunna, young Wunna, I can't break the code (Young Wunna)"], "meaning": "“Wunna” is one of Gunna’s nicknames and is the title of his sophomore studio album. He revealed the nickname’s true meaning in a tweet on March 17, 2020:\n\nWUNNA- Wealthy Unapologetic Nigga Naturally Authentic !!", "annotation_id": "19320572", "url": "https://genius.com/19320572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Smoke on that thrax, I’m on strawberry peels Strawberry peels, strawberry peels Strawberry peels, strawberry peels (Yeah) Strawberry peels", "vault_lines": ["Strawberry peels, strawberry peels"], "meaning": "Thugger repeats the phrase “strawberry pills,” which was censored to “Strawberry Peels” for the song’s title, to emphasize his excitement over these drugs. Drugs such as ecstasy, which Thug has dedicated an entire song to in the past, can appear in a red pressed form like the one he describes here.\n\nVarious other drugs, such as lean and weed, are mentioned throughout the song. Both can obtain a similar strawberry flavor to the one Thug describes here – marijuana can be added to a container with sliced or crushed strawberry and allow its juices to evaporate in the same environment as marijuana, which hydrates the drug along with giving it a strawberry flavor, while lean can be mixed with strawberry soda as the additive flavoring beverage.\n\nAs mentioned above, the song’s title, “Strawberry Peels,” is a censorship of this phrase, “strawberry pills,” which refers to a collection of red-colored pills. Censoring explicit words and drugs in song titles for public relations purposes is common in hip-hop, a genre that can frequently discuss more mature topics like drug use. It also recently happened to the title of Migos‘ February 2020 single “Give No Fxk,” which Thug appeared on as a featured artist.", "annotation_id": "19280009", "url": "https://genius.com/19280009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Hop out a jet, hop in a Rolls Icy Patek straight off of shows (Straight off of shows)", "vault_lines": ["Hop out a jet, hop in a Rolls"], "meaning": "Gunna flexes multiple expensive brands with these lines. “Rolls” is short for Rolls Royce, an English maker of luxury vehicles. “Patek” is another abbreviation short for Patek Phillipe, which is an iconic Swiss watchmaker that is often mentioned in hip-hop.\n\nGunna also borrows the flow from his first verse on his April 2018 record “Sold Out Dates” for these lines, with the lyrical content of the lines containing very similar themes as well. On the original track, he raps:\n\n‘Nother backend, I’m back on the road\nFlooded Patek, paid off a show", "annotation_id": "19275914", "url": "https://genius.com/19275914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "YSL slatt life, we slimy and slick (Slatt)", "vault_lines": ["YSL slatt life, we slimy and slick (Slatt)"], "meaning": "Young Stoner Life Records, abbreviated as YSL Records, is Young Thug’s Atlanta-based record label. Gunna signed to the label in 2017.\n\nThe following terms in the line are both trademarks of Thug and artists signed to the record label. “Slatt” is an acronymic term standing form Slime Love All The Time. “Slime” is another acronymic term, meaning Street Life Intelligence and Money is Everything, and also can be used to describe a friend. Thugger is often credited with popularizing both terms.", "annotation_id": "19275465", "url": "https://genius.com/19275465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "VLONE, Chrome Heart, it’s still stuck on the rich", "vault_lines": ["VLONE, Chrome Heart, it's still stuck on the rich"], "meaning": "Gunna drops two luxury fashion brands, which is a common trope for him his music. Chrome Hearts is an American luxury accessory and clothing maker based in Los Angeles, CA. He preciously mentioned the brand on his February 2018 track “Spending Addiction”:\n\nChrome Hearts on my face just to help me look cool (Yeah)\n\nVLONE is an American streetwear brand based in New York, NY. The brand was started by and is owned by rapper A$AP Rocky and designer A$AP Bari. Gunna previously paid homage to the brand with his  October 2018 track “Off White VLONE”:\n\nOff-White, Vlone 1’s, foreigns parked in my lawn", "annotation_id": "19274995", "url": "https://genius.com/19274995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Stand on my money like my name Shaquille", "vault_lines": ["Stand on my money like my name Shaquille"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi compares himself to legendary former NBA player Shaquille O'Neal. Both men have become extremely successful financially, with Uzi’s net worth estimated to be around $17 million and Shaq’s net worth estimated to be around $400 million at the time of this song’s release.\n\n\n\nAdditionally, Uzi has a below average height for US males, standing at just 5' 4\"; however, Shaq is known for being exceptionally tall, with a height of 7' 1\". With the amount of money Uzi has accumulated, though, he could give himself a substantial height boost if he stood on top of it all.\n\nLil Uzi has made this kind of connection before on his 2019 track “Sanguine Paradise”:\n\nIn reality, I’m 5' 4\"\nStand on my money, now I’m 6' 6\"\n\nHe has also compared himself to Shaquille O'Neal on his DJ Esco and Future collaboration “Too Much Sauce”:\n\nShaquille O'Neal with the haters ‘cause I’m blockin’ y'all", "annotation_id": "19274222", "url": "https://genius.com/19274222", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "She give me brain, that’s that Urkel and chill She mixed with white, told her my name Jaleel", "vault_lines": ["She give me brain, that's that Urkel and chill"], "meaning": "Steve Urkel was a character on the sitcom Family Matters who was played by actor Jaleel White. Urkel was appeared very nerdy and smart on the show due to characteristics such as large, thick glasses and frequently wearing suspenders.\n\n\n\nUzi compares Urkel’s intelligent persona to his girl giving him oral sex, which is frequently referred to as “brain.” Uzi also uses “and chill” to end the line, relating the TV show themes to the phrase “Netflix and chill,” where sexual activities happen while watching TV or movies on the streaming service.\n\nUzi has made reference to Urkel before, exemplified by his verse on his August 2017 track “Neon Guts”:\n\nStay with a nerd just like Urkel, Jaleel", "annotation_id": "19272863", "url": "https://genius.com/19272863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Strawberry Peels", "line": "Spider (Hey) Hey (SEX, Spider, SEX)", "vault_lines": ["Hey (SEX, Spider, SEX)"], "meaning": "King Spider (shortened to Spider) and SEX are some of Thugger’s monikers.\n\nSpider was first used in 2019 with the launch of Spider Worldwide, Thugger’s clothing brand. The brand offers a variety of items ranging from rhinestone spider web encrusted trucker jackets to bright red tracksuits with stylized web motifs.\n\n\n\nThug performing in his Spider clothes at Wireless Festival in 2019\n\nIn February 2018, Thug tweeted:\n\nI’m changing my name to SEX….\n\nannouncing his new rap moniker. Following up with a second tweet, Thug declared:\n\nFor now on call me SEX!!!\n\nSimilarly, Thug attempted to change his name to Jeffery (also referred to as No, My Name Is Jeffery) in 2016 after his birth name along with the release of his mixtape No, My Name Is Jeffery (released in August 2016 as JEFFERY) but only if the mixtape sold 100,000 copies in its first week. However, he later explained that he wanted to go back to his real name, Jeffery, for professional purposes.", "annotation_id": "19272791", "url": "https://genius.com/19272791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
