{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Stay", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-stay-lyrics", "genius_title": "Stay", "genius_id": 4381737, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "That Glock, it don’t miss, got a dot (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["That Glock, it don't miss, got a dot (Woo)"], "meaning": "A red dot or laser beam is an aiming tool designed to increase accuracy while shooting a weapon.\n\n\n\nOn his 2020 track “Lo Mein,” Uzi contrasts this claim, saying he doesn’t have aim when using an extra clip:\n\nExtra clip in it, nigga, I ain’t got no aim", "annotation_id": "19786965", "url": "https://genius.com/19786965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "I sold over, so how could I flop? (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I sold over, so how could I flop? (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Uzi’s Eternal Atake was expected to sell 275k first week. While becoming his second number one album, it sold 288k first week, also taking the place of fourth largest streaming week since Lil Wayne’s Tha Carter V.\n\nUzi then asks with those numbers how could flop in sales proving his status in the music industry as one of the top artists, as Forbes stated he is the fourth most consumed rapper.", "annotation_id": "19786784", "url": "https://genius.com/19786784", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "One-nine-four-two, yeah Shot, shot, shot, shot, shot, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Shot, shot, shot, shot, shot, yeah"], "meaning": "In this line, Uzi references Don Julio’s 1942 Tequila, which is priced at around $130 per bottle.\n\n\n\nHe’s previously mentioned the drink on several tracks, perhaps most notably on his recent 2020 track “Lo Mein,“ on which he similarly raps:\n\n1942 in my section, no Remy (Let’s go)\nTook JT out the city (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "19786592", "url": "https://genius.com/19786592", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "Got an XO piece, square rocks (Rocks)", "vault_lines": ["Got an XO piece, square rocks (Rocks)"], "meaning": "XO Record Label is NAV’s record label, and was founded by singer The Weeknd.\n\n\n\nNAV pictured with XO record label founder The Weeknd.\nNAV frequently mentions XO in plenty of music, most notably on his 2017 smash hit “Some Way,“ in which he raps:\n\nWay, we got ‘em feelin’ some way\nWay, ‘cause you see XO in the place, told her, “Wait\"\n\nFurthermore, within another track on Good Intentions entitled “No Debate,“ NAV raps a similar line:\n\nGot an XO piece and it’s all glass (All glass)", "annotation_id": "19786352", "url": "https://genius.com/19786352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "That girl, she a nat-nat, yeah (Nat) I need a fly swat, swat, uh (Swat, swat)", "vault_lines": ["That girl, she a nat-nat, yeah (Nat)"], "meaning": "A ‘nat nat’ is slang for a promiscuous woman, similar to “thot” or “hoe.” Uzi used the term previously on  “That’s a Rack”\n\nFuck that ho ‘cause she a nat nat\n\nA “gnat” (also pronounced “nat”) on the other hand is a small, flying insect. Uzi wants to swat away the girl, like he would with the similarly named insect.", "annotation_id": "19781963", "url": "https://genius.com/19781963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Status", "line": "How much money you got? (You got?) I told her a lot, lot, lot (A lot)", "vault_lines": ["How much money you got? (You got?)"], "meaning": "Nav brags about his wealth with a reference to 21 Savage’s hit song “a lot”:\n\nHow much money you got? (A lot)", "annotation_id": "19780851", "url": "https://genius.com/19780851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
