{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "All the rings on like I’m Horry, ayy", "vault_lines": ["All the rings on like I'm Horry, ayy"], "meaning": "Robert Horry, a former NBA player, won seven championship rings with three different teams during his career.", "annotation_id": "16283455", "url": "https://genius.com/16283455", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Yeah, takin’ Xans, catch my Z’s", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, takin' Xans, catch my z's"], "meaning": "The prescription drug Xanax is known for making its users sleepy, as referenced in Sicko Mode", "annotation_id": "16283444", "url": "https://genius.com/16283444", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Pull out that Rollie, it got the bezel All of my jewelry is real metal", "vault_lines": ["Pull out that Rolly, it got the bezel"], "meaning": "A bezel is a ring that holds a watch face down. Many rappers, such as Twista, have worn fancy watches with fancy bezels. Uzi is also stating that every piece of jewelry he has, including his Rolex, is all real, and probably precious metal such as gold or platinum.", "annotation_id": "16283411", "url": "https://genius.com/16283411", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "All the rings on like I’m Horry, ayy", "vault_lines": ["All the rings on like I'm Horry, ayy"], "meaning": "Robert Horry is an American basketball player known for his clutch performances and whopping seven championship rings, earned while playing as a forward for the Houston Rockets, the Los Angeles Lakers and the San Antonio Spurs from 1992-2008.\n\n\n\nUzi is boasting how well off he is by likening Horry’s massive amount of hardware to his excessive bling.", "annotation_id": "14846211", "url": "https://genius.com/14846211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Yeah, run through them hoes like Ray Rice", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, run through them hoes like Ray Rice"], "meaning": "Known for his explosive speed and power, Ray Rice was a running back for the Baltimore Ravens from 2008-2013.\n\n\n\nIn February 2014, however, Rice was charged with third-degree assault after a surveillance camera captured him knocking out Janay Palmer, his then-fiancée, in an elevator at Atlantic City’s Revel Casino Hotel.", "annotation_id": "14843506", "url": "https://genius.com/14843506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Ksubi jeans tight, kinda hurtin’", "vault_lines": ["Ksubi jeans tight, kinda hurtin'"], "meaning": "Specializing in intricate denim designs, Ksubi is an Australian luxury fashion company founded in 1999.\n\n\n\nUzi has been known to rep the brand. For instance, he  mentioned it previously in the 2016 track, “Canadian Goose”:\n\nCopped the double plus cause I’m rockin' Ksubi’s…", "annotation_id": "14843442", "url": "https://genius.com/14843442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Cut that bitch off like I’m Zorro, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Cut that bitch off like I'm Zorro, yeah"], "meaning": "Known for his great agility and imposing skill with his rapier, Zorro is a fictional character created by Johnston McCulley in mid-1919. Similar to Uzi, after originating as a small act, Zorro has since been portrayed in many short stories and movies bearing his namesake.", "annotation_id": "14837444", "url": "https://genius.com/14837444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "That be Chanel on my sneaks", "vault_lines": ["That be Chanel on my sneaks"], "meaning": "Chanel is a stellar luxury fashion company founded by Coco Chanel in 1909 based in Paris, France. Known for their various perfumes, handbags, and jewelry, prestigious artists like Lil Uzi Vert and Young Thug have recently introduced sneakers and from the group to the rap industry.\n\n\n\nIn Uzi and Pharrell William’s 2017 track, “Neon Guts”, Uzi also threw in a reference about the exquisite brand;\n\nI put Chanel on my shooter", "annotation_id": "14835947", "url": "https://genius.com/14835947", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Both of my choppers be brothers Callin’ em Lil Bert and Lil Ernie", "vault_lines": ["Both of my choppers be brothers"], "meaning": "Bert and Ernie are popular characters from the Sesame Street television franchise, known to be inseparable.\n\nAs “chopper” is a slang term for an automatic firearm, Uzi compares the  camaraderie of his dual-wielded weapons to the cohesion of Bert and Ernie.", "annotation_id": "14835090", "url": "https://genius.com/14835090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Damn DJ Plugg, you just killed it!", "vault_lines": ["Smoke, smoke, smoke my dope"], "meaning": "This is long time Uzi collaborator, DJ Plugg’s producer tag. He has worked with other big artists, such as Migos, Future, and Rich Homie Quan.", "annotation_id": "14834969", "url": "https://genius.com/14834969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Smoke My Dope", "line": "Heel toeing right in my visvims I do not rock on no Jordans Lil Uzi he got the vision, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Heel toeing right in my Visvims"], "meaning": "Visvim is a luxurious designer company founded by Hiroki Nakamura in the fashion district of Ura-Harajuku, Japan in 2001. The brand is known for their exceptional footwear.\n\n\n\nLil Uzi Vert in Visvims.\n\nUzi has shown to be very into the shoes, and has mentioned them in several of his tracks, such as his 2017 song, “3 Pills”;\n\nThese are not Jordans, these Visvims;\n\nThe Philadelphia native uses a play on words in the first and latter part of the verse, as “visvims” and “vision” sound alike.", "annotation_id": "14834613", "url": "https://genius.com/14834613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
