{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Sinner (Been Up)", "line": "All my sons good, like I’m LaVar Ball", "vault_lines": ["Like, on God (For real)"], "meaning": "Uzi is probably talking about his sons as his homies, saying they are all doing well and making money just like he is but also references LaVar Ball, who’s a father of 3 sons, Lonzo, LaMelo and LiAngelo Ball. As of 2020, all 3 of them have made the NBA which has never been done before. Lonzo plays for the New Orleans Pelicans, LaMelo plays for the Charlotte Hornets and LiAngelo plays for the Detroit Pistons.", "annotation_id": "21676070", "url": "https://genius.com/21676070", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Sinner (Been Up)", "line": "Stand on my money, a sinner (Ayy, what?)", "vault_lines": ["Like, on God (For real)"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi is very short (5′ 4″) but often mentions standing on his money and being very tall, on the song Sanguine Paradise he mentions standing on his money and his height turning to 6'6, then on Myron he said he turned to being 9'10 and on the song Strawberry Peels he mentions being as tall as NBA center Shaquille O'Neal (7′ 1″). In the previous line, Uzi mentions playing his position and the center position is usually the tallest position on a basketball team, that’s why Uzi says a center in this line.", "annotation_id": "21675997", "url": "https://genius.com/21675997", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
