{"type": "song", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shooter", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-uzi-vert-shooter-lyrics", "genius_title": "Shooter", "genius_id": 11432737, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Fuck with me and you gon’ lose (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with me and you gon' lose (What?)"], "meaning": "Playboi Carti seems to use this line in the context of rap beef, suggesting that anyone who challenges him will ultimately lose. The ad-lib playfully mocks how haters react to his confidence in his own success.\n\nAs a double entendre, “tool” here could refer to a gun, indicating that if anyone messes with him in the streets, they’ll lose because he’s armed. He also expresses appreciation for his fans—his “goons\"—who helped him rise to fame. But if someone crosses him, he won’t hesitate to use his “toolie.”", "annotation_id": "33101484", "url": "https://genius.com/33101484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "We gon’ rob the bank, bring the loot, uh, uh", "vault_lines": ["We gon' rob the bank, bring the loot, uh, uh"], "meaning": "Carti isn’t actually robbing a bank. Rather, he’s legally withdrawing so much money that the bank’s reserve has been depleted.\n\nThe unreleased Carti and Uzi collaboration “Break the Bank” has a similar message:\n\nI'ma break the bank (Yeah)\nI'ma break the bank\nI'ma break the bank (What?)", "annotation_id": "27804346", "url": "https://genius.com/27804346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Money on the floor just like some shoes", "vault_lines": ["Money on the floor just like some shoes"], "meaning": "Just as many could care less if the bottom of a shoe comes into contact with the floor, Carti isn’t very worried about his money. He has plenty.\n\nIt’s an ironic analogy because money is typically kept in a much more secure (not to mention clean) place, such as a wallet or bank.", "annotation_id": "26005484", "url": "https://genius.com/26005484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Hit your girl, that’s check-free She ain’t used to text me Now she wanna caress me She keep tryna neck me", "vault_lines": ["Hit your girl, that's check-free"], "meaning": "Lil Uzi refers to gold-digging girls who ignored him when he was broke and unknown, but started showing interest once he gained fame and money—even while in relationships.\n\nIn this context, “neck me” has a double meaning. On one hand, it’s slang for “killing,” as in the overwhelming attention he’s getting from these girls who only love him for his success. On the other hand, it’s also slang for oral sex, highlighting the intensity of their sudden affection.", "annotation_id": "23105032", "url": "https://genius.com/23105032", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Whip, it look like butter, baby, pecan drop", "vault_lines": ["Whip, it look like butter, baby, pecan drop"], "meaning": "Uzi is referencing the interior of his car, noting the luxurious creamy brown leather found in many high-end cars, particularly brands like Porsche and Ferrari. This detail highlights that he’s driving an expensive sports car.\n\nAdditionally, there might be a subtle wordplay with “pecan drop,” sounding like “peak and drop,” which ties into the next line where he mentions lean consumption.", "annotation_id": "22990016", "url": "https://genius.com/22990016", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Pecan drop, put that four in Sun Drop", "vault_lines": ["Pecan drop, put that four in Sun Drop"], "meaning": "Uzi implies that he is pouring 4oz of promethazine cough syrup into the citrus flavored soda Sun Drop, as opposed to the more commonly used Sprite.", "annotation_id": "21533396", "url": "https://genius.com/21533396", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "We gon’ take these boys back to school, uh", "vault_lines": ["We gon' take these boys back to school, uh"], "meaning": "This is a slick reference to an old English saying “teach you a lesson”, usually meaning to cause some form of harm (usually physical or verbal) to someone to discourage them from repeating an undesirable action.\n\nIn this case, his crew is going to teach their haters a lesson, or take them back to school, for not liking him and his crew.", "annotation_id": "21197628", "url": "https://genius.com/21197628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Let that thing down and point at you, huh, uh", "vault_lines": ["Let that thing down and point at you, huh, uh"], "meaning": "Carti explains that the aforementioned shooters will perform a drive-by shooting\n\n\n\nWhen the time comes to wound Carti’s doubters his shooters will “Let that thing down” with “thing” referring to the windows of the cars in the subsequent line. He is declaring to his doubters that the shooters will “point at” them. They will aim their gun at his skeptics.", "annotation_id": "18626349", "url": "https://genius.com/18626349", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Got them rocks, diamond rocks, whip the pot", "vault_lines": ["Got them rocks, diamond rocks, whip the pot"], "meaning": "When powdered cocaine is mixed with baking soda and water and then heated, it transforms into crack in a rock or crystal form. The process of “whipping” or stirring the mixture is a crucial and important step in producing crack.", "annotation_id": "18612827", "url": "https://genius.com/18612827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Stack my knots, count a lot, saw a lot", "vault_lines": ["Stack my knots, count a lot, saw a lot"], "meaning": "Knots also known as bankrolls are wads of money put together that resemble – like the name says – a knot.\n\n\n\nUzi has countless knots, with a net worth of $17 million in 2020.", "annotation_id": "18612825", "url": "https://genius.com/18612825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "You know that I’m smokin’ dope, I’ll be high ’til next week", "vault_lines": ["You know that I'm smokin' dope, I'll be high 'til next week"], "meaning": "Uzi is a big fan of dope or marijuana and cannabis.\n\nUzi has expressed his fondness of the drug in an interview with Sway as well as an interview with Hot 97.\nhttps://youtu.be/4QYfD43mJSU?t=19m53s\n\nUzi is saying that his weed is so strong that when he smokes it, it’ll have him high for an entire week.\n\n\n\nIn a song that was leaked after the release of Shoota, “1600”, Uzi raps:\n\nI be so high ‘til the morning (What)\nI be on drugs and I’m a stoner (Yeah)", "annotation_id": "16086322", "url": "https://genius.com/16086322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "I gotta tell my bestie Someone call my bestie Think I found my bestie Link up, make a check bleed", "vault_lines": ["I gotta tell my bestie"], "meaning": "Uzi and Carti are known to hang out together, whether it be making songs or just during their free time. They have collaborated on multiple songs, such as “wokeuplikethis*”, “Lookin” and “Of Course We Ghetto Flowers”.\nhttps://www.google.com/imgres?imgurl=http%3A%2F%2Fimages.genius.com%2Fd7637108032b6a241db87c991091e403.803x803x1.jpg&imgrefurl=https%3A%2F%2Fgenius.com%2Fartists%2FPlayboi-carti-and-lil-uzi-vert&docid=exKb7uA_jJKNUM&tbnid=sHCxyhGzzX7cdM%3A&vet=10ahUKEwiZ2Zyup9vbAhUDSa0KHc0fCokQMwjhASgDMAM..i&w=803&h=803&hl=en-us&client=safari&bih=622&biw=414&q=uzi%20and%20carti&ved=0ahUKEwiZ2Zyup9vbAhUDSa0KHc0fCokQMwjhASgDMAM&iact=mrc&uact=8\nWhile Uzi often claims to have no friends at all, he has featured a few friends while in an interview with Complex\nhttps://twitter.com/liluzivert/status/534447424048472066?lang=en\nhttps://youtu.be/RAy3h9UrCiI?t=6m34s\nDue to these contradictory statements, it is safe to say that Uzi can be referring to Carti as his bestie.", "annotation_id": "14804158", "url": "https://genius.com/14804158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 107, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "And I love my goons, yeah And I love my tool (Yeah), yeah (Yeah) And I love my loot (What?), yeah", "vault_lines": ["And I love my goons, yeah"], "meaning": "Carti is very grateful for the love and loyalty he gets from his crew (his goons).\n\nSince the release of his debut commercial mixtape, Carti quickly rose to fame with songs like Magnolia, peaking at nº 29 on the Billboard Hot 100, and\n​w​okeuplikethis*, which also featured Lil Uzi Vert and peaked at nº 76.\n\nWith fame and money, it is only natural that friends and loved ones could show a side that has never been seen before. Carti implies that even though he is living a different and exuberant lifestyle, his friends and family are still on his side, supporting him and showing him love, something he also reciprocates.\n\nCarti continues down these lines to talk about his other affections, his tools (a slang for guns) and all the things his money can buy: cars, jewelry, designer clothes, mansions and etc. (his loot).", "annotation_id": "14672060", "url": "https://genius.com/14672060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Don’t talk to me, just talk to my lil’ dude Don’t talk to me, just talk to my lil’ dude", "vault_lines": ["Don't talk to me, just talk to my lil' dude"], "meaning": "In this line, Carti is referring to his gun–the previously mentioned “toolie\"–as his \"lil' dude.” Carti doesn’t want to talk; he lets his gun do the talking.\n\nThis line could be a reference to Al Pacino’s memorable line in the movie Scarface:\n\nSay hello to my little friend!", "annotation_id": "14615157", "url": "https://genius.com/14615157", "state": "accepted", "votes": 106, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Uh, woke up with my toolie, what it do? Huh, uh Meet me in the alley with the troops, uh", "vault_lines": ["Uh, woke up with my toolie, what it do? Huh, uh"], "meaning": "In this line, Carti explains that he has just woken up with his “toolie,” or gun. Toolie is a common term for a firearm in the hip-hop world, with French Montana using the term on “Lockjaw,” Chief Keef on “Love No Thotties,” and even Lil Yachty on his “Minnesota (Remix).”\n\nCarti is ready to use his firearm for whatever may be necessary, as he taunts his doubters to “meet [him] in the alley with the troops.” This comes before he explains that he has “shooters” from multiple gangs, so it can be safely inferred that he is alluding to using violence against those who are not on his side.", "annotation_id": "14577278", "url": "https://genius.com/14577278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 153, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Know I had to let her go ’cause she can’t arrest me", "vault_lines": ["Know I had to let her go 'cause she can't arrest me"], "meaning": "Uzi doesn’t want to be tied down to one girl right now, so he cuts them off before they can get attached.\n\nTo be “cuffed” is a term for being committed to having a boyfriend or girlfriend. By saying this girl can’t arrest him, Uzi is refusing to be cuffed.\n\nIt seems like Uzi hasn’t been ready for a long term relationship for awhile, as he expressed the same feelings back in 2016 on his track “$ub Zero”:\n\nLittle girl, you cannot cuff me", "annotation_id": "14557750", "url": "https://genius.com/14557750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Everybody rock with me because I’m up now", "vault_lines": ["Everybody rock with me because I'm up now"], "meaning": "After “XO TOUR Llif3” blew up, peaking at #1 on the Billboard Top 100 in rap streams, Uzi’s haters have quieted down as he is now achieving a level of success only a few rappers have found in recent times. With this popularity, thousands of new fans have hopped on the bandwagon for supporting Uzi – because it’s easier to support a rapper who’s making hits and is on top of the game.\n\nUzi’s touched on this subject of fans flocking him due to his success before, on “Boring Shit” which dropped on Soundcloud in early 2017:\n\nOf course you rock with me ‘cause I just came out this year", "annotation_id": "14557729", "url": "https://genius.com/14557729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Took your girl and I’ma score like I made the touchdown", "vault_lines": ["Took your girl and I'ma score like I made the touchdown"], "meaning": "Uzi uses wordplay to compare taking someone else’s girl to catching an interception in football. He will “score” by obtaining the female in question and getting laid on a sexual conquest. “Touch-down” also symbolizes him taking the win and serves as a sexual reference in addition.", "annotation_id": "14549906", "url": "https://genius.com/14549906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "I’ma fuck your thot, she just a swoop, hah, yeah I’ma fuck your thot, she just a swoop, hah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'ma fuck your thot, she just a swoop, hah, yeah"], "meaning": "Swoop is another word for a thot or a hoe. Carti used a similar line in the second verse of “Yah Mean”:\n\nOoh fucking on that swoop, fucking on that ho", "annotation_id": "14548037", "url": "https://genius.com/14548037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Swervin’ in that Lambo’, doors go up, not on a bus now", "vault_lines": ["Swervin' in that Lambo', doors go up, not on a bus now"], "meaning": "Unlike previous years when he was taking the bus, Uzi is presently wealthy enough to drive his own Lamborghini with custom scissor doors that open upwards, as opposed to standard manual car doors, which open sideways.", "annotation_id": "14542534", "url": "https://genius.com/14542534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "I got red shooters, I got blue, huh, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I got red shooters, I got blue, huh, yeah"], "meaning": "Carti has shooters from both the Blood and Crip gangs. Carti, a well-known Blood, has mentioned his affiliation with the gang numerous times, notably in his verse on the “2017 XXL Freshmen List Cypher,” on which he rapped:\n\nYuh, Ben Baller, no Johnny Dang\nYuh, uh, all my niggas Blood gang\n\nDespite being a Blood, Carti is friends with a number of Crips, including Houston rapper Maxo Kream who is a Five-deuce Hoover Gangster Crip. Carti and Maxo have collaborated on Maxo’s song “Spike Lee,” as well as Carti’s breakout track “Fetti”.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Carti’s got hundreds. In the United States, the $100 bill has a blue tint and a blue ribbon woven into the centre.", "annotation_id": "14480973", "url": "https://genius.com/14480973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 113, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "(That-that-that-that-that-that be Maaly Raw)", "vault_lines": ["Now is my time"], "meaning": "This is the tag for the song’s producer Maaly Raw, spoken by Lil Uzi Vert.\n\n“Shoota” marks the third released collaboration between Carti and Maaly Raw. Carti was featured on Uzi’s 2016 tracks “Left Right” and “Of Course We Ghetto Flowers,” both of which featured production from Maaly Raw.\n\nAn unreleased track titled “AR Whip” recorded in 2016 features production from Maaly Raw; it was leaked in 2017.", "annotation_id": "14480900", "url": "https://genius.com/14480900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 146, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Bentley or the ’Rari, ho, let’s choose, ooh", "vault_lines": ["Bentley or the 'Rari, ho, let's choose, ooh"], "meaning": "Carti claims to be wealthy enough to decide which expensive and luxurious car he wants. He is able to pick between two cars: a Bentley and a Ferrari.\nHe makes the proposal of making the decision alongside his female companion.\n\n\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Carti actually owns a Ferrari of his own and has been spotted riding around in it with model Blac Chyna.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i_lGIGM1i-0\nHe’s also been spotted in a Bentley, but it is unclear, whether it belongs to him or his close friend and collaborator, Lil Uzi Vert.\n\n\n\nPerhaps Carti was actually referring to Blac Chyna when he said ho.", "annotation_id": "14478206", "url": "https://genius.com/14478206", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Used to want a G-Shock, now I’m walking with a bustdown Pull up and I’m flooded with a iced out watch", "vault_lines": ["Used to want a G-Shock, now I'm walking with a bustdown"], "meaning": "G-Shock is a line of watches manufactured by Casio. The watch can be classified as high-end; however, it is nothing like a bust down watch as Uzi refers to. In the time Uzi was growing up, the G-Shock was considered a sign of flavor, but he’s since moved on to bigger things.\n\nA bust down is often a very expensive piece of jewelry, however, here Uzi mentions an expensive watch. One of the characteristics of a bust down watch would be that it is flooded with diamonds.\n\nUzi even made a song dedicated to his expensive jewelry and watches, also named “Bust Down”\n\n\n\nAfter all the acclaimed success that Lil Uzi Vert has received, which more than likely would’ve gotten him plenty of money, a G-Shock seems merely nothing for him and now he rocks a bust down, or as Uzi says himself, ‘an iced out watch’", "annotation_id": "14474327", "url": "https://genius.com/14474327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Lil Uzi Vert", "song": "Shoota", "line": "Suicide, 1600, that’s the block", "vault_lines": ["Suicide, 1600, that's the block"], "meaning": "Uzi grew up on the 1600 block in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He also speaks of 1600 block in other songs, such as “Dark Queen”:\n\nMomma said stay down there ‘fore you get hurt (1600 block)\nThat was way before I was Lil Uzi Vert (1600 block)\nMomma saw me in action it could’ve got worse (1600 block)\n\nBoth this line and the bars from “Dark Queen” suggest that 1600 block is a deadly place to go – if you want to be killed, its an area where you can find death.", "annotation_id": "13157483", "url": "https://genius.com/13157483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
